	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- structure
	"cx_bolt": ["螺栓", "BOLT"],
	"cx_bolt_a": ["螺栓用来固定船上的零件，可以使用维护工具拧下来。这样拆除不会损坏零件，设备也能保持完整。", "Bolts hold parts onto the ship and can be undone with the maintenance tool. Removing a part this way does not damage it, so the equipment stays whole."],
	"cx_bolt_b": ["拧下最后一颗螺栓以后，零件就失去了固定。如果没有提前固定好，零件可能会带着惯性漂走。", "Once the last bolt is out, nothing holds the part any more. If it has not been secured beforehand, it can drift away with whatever motion it had."],
	"cx_bolt_c": ["拆除之前，先用抓钩固定住零件，确认不会漂走以后，再拧下最后一颗螺栓。", "Before removing it, secure the part with the grapple. Once you are sure it will not drift off, take out the last bolt."],
	"cx_bolt_x": ["船上常用的是 M12–M24 高强度螺栓，拧紧以后会产生预紧力，把连接的两个零件压在一起。连接处主要依靠接触面的摩擦力防止零件滑动，螺栓本身也能承受一定的拉力和剪切力。\n拆除螺栓不会损坏设备，所以能用维护工具拆下来的零件，就尽量不要使用切割工具。完整拆下来的设备可以保留全部价值，一旦切开，就只能按照废金属的价格回收。\n还要注意，失重环境下没有地板帮你接住松开的零件。一块重达 0.5 吨的金属板，即使只有 0.1 米每秒的剩余速度，经过 10 秒也会漂出去 1 米，所以拆除最后一颗螺栓之前，一定要先把零件固定好。", "Ship bolts are mostly high-strength M12–M24. Tightening them creates a preload that presses the two joined parts together. The joint mainly relies on friction between the contact faces to stop the parts sliding, and the bolt itself can also carry some tension and shear.\nRemoving a bolt does not damage the equipment, so use the maintenance tool rather than the cutting tool wherever a part can be unbolted. Equipment removed whole keeps its full value; once it is cut, it can only be recovered at scrap-metal price.\nAlso note that in weightlessness there is no floor to catch a part you have loosened. A 0.5 t metal plate with just 0.1 m/s of residual speed drifts 1 m away in 10 seconds, so always secure the part before removing the last bolt."],
	"cx_weld": ["焊缝", "WELD"],
	"cx_weld_a": ["两块金属通过焊接连在一起，已经成为一个整体，没办法用扳手拆开。", "Two pieces of metal are joined by welding and have become one body. A wrench cannot undo it."],
	"cx_weld_b": ["焊缝只能通过切割拆除，切割时如果损坏了旁边的设备，还会影响回收价值。", "A weld can only be removed by cutting. If the cut damages the equipment beside it, the recovery value drops."],
	"cx_weld_c": ["沿着焊缝或者标记好的切割线慢慢切开，注意不要切到设备本体。", "Cut slowly along the weld seam or the marked cutting line, and take care not to cut into the equipment itself."],
	"cx_weld_x": ["结构焊缝的强度和连接的金属差不多，所以激光需要切透整个截面，才能把两边彻底分开。\n不同材料的切割速度也不一样，普通钢板比较容易切开，装甲和厚梁需要更长时间，冰和复合材料则有各自的切割要求。\n切割时，激光会按照材料允许的速度跟随光标移动。尽量贴着切割线缓慢移动，等激光把材料完全切透以后再继续向前。如果移动得太快，激光就只能在表面留下浅浅的切痕，需要重新切割。", "A structural weld is about as strong as the metal it joins, so the laser has to cut through the whole cross-section before the two sides come apart.\nCutting speed also varies with the material. Ordinary steel plate is fairly easy to cut, armour and heavy beams take longer, and ice and composites each have their own cutting requirements.\nWhile cutting, the laser follows the cursor at whatever speed the material allows. Move slowly along the cutting line and wait until the laser has cut right through before moving on. If you move too fast, the laser only leaves a shallow groove on the surface and you have to cut again."],
	"cx_lock": ["锁扣", "LOCK"],
	"cx_lock_a": ["锁扣是一种带有锁销的固定零件，拆卸起来比较方便，通常安装在检修盖或其他零件的背面。由于安装位置比较隐蔽，需要仔细检查才能找到。", "A lock is a fixing part with a locking pin. It is easy to remove and is usually fitted on the back of a service cover or another part. Because it is hidden, you need to look carefully to find it."],
	"cx_lock_b": ["如果还有锁扣没有拆除，就直接使用抓钩拉扯零件，可能会损坏零件的连接位置，拉力过大时还会把锁扣直接扯断。", "If a lock has not been removed and you pull the part with the grapple anyway, you may damage the part’s mounting point, and with too much pull the lock snaps outright."],
	"cx_lock_c": ["使用抓钩拉扯零件之前，先查看光标上的提示，确认还有多少个固定点没有拆除，全部处理完成后再进行拆卸。", "Before pulling a part with the grapple, check the hint on the cursor to see how many fixing points are still left, and pull only after all of them are dealt with."],
	"cx_lock_x": ["锁扣通常安装在需要经常拆卸的地方，像检修盖、可更换的设备和货物托盘，都可能使用锁扣固定。拆卸方法和螺栓差不多，使用维护工具就可以将锁扣打开。\n如果没有提前拆除锁扣，就直接使用抓钩强行拉扯，拉力超过锁扣的承受范围后，锁扣就会断裂，零件的安装位置也可能受到损坏。\n抓钩可以强行扯断锁扣和管线，但无法扯断螺栓。如果零件还有螺栓固定，就需要先使用维护工具将螺栓拆除，才能继续拆卸零件。", "Locks are usually fitted where parts need to be removed often. Service covers, replaceable equipment and cargo pallets may all be held by locks. They are removed much like bolts: the maintenance tool opens them.\nIf a lock has not been removed and you pull with the grapple anyway, the lock breaks once the pull exceeds what it can take, and the part’s mounting position may also be damaged.\nThe grapple can forcibly break locks and lines, but it cannot break bolts. If a part is still held by bolts, remove them with the maintenance tool first before you can continue taking the part off."],
	"cx_clamp": ["船坞夹具", "BERTH CLAMP"],
	"cx_clamp_a": ["船坞里的液压夹具，用来把整艘船固定在泊位上，防止船体在拆解过程中发生移动。", "The hydraulic clamps in the berth hold the whole ship in its bay so the hull cannot move during dismantling."],
	"cx_clamp_b": ["夹具只固定着船体上的几处结构，如果提前把这些结构拆掉，船体就会失去固定，可能在泊位里发生漂移。", "The clamps grip only a few structures on the hull. If you remove those structures too early, the hull comes loose and may drift inside the bay."],
	"cx_clamp_c": ["拆解船体的时候，先保留被夹具固定的结构，等其他部分都拆得差不多了，再处理这些位置。", "When dismantling the hull, keep the structures held by the clamps until last. Deal with those positions only when most of the rest has been taken apart."],
	"cx_clamp_x": ["船坞夹具一般固定在龙骨或底板上，虽然船体的移动速度可能很慢，但一艘几百吨重的船就算只以 0.05 m/s 的速度撞上泊位端墙，也可能因为撞击而损坏舱内没有固定好的设备。\n蓝图上会标出夹具固定的位置，拆解进入后半段以后，记得检查剩下的船体是否还被夹具固定，确认安全以后再继续拆解。", "Berth clamps are usually fixed to the keel or the floor plates. The hull may move slowly, but even a ship of several hundred tonnes hitting the end wall of the bay at only 0.05 m/s can damage any loose equipment inside the rooms.\nThe positions held by the clamps are marked on the blueprint. Once the job is in its second half, check whether the remaining hull is still held by the clamps, and carry on only when it is safe."],
	"cx_hull": ["外壳板", "HULL PLATE"],
	"cx_hull_a": ["外壳板是船体外侧的金属板，负责保护内部结构，同时保持舱室密封，防止舱内气体泄漏。", "Hull plates are the metal plates on the outside of the hull. They protect the internal structure and keep the rooms sealed so that gas cannot leak out."],
	"cx_hull_b": ["如果舱室里面还有气压就直接切开外壳板，内部的高压气体会从切口快速喷出，可能把切开的板材和舱内没有固定好的设备一起冲出去。", "If you cut a hull plate while a room still holds air pressure, the high-pressure gas inside shoots out through the cut and can blow the cut plate out together with any loose equipment in the room."],
	"cx_hull_c": ["拆除外壳板之前，先检查舱室的气压，等气压降低到 5 kPa 以下以后，再开始切割。", "Before removing a hull plate, check the pressure in the room, and start cutting only after it has dropped below 5 kPa."],
	"cx_hull_x": ["一个标准大气压大约是 101 kPa，相当于每平方米承受约 10 吨的压力作用力。如果一块长 2 米、宽 1 米的外壳板承受着 100 kPa 的压差，那么整块板受到的推力就相当于 20 吨重物产生的重力。\n这种情况下直接切开外壳板，高压气体就会从切口快速喷出，气流速度甚至可能达到音速，几秒钟内就能把舱室里没有固定好的零件和碎屑冲出去。\n所以拆解之前一定要先完成泄压，确认舱室气压已经降低到 5 kPa 以下，再进行切割。", "One standard atmosphere is about 101 kPa, which is a force of about 10 tonnes on every square metre. If a hull plate 2 m long and 1 m wide has a pressure difference of 100 kPa across it, the thrust on the whole plate equals the weight of a 20 t load.\nCutting the plate in that state lets the high-pressure gas shoot out through the cut, at speeds that can even reach the speed of sound, and within seconds it blows out the loose parts and debris in the room.\nSo always vent the pressure before dismantling, and cut only after you have confirmed the room pressure is below 5 kPa."],
	"cx_bulkhead": ["舱壁", "BULKHEAD"],
	"cx_bulkhead_a": ["舱壁是船体内部的隔墙，负责把船舱分成多个独立的密封区域，防止一个舱室发生事故以后影响到其他舱室。", "A bulkhead is an internal wall of the hull. It divides the ship into several separate sealed areas so that an accident in one room does not affect the others."],
	"cx_bulkhead_b": ["如果舱壁两侧的气压不同，直接切开舱壁就会让高压一侧的气体迅速进入低压舱室，还可能把附近没有固定好的设备和零件一起冲过去。", "If the pressure is different on the two sides of a bulkhead, cutting it lets gas from the high-pressure side rush into the low-pressure room, and it may sweep nearby loose equipment and parts along with it."],
	"cx_bulkhead_c": ["切割舱壁之前，先检查两侧舱室的气压，如果存在压差，就先进行泄压或者平衡两侧的气压，确认安全以后再开始拆除。", "Before cutting a bulkhead, check the pressure in the rooms on both sides. If there is a pressure difference, vent or equalise the two sides first, and start removal only when it is safe."],
	"cx_bulkhead_x": ["舱壁可以把不同舱室隔开，这样即使其中一个舱室发生泄漏，也不会直接影响整艘船。拆解的时候也要注意，即使你已经把一个舱室的气体排空，隔壁的舱室也可能还保持着原来的气压。\n真正需要注意的是两侧的压差。如果两个舱室都是 100 kPa，切开中间的舱壁一般不会因为气压差而发生喷气，但两个舱室也会从此连通。\n如果之后还需要泄压，就得把连通的舱室一起处理，所以切割之前最好确认两侧的气压，避免增加后面的拆解工作。", "Bulkheads separate the rooms, so even if one room leaks, the whole ship is not directly affected. Remember this when dismantling too: even after you have emptied one room of gas, the next room may still hold its original pressure.\nWhat really matters is the pressure difference between the two sides. If both rooms are at 100 kPa, cutting the bulkhead between them generally will not cause a blast of gas, but the two rooms become connected from then on.\nIf you still need to vent afterwards, you have to treat the connected rooms together, so it is best to check the pressure on both sides before cutting, to avoid adding to the dismantling work later."],
	"cx_frame": ["承力结构", "LOAD-BEARING FRAME"],
	"cx_frame_a": ["船体内部的龙骨、肋骨、纵梁和支撑杆都属于承力结构，它们组成了船体的主要骨架，负责支撑和固定其他设备。", "The keel, ribs, longitudinals and struts inside the hull are all load-bearing structures. Together they form the main skeleton of the hull and support and hold the other equipment."],
	"cx_frame_b": ["有些承力结构还在支撑其他设备，如果直接把它们切断，原本固定好的设备和船体结构就可能突然移动，甚至发生弹开、扭曲或断裂的情况。", "Some load-bearing structures are still supporting other equipment. If you cut them directly, equipment and hull structure that were held firmly may suddenly move, and may even spring off, twist or break."],
	"cx_frame_c": ["拆解之前，先检查承力结构连接着哪些设备，把它支撑的重量卸下来，确认没有其他结构需要依靠它固定以后，再进行切割。", "Before dismantling, check what equipment the load-bearing structure is connected to. Take off the weight it supports, make sure no other structure depends on it, and then cut."],
	"cx_frame_x": ["虽然太空里没有正常的重力载荷，但船体内部仍然存在预紧力、惯性作用，以及船坞夹具传递过来的外力。有些梁甚至需要同时固定两台几十吨重的设备，直接切断就可能让这些设备失去支撑。\n承力结构本身通常也比较重，有些会超过抓钩 3 t 的承重上限，所以拆解时需要沿着标记好的切割线分成几段，再分别运走。", "There is no normal gravity load in space, but the hull still has preload, inertia, and external forces passed on by the berth clamps. Some beams even hold two machines weighing tens of tonnes at once, and cutting them straight through can leave those machines unsupported.\nLoad-bearing structures are usually heavy themselves, and some exceed the grapple’s 3 t load limit, so they must be cut into several sections along the marked cutting lines and carried away one by one."],
	"cx_door": ["舱门与货舱门", "DOORS AND HATCHES"],
	"cx_door_a": ["船上的舱门用来连接不同的舱室，大部分都需要通过船体总线供电，才能正常开启和关闭。", "Doors on the ship connect the different rooms. Most of them need power from the ship’s bus to open and close properly."],
	"cx_door_b": ["如果舱室里面还有气压，直接打开舱门可能会让舱门受到气压冲击，严重时甚至会被直接冲飞。有些舱门还需要电力才能开启，一旦提前切断电源，就可能再也无法正常打开。", "If a room still holds air pressure, opening its door may subject the door to a pressure shock, and in bad cases it is blown off outright. Some doors also need power to open, so if you cut the power too early, they may never open normally again."],
	"cx_door_c": ["打开舱门之前，先确认舱室里面的气压已经排空。需要使用电力开启的舱门，最好在切断船体电源之前就打开。", "Before opening a door, make sure the pressure in the room has been vented. For doors that need power to open, it is best to open them before cutting the ship’s power."],
	"cx_door_x": ["一扇面积为 2 m² 的舱门，如果两侧存在 60 kPa 的气压差，舱门就会承受相当于约 12 吨重物的压力。这种情况下，驱动电机可能无法正常开启舱门，一旦解除门锁，舱门甚至可能被气压直接冲飞。\n大型货舱门一般需要电机或者液压系统驱动，如果提前拆除了供电电池，后面可能就只能使用切割工具强行打开。不过船坞也提供了外部供电插座，即使已经切断船体电源，也可以通过外部供电临时启动舱门。", "If a 2 m² door has a pressure difference of 60 kPa across it, the door bears a force equal to about 12 tonnes. In that case the drive motor may not be able to open the door, and once the latch is released, the door may even be blown off by the pressure.\nLarge cargo doors usually need a motor or a hydraulic system to drive them. If you remove the power battery too early, the only way left may be to force them open with the cutting tool. However, the berth also provides an external power socket, so even after the ship’s power is cut, a door can be started temporarily from external power."],
	"cx_rail": ["轨道", "RAIL"],
	"cx_rail_a": ["安装在船体内部的导轨，主要用来运输货物，或者让吊车和滑架沿着固定的路线移动。", "A guide rail installed inside the hull, used mainly to carry cargo, or to let cranes and cradles move along a fixed route."],
	"cx_rail_b": ["如果轨道上还有货物或者设备，直接切断轨道可能会让它们失去支撑，导致设备损坏，严重时还可能直接掉落。", "If a rail still carries cargo or equipment, cutting it directly may leave them unsupported, damaging the equipment, and in bad cases they may drop."],
	"cx_rail_c": ["拆除轨道之前，先把上面的货物和设备全部移走，确认轨道上没有剩余载荷以后，再开始拆解。", "Before removing a rail, move all the cargo and equipment off it, and start dismantling only once you have confirmed no load is left on the rail."],
	"cx_rail_x": ["轨道通常由多个支座共同承受重量，这样就能把货物的重量分散到不同位置。如果直接切断其中一段，原本由整条轨道承担的部分重量就会集中到断口附近的支座上，一旦超过它们的承重能力，就可能发生变形或者断裂。\n如果货物通过锁轨固定在轨道上，需要先沿着轨道把货物运出去，不能直接使用扳手拆除固定装置。具体操作可以查看对应船型的锁轨说明。", "A rail is usually carried by several mounts, which spread the weight of the cargo over different positions. If you cut one section, part of the weight the whole rail was bearing is concentrated on the mounts next to the break, and if it exceeds what they can take, they may deform or break.\nIf cargo is fixed to the rail by a rail lock, it has to be driven out along the rail first, and the fixing cannot simply be removed with the wrench. For the exact procedure, see the rail-lock entry for the ship type concerned."],
	"cx_film": ["薄膜", "FILM"],
	"cx_film_a": ["一种只有几微米厚的聚酰亚胺薄膜，主要用在飞船的帆面、气囊外壁和遮阳膜上。", "A polyimide film only a few microns thick, used mainly for sail panels, gasbag walls and sunshades on ships."],
	"cx_film_b": ["薄膜在绷紧的时候很容易被撕裂，如果直接使用切割工具，切口可能会在张力作用下迅速扩大，最后导致整片薄膜破裂。", "Film tears easily when taut. If you use the cutting tool directly, the cut may spread rapidly under tension and eventually tear the whole film."],
	"cx_film_c": ["拆解薄膜之前，先解除固定装置，让薄膜完全松弛下来，再把整片薄膜拆下来。", "Before dismantling film, release the fixings so the film goes completely slack, and then take the whole film off."],
	"cx_film_x": ["这种薄膜的抗撕裂强度只有每米几牛，而绷紧的帆面每米可能承受几十牛的张力。如果直接使用激光切割，切口就可能成为裂纹的起点，在张力作用下，裂纹甚至能以接近声速的速度扩展。\n薄膜本身非常轻，基本不会阻挡物体碰撞，也不会影响正常的移动路径，不过它仍然能够遮挡光线，而且表面容易积累静电，拆解的时候也需要注意。", "The tear strength of this film is only a few newtons per metre, while a taut sail panel may carry tens of newtons per metre of tension. If you cut with the laser directly, the cut can become the start of a crack, and under tension the crack can spread at close to the speed of sound.\nThe film itself is very light. It basically does not block collisions or affect normal movement paths, but it can still block light and easily builds up static charge, so take care of this when dismantling."],
	"cx_cable": ["电缆", "CABLE"],
	"cx_cable_a": ["连接船体电网和各种设备的供电电缆，两端都有可以拆卸的接头，用来给设备提供电力。", "A power cable that connects the ship’s grid to various equipment. Both ends have removable plugs, which supply power to the equipment."],
	"cx_cable_b": ["如果电缆还带着电，直接拔掉接头或者使用切割工具，就可能产生电弧，损坏附近的设备，甚至伤到正在作业的无人机。", "If a cable is still live, pulling the plug or using the cutting tool directly can produce an arc, damaging nearby equipment and even hurting the drone at work."],
	"cx_cable_c": ["拆卸电缆之前，先用验电工具确认电压已经降到 0 V，再拔掉两端的接头，之后就可以正常搬走设备了。", "Before removing a cable, check with the voltage tester that the voltage has dropped to 0 V, then unplug the connectors at both ends. After that the equipment can be carried away as normal."],
	"cx_cable_x": ["30 V 以下的电压通常不会对无人机造成伤害，不过船上的供电总线一般在 28–400 V 之间，部分电容组的电压甚至能达到上千伏，拆卸之前一定要确认电路已经断电。\n直流电弧没有交流电那种周期性的电流过零点，一旦产生电弧，就可能持续放电，直到电流被切断。\n搬运设备的时候也要注意，如果连接设备的电缆还没有拔掉，抓钩就可能无法正常拖动设备。继续增加拉力的话，还可能直接把电缆接头扯坏。", "Voltages below 30 V generally do not harm the drone, but the ship’s power buses are usually between 28 and 400 V, and some capacitor banks even reach over a thousand volts, so always confirm the circuit is dead before removal.\nA DC arc has no periodic current zero crossing like AC, so once an arc forms, it can keep discharging until the current is cut off.\nAlso take care when moving equipment: if the cable connecting the equipment has not been unplugged, the grapple may be unable to drag the equipment properly. If you keep increasing the pull, it may even tear the cable plug off."],
	"cx_pipe_line": ["管线", "PIPE"],
	"cx_pipe_line_a": ["船上的管线主要用来输送冷却液、燃料和气体，两端都有可以拆卸的接头，方便连接设备或者其他管路。", "Lines on the ship mainly carry coolant, fuel and gas. Both ends have removable couplings so they can be connected to equipment or to other pipes."],
	"cx_pipe_line_b": ["如果管线里面还残留着液体或者气体，直接切开就可能造成泄漏。燃料泄漏以后可能形成易燃的气体云团，而温度过高的管线还可能损坏正在作业的无人机。", "If a line still holds liquid or gas, cutting it directly may cause a leak. Leaked fuel can form a flammable gas cloud, and an over-hot line can damage the drone at work."],
	"cx_pipe_line_c": ["拆卸管线之前，先通过低处的排放口把内部的液体抽干净，再检查管线温度，确认已经冷却到安全范围以后，才能拔掉接头或者进行切割。", "Before removing a line, draw the contents off through the low-point drain, then check the line temperature, and uncouple or cut it only after confirming it has cooled to a safe range."],
	"cx_pipe_line_x": ["关闭阀门以后，管线里面可能仍然残留着液体，尤其是两个阀门之间的管段，即使两端都已经关闭，中间的液体也不会自动排出去，所以拆卸之前还需要单独排空。\n在失重环境下，泄漏的液体不会流到地面，而是会形成漂浮的液团。如果这些液体接触到带电设备，就可能造成短路。\n管线的温度如果超过 60°C，还可能损坏负责抓取和搬运的无人机，所以拆卸之前要先测量温度，确认安全以后再继续操作。", "After a valve is closed, the line may still hold liquid. This is especially so for the length between two valves: even with both ends closed, the liquid in the middle does not drain by itself, so it needs to be drained separately before removal.\nIn weightlessness, leaked liquid does not run to the floor but forms floating globules. If these touch live equipment, they can cause a short circuit.\nIf a line is hotter than 60°C, it may also damage the drone that grips and moves it, so measure the temperature before removal and continue only when it is safe."],
	"cx_cut_line": ["标线（分段线）", "MARKED CUT LINE"],
	"cx_cut_line_a": ["一些大型设备的重量超过了抓钩的搬运上限，所以设备表面会提前标出可以安全切割的位置，方便拆解时将设备分成几个部分。", "Some large equipment weighs more than the grapple can carry, so safe cutting positions are marked on its surface in advance, to let you split the equipment into several parts when dismantling."],
	"cx_cut_line_b": ["如果随便选择位置切割，很容易损坏设备内部的零件，导致回收价值大幅下降。但如果不进行分段，整台设备又可能因为重量太大，无法使用抓钩搬运。", "If you pick a position at random to cut, it is easy to damage the parts inside the equipment, and the recovery value drops sharply. But if you do not split it into sections, the whole piece may be too heavy for the grapple to move."],
	"cx_cut_line_c": ["按照设备表面的标线进行切割，把设备分成几个部分，并确认每个部分的重量都没有超过抓钩的搬运上限。", "Cut along the marked lines on the equipment surface to split it into several parts, and confirm that the weight of each part does not exceed the grapple’s carrying limit."],
	"cx_cut_line_x": ["抓钩最初的搬运上限是 3 吨，升级以后可以提高到 5 吨。对于重量超过这个上限的设备，设计时一般都会预留能够安全分段的位置，通常位于连接法兰、模块接缝或者没有管线经过的地方。\n只要沿着标线进行切割，拆下来的每个部分仍然可以按照设备部件回收，保留原有的回收价值。如果随意切割，就可能切坏内部的线圈绕组、管束或者电路板，到时候损坏的部分就只能按照废金属的价格回收了。", "The grapple’s original carrying limit is 3 t, and after an upgrade it rises to 5 t. For equipment heavier than this limit, safe splitting positions are normally built in at the design stage, usually at connecting flanges, module seams, or places no line passes through.\nAs long as you cut along the marked lines, each part removed can still be recovered as equipment parts and keep its original recovery value. If you cut at random, you may ruin internal coil windings, tube bundles or circuit boards, and the damaged parts can then only be recovered at scrap-metal price."],
	"cx_glass": ["玻璃与舷窗", "GLASS AND WINDOWS"],
	"cx_glass_a": ["船上的舷窗和精密玻璃罩板，一般通过压条和螺栓固定在船体上，拆解时可以将整块玻璃完整取下来。", "Ship windows and precision glass cover plates are usually held to the hull by clamping strips and bolts, and can be taken off whole when dismantling."],
	"cx_glass_b": ["如果玻璃背后还有气压，直接拆除固定螺栓可能会让整块玻璃被气压推出去，造成玻璃破碎。在玻璃附近使用激光切割工具，也可能因为温度变化过大而导致玻璃开裂。", "If there is still pressure behind the glass, removing the fixing bolts directly may let the pressure push the whole pane out and shatter it. Using the laser cutting tool near the glass may also crack it through too large a temperature change."],
	"cx_glass_c": ["拆除玻璃之前，先确认舱室已经完成泄压，切割周围结构的时候也要和玻璃保持距离。等附近的拆解工作完成以后，再拧下固定压条的螺栓，把整块玻璃取出来。", "Before removing glass, make sure the room has been vented, and keep your distance from the glass when cutting the surrounding structure. Once the nearby dismantling is finished, undo the bolts of the clamping strips and take the whole pane out."],
	"cx_glass_x": ["玻璃能够承受较大的压力，但受到拉力或者局部温度变化时就容易出现裂纹，表面原本存在的划痕也会增加破裂的风险。\n如果在距离玻璃 0.7 m 以内使用激光切割工具，切割产生的热辐射和高温飞溅物可能让玻璃两侧的温差超过 100°C，产生的热应力足以让玻璃开裂。\n完整的光学玻璃可以卖出很高的价格，一旦发生破碎，基本就没有多少回收价值了。", "Glass can bear high compression, but it cracks easily under tension or local temperature change, and scratches already on the surface increase the risk of breaking.\nIf you use the laser cutting tool within 0.7 m of the glass, the thermal radiation and hot spatter from cutting can put a temperature difference of over 100°C between the two faces, and the resulting thermal stress is enough to crack the glass.\nIntact optical glass sells for a high price, but once it breaks, there is almost no recovery value left."],
	"cx_armor": ["装甲", "ARMOUR"],
	"cx_armor_a": ["船体外部安装的厚重防护板，包括分层装甲、隔热瓦和辐射屏蔽层，主要用来保护船体和内部设备。", "Thick protective plates on the outside of the hull, including layered armour, heat tiles and radiation shielding, used mainly to protect the hull and the equipment inside."],
	"cx_armor_b": ["装甲的厚度和硬度都比较高，使用切割工具拆除时会花费很长时间，而且切割产生的热量容易集中在切口附近。如果周围安装了其他设备，持续产生的高温就可能把这些设备损坏。", "Armour is thick and hard, so removing it with the cutting tool takes a long time, and the heat from cutting tends to collect around the cut. If other equipment is installed around it, the continuing high temperature may damage that equipment."],
	"cx_armor_c": ["拆解装甲之前，先检查有没有固定螺栓，能够直接拆卸的就尽量不要使用切割工具。如果必须进行切割，最好选择远离其他设备的位置，避免高温造成额外损失。", "Before dismantling armour, check for fixing bolts, and wherever it can be unbolted, avoid the cutting tool. If you must cut, choose a position away from other equipment to avoid extra losses from the heat."],
	"cx_armor_x": ["装甲主要依靠自身的厚度和硬度来吸收冲击能量，所以切割起来会比较困难，有些装甲的切割速度甚至只有普通钢板的十分之一。\n部分船体还安装了钨或氢化锂制成的辐射屏蔽层，这些材料主要用来阻挡辐射，通常重量较大，而且比较容易发生脆裂。\n船体外部的装甲条一般通过螺栓固定，如果能够找到固定位置，直接拆除螺栓通常会比切穿整块装甲快得多，也能减少切割过程中产生的热量。", "Armour absorbs impact energy mainly through its own thickness and hardness, so it is hard to cut, and some armour cuts at only a tenth of the speed of ordinary steel plate.\nSome hulls also carry radiation shielding made of tungsten or lithium hydride. These materials mainly block radiation, are usually heavy, and are fairly prone to brittle cracking.\nArmour strips on the outside of the hull are generally held by bolts. If you can find the fixing positions, removing the bolts is usually much faster than cutting through the whole armour plate, and also reduces the heat produced by cutting."],
	"cx_insul": ["隔热层", "INSULATION"],
	"cx_insul_a": ["船体内部用来隔绝热量的结构，有些是在两层金属蒙皮之间填充隔热泡沫，有些则使用多层隔热毯，主要用来保持冷藏舱和低温储罐的温度。", "Structures inside the hull that block heat. Some have insulating foam filled between two metal skins, others use multilayer insulation blankets. They mainly keep cold rooms and cryogenic tanks at temperature."],
	"cx_insul_b": ["如果提前拆除了隔热层，外部的热量就会更快进入冷藏舱和低温储罐，导致内部温度上升。低温储罐里的液体还可能因为受热而加快蒸发，让罐内压力不断增加。", "If the insulation is removed too early, heat from outside reaches cold rooms and cryogenic tanks faster, and the temperature inside rises. The liquid in a cryogenic tank may also boil off faster when heated, so the pressure in the tank keeps rising."],
	"cx_insul_c": ["拆解隔热层之前，先确认附近的冷藏设备和低温储罐已经处理完成。如果里面还有需要保持低温的货物，就暂时保留隔热层，等货物转移完成以后再拆除。", "Before dismantling insulation, make sure the nearby refrigeration equipment and cryogenic tanks have been dealt with. If there is still cargo inside that must be kept cold, leave the insulation in place for now and remove it after the cargo has been moved."],
	"cx_insul_x": ["真空环境中的多层隔热毯通常由几十层镀铝薄膜组成，可以通过反射热辐射来减少热量传递。隔热层保持完整时，每平方米的漏热量通常只有零点几瓦。\n如果在隔热毯上划开一道缺口，受损区域的漏热量就可能增加到原来的十倍以上，导致内部温度上升得更快。\n对于装有低温货物的储罐来说，隔热层的完整程度会直接影响货物的升温和蒸发速度，所以最好等低温货物全部处理完成以后，再开始拆除隔热结构。", "In vacuum, a multilayer insulation blanket is usually made of dozens of layers of aluminised film, which reduces heat transfer by reflecting thermal radiation. While the insulation is intact, the heat leak is usually only a fraction of a watt per square metre.\nIf you slit the blanket, the heat leak in the damaged area may rise to more than ten times the original, and the temperature inside rises faster.\nFor a tank holding cryogenic cargo, how intact the insulation is directly affects how fast the cargo warms and boils off, so it is best to start removing insulation only after all the cryogenic cargo has been dealt with."],
	"cx_cover": ["检修盖与护板", "SERVICE COVERS"],
	"cx_cover_a": ["船体上用来保护设备或遮挡固定位置的盖板，有些设备和螺栓安装在盖板后面，需要拆除盖板以后才能接触到。", "Panels on the hull that protect equipment or hide fixing points. Some equipment and bolts sit behind a cover and can only be reached after it is removed."],
	"cx_cover_b": ["有些固定螺栓藏在盖板后面，从外面看不到，也无法直接拆卸。如果没有注意到这些位置，就可能漏掉固定螺栓，导致后面的设备无法正常拆除。", "Some fixing bolts are hidden behind covers, so they cannot be seen from outside and cannot be removed directly. If you do not notice these positions, you may miss a fixing bolt, and then the equipment behind cannot be removed properly."],
	"cx_cover_c": ["遇到检修盖或者护板时，可以先把盖板拆下来，再检查后面有没有隐藏的螺栓或其他固定位置，确认以后再继续拆解设备。", "When you meet a service cover or guard plate, take the cover off first, then check behind it for hidden bolts or other fixing points, and carry on dismantling the equipment only after confirming."],
	"cx_cover_x": ["工程蓝图通常会标出盖板后面的设备和固定位置，不过图纸记录的是船体设计时的结构，实际拆解的船只可能经过维修或者改装，所以有些位置会和图纸不一样。\n被盖板挡住的固定点不会在光标上显示，也无法直接操作。只有拆除盖板以后，才能找到并拆卸后面的固定螺栓。", "Engineering blueprints usually mark the equipment and fixing points behind a cover. However, the drawing records the structure at the time of design, and a ship being dismantled may have been repaired or modified, so some positions may differ from the drawing.\nFixing points hidden behind a cover are not shown on the cursor and cannot be operated directly. Only after the cover is removed can you find and undo the fixing bolts behind it."],
	"cx_port": ["接口（测压口 / 回收口）", "PORT"],
	"cx_port_a": ["船体上用来连接测量工具或者回收软管的接口，一般安装在舱室、储罐或者管路上，可以通过这些接口检查内部压力，也可以把里面的气体和液体回收出来。", "A connection on the hull for the measuring tool or the recovery hose, usually fitted on a room, tank or line. Through it you can check the internal pressure, and recover the gas and liquid inside."],
	"cx_port_b": ["测压口只能测量与它连通的那段管路，如果中间的阀门处于关闭状态，就算压力读数显示为零，也不能说明舱室或者储罐里面已经没有气压。", "A pressure port can only measure the section of line it is connected to. If a valve in between is shut, a pressure reading of zero does not mean the room or tank has no pressure."],
	"cx_port_c": ["使用接口之前，先打开工程图，检查接口连接到了哪个舱室或者储罐，再确认中间的阀门已经打开，避免测量到错误的压力数据。", "Before using a port, open the engineering drawing and check which room or tank it is connected to, then confirm the valves in between are open, so you do not read the wrong pressure."],
	"cx_port_x": ["测压口后面通常连接着一小段管路和阀门，如果阀门处于关闭状态，测量工具只能读取这段短管里面的压力，即使显示为零，阀门另一侧也可能还有大量高压气体。\n回收口则可以连接软管，通过船坞的回收泵把船内的气体或者液体抽出来，其中回收的气体会按照对应价值计入合同收益。\n回收速度主要取决于接口的口径和回收泵的工作能力，如果接口太小，就算使用更大的回收泵，也很难明显提高回收速度。", "Behind a pressure port there is usually a short pipe and a valve. If the valve is shut, the measuring tool can only read the pressure in that short pipe, and even if it shows zero, there may still be a lot of high-pressure gas on the other side of the valve.\nA recovery port can take a hose, and the berth’s recovery pump draws the gas or liquid out of the ship. The gas recovered is counted into the contract income at its corresponding value.\nRecovery speed mainly depends on the port’s bore and the recovery pump’s capacity. If the port is too small, even a larger recovery pump will hardly raise the recovery speed."],
	"cx_valve": ["阀门", "VALVE"],
	"cx_valve_a": ["安装在船体管路上的手动阀门，可以控制管路的开启和关闭，也能用来切断两个舱室或容器之间的连接。", "A manual valve fitted on the ship’s lines. It opens and closes the line, and can also cut the connection between two rooms or containers."],
	"cx_valve_b": ["关闭的阀门会把管路隔成不同的部分，如果只测量其中一段，就可能误以为整条管路都已经排空。有些阀门还可能因为故障而卡住，导致后面无法正常连接软管。", "A closed valve splits a line into separate parts. If you measure only one section, you may wrongly think the whole line has been emptied. Some valves may also jam through a fault, so a hose cannot be connected properly afterwards."],
	"cx_valve_c": ["可以使用维护工具开启或关闭阀门。如果遇到卡死的阀门，就先使用扳手把它拧开，再继续处理管路。", "You can open or close a valve with the maintenance tool. If a valve is jammed, free it with the wrench first, then carry on with the line."],
	"cx_valve_x": ["阀门可以把整套管路分成几个独立的部分，每一段管路里面的压力和液位都可能不同，所以其中一段已经排空，并不代表其他部分也已经安全。\n检查管路的时候，可以按照工程图找到对应接口，再沿着管路逐段检查。每经过一个阀门，都要确认它当前处于开启还是关闭状态，避免遗漏仍然存在压力或残留液体的管路。", "Valves can divide a whole line system into several independent parts, and the pressure and liquid level in each section may differ, so one section being empty does not mean the other parts are safe.\nWhen checking lines, follow the engineering drawing to find the matching port, then check the line section by section. At every valve, confirm whether it is currently open or shut, so you do not miss a line that still holds pressure or leftover liquid."],
	"cx_switch": ["开关", "SWITCH"],
	"cx_switch_a": ["船上的开关可以用来切断电路、控制设备待发状态，也可以操作刹车和机械锁等装置。不同开关控制的设备和功能也会有所区别。", "Switches on the ship can cut a circuit, set equipment to standby, and operate devices such as brakes and mechanical locks. Different switches control different equipment and functions."],
	"cx_switch_b": ["关闭一个开关，通常只能切断它所控制的那条线路。如果船上还有备用电池、独立电源或者储能设备，其他线路就可能仍然带电，直接拆解会有危险。", "Turning off one switch usually cuts only the line it controls. If the ship also has backup batteries, independent supplies or energy storage, other lines may still be live, and dismantling them directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_switch_c": ["关闭开关以后，先使用测量工具检查对应线路的电压，确认电压已经降到 0 V，再继续拆解相关设备。", "After turning a switch off, use the measuring tool to check the voltage of the line concerned, confirm it has dropped to 0 V, and only then continue dismantling the related equipment."],
	"cx_switch_x": ["设备关闭以后，不代表内部已经完全断电。主开关一般只能切断主电源，备用电池和独立供电线路仍然可能带电，电容组也可能保留之前储存的电能。\n部分设备还需要按照指定顺序操作开关，比如先完成冷却再解除刹车，或者先释放内部压力再拔出锁销。如果操作顺序错误，可能会导致设备损坏，甚至引发危险，所以拆解之前最好先确认每个开关的作用。", "Equipment being switched off does not mean it is completely dead inside. The main switch can usually cut only the main supply, while backup batteries and independent supply lines may still be live, and capacitor banks may still hold the energy stored earlier.\nSome equipment also needs its switches operated in a set order, such as finishing cooling before releasing the brake, or releasing internal pressure before pulling the locking pin. A wrong order may damage the equipment or even cause danger, so it is best to confirm what each switch does before dismantling."],
	"cx_test": ["验电点", "TEST POINT"],
	"cx_test_a": ["船体电网上专门用来测量电压的位置，可以使用测量工具读取对应线路的电压，检查这部分电路是否已经断电。", "A place on the ship’s grid made for measuring voltage. You can use the measuring tool to read the voltage of that line and check whether this part of the circuit has been de-energised."],
	"cx_test_b": ["验电点只能显示它所在那段线路的电压，其他支路可能连接着独立电源，所以一个位置显示 0 V，并不代表整艘船的电路都已经断电。", "A test point shows only the voltage of the section of line it is on. Other branches may be connected to independent supplies, so 0 V at one position does not mean the circuits of the whole ship are dead."],
	"cx_test_c": ["先切断相关线路的电源，再释放电容等设备中储存的电能，完成这些操作以后，重新使用测量工具检查电压，确认读数为 0 V 再开始拆解。", "First cut the power to the lines concerned, then release the energy stored in capacitors and similar equipment. After that, check the voltage with the measuring tool again, and start dismantling only when the reading is 0 V."],
	"cx_test_x": ["验电点显示的是测量时的电压，如果测量完成以后又操作了其他开关，线路的供电状态就可能发生变化，之前的读数也就不能继续作为判断依据。\n比较安全的操作顺序是先断开电源，再释放储存的电能，随后进行验电。一定要在前两项操作完成以后重新测量，如果中途修改了开关状态，也需要再次确认电压，避免根据之前的读数进行拆解。", "A test point shows the voltage at the time of measurement. If you operate other switches after measuring, the supply state of the line may change, and the earlier reading can no longer be relied on.\nThe safer order is to isolate the power first, then release the stored energy, and then test. Always measure again after the first two steps are done, and if you change any switch state in between, confirm the voltage again, so you never dismantle on the strength of an earlier reading."],
	"cx_probe": ["探头", "PROBE"],
	"cx_probe_a": ["安装在船体和各种设备上的传感器，可以用来测量温度、液位、辐射剂量、张力和转速等数据，帮助你了解设备当前的运行状态。", "Sensors fitted on the hull and various equipment. They can measure data such as temperature, level, radiation dose, tension and rotation speed, and help you see the equipment’s current state."],
	"cx_probe_b": ["有些设备即使已经停止运行，内部也可能残留压力、热量或者其他危险。如果没有提前查看探头的读数，就很难判断设备是否已经达到安全的拆解条件。", "Some equipment may still hold pressure, heat or other dangers inside even after it has stopped running. If you have not read the probe beforehand, it is hard to tell whether the equipment has reached a safe condition for dismantling."],
	"cx_probe_c": ["开始拆解之前，先使用测量工具查看相关探头的读数，确认设备目前的状态。完成操作以后再测量一次，检查数值有没有达到安全范围。", "Before dismantling, read the relevant probes with the measuring tool to confirm the equipment’s current state. After the work, measure again and check whether the values have reached the safe range."],
	"cx_probe_x": ["船上的很多特殊设备都有对应的测量探头，包括线圈的储存能量、飞轮的转速、钻杆的扭矩、储罐的压力、舱室内的氧气浓度、辐射剂量率和炉芯温度等。\n这些读数可以帮助你判断设备是否已经达到安全状态。如果数值还没有降到要求的范围，就说明可能还需要继续等待，或者检查有没有遗漏的操作。拆解之前多检查一次，通常能避免后面出现不必要的事故。", "Many special pieces of equipment on the ship have matching measuring probes, including a coil’s stored energy, a flywheel’s rotation speed, a drill string’s torque, a tank’s pressure, the oxygen concentration in a room, radiation dose rate and a furnace core’s temperature.\nThese readings help you judge whether the equipment has reached a safe state. If a value has not yet dropped to the required range, you may need to keep waiting, or check for a step you missed. Checking once more before dismantling usually avoids needless accidents later."],
	"cx_socket": ["外部插座", "EXTERNAL SOCKET"],
	"cx_socket_a": ["船坞外部面板上的连接接口，可以为船体提供临时电力、冷却系统和接地线路，方便在拆解过程中继续使用部分设备。", "Connection ports on the berth’s external panel. They can supply the hull with temporary power, a cooling system and an earthing line, so that some equipment can keep running during dismantling."],
	"cx_socket_b": ["有些设备在切断船体电源以后，仍然需要电力或者冷却才能安全关闭。如果提前断开电源，又没有接好船坞提供的外部接口，就可能导致这些设备无法正常工作。", "Some equipment still needs power or cooling to shut down safely after the ship’s power is cut. If you cut the power too early without connecting the berth’s external ports, this equipment may fail to work properly."],
	"cx_socket_c": ["切断船体电源之前，先找到船坞外部面板上的对应插座，把需要的供电、供冷或者接地线路连接好，再继续拆解。", "Before cutting the ship’s power, find the matching sockets on the berth’s external panel, connect the power, cooling or earthing lines you need, and then continue dismantling."],
	"cx_socket_x": ["船坞的外部供电可以让舱门、水泵和制冷机在船体断电以后继续工作，这样就不用担心拆除电池后，还有设备需要通电才能完成操作。\n外部供冷可以让冷链货舱继续保持低温，避免货物因为温度升高而损坏。接地线路则可以把帆面等大面积结构上积累的静电导走，减少拆解时发生静电放电的风险。\n这些接口都安装在船坞的外部面板上，需要完成连接以后才能发挥作用。", "The berth’s external power lets doors, pumps and chillers keep working after the ship’s power is cut, so you need not worry that some equipment still needs power to finish its operation after the battery is removed.\nExternal cooling lets a cold-chain hold stay cold, so cargo is not spoiled by a temperature rise. The earthing line can conduct away the static charge built up on large structures such as sail panels, reducing the risk of electrostatic discharge during dismantling.\nThese ports are all fitted on the berth’s external panel and only take effect once they are connected."],
	"cx_discharge": ["放电点", "DISCHARGE POINT"],
	"cx_discharge_a": ["安装在设备附近接线盒上的放电开关，可以让电容组通过电阻缓慢放电，把内部储存的电能释放掉。", "A discharge switch fitted on a junction box near the equipment. It lets a capacitor bank discharge slowly through a resistor and releases the energy stored inside."],
	"cx_discharge_b": ["电容即使已经断开电源，内部也可能储存着大量电能。如果没有完成放电就直接拆解，接触带电部件时可能产生高压电弧，造成严重伤害。", "Even when disconnected from the power, a capacitor may still store a great deal of energy. If you dismantle it before discharging, touching a live part can produce a high-voltage arc and cause serious injury."],
	"cx_discharge_c": ["拆解电容组之前，先找到附近接线盒上的放电开关，启动放电程序。等电量显示归零以后，还需要使用检测工具确认没有残余电压，再开始拆解。", "Before dismantling a capacitor bank, find the discharge switch on the nearby junction box and start the discharge. When the charge reading falls to zero, also check with the test tool that no residual voltage is left, and only then start dismantling."],
	"cx_discharge_x": ["电容可以在断电以后继续储存电能，储存的能量可以通过公式 E = ½CV² 计算。一组容量为 0.1 F 的电容，如果电压达到 400 V，内部就储存着 8 kJ 的能量，即使已经切断电源，也可能在接触时产生危险的电弧。\n通过电阻放电时，电容的电压会按照 e^(−t/RC) 的规律逐渐降低，大约经过五个时间常数以后，电压就会降到初始值的 1% 以下。\n放电开关一般安装在设备附近的接线盒上，完成放电以后还要检查剩余电压，确认安全才能继续拆解。", "A capacitor can keep its stored energy after the power is cut, and the stored energy can be calculated with the formula E = ½CV². A bank of 0.1 F at 400 V stores 8 kJ of energy, and even after the supply is cut, touching it can produce a dangerous arc.\nWhen discharging through a resistor, the capacitor’s voltage falls gradually following e^(−t/RC), and after about five time constants it drops below 1% of its initial value.\nThe discharge switch is generally on a junction box near the equipment. After discharging, check the remaining voltage, and continue dismantling only once it is confirmed safe."],
	"cx_seal": ["密封盖", "SEAL"],
	"cx_seal_a": ["用来封存船上生物危险品的装置，可以通过密封袋或者密封盖把危险品封闭起来，防止污染物在搬运过程中扩散。", "A device for sealing the ship’s biohazard items. It closes the hazardous item in with a sealing bag or sealing cap, to stop contaminants spreading while it is being moved."],
	"cx_seal_b": ["如果还没有完成密封就直接搬运或者切割，里面的污染物可能会进入舱室空气，并随着空气流动扩散到其他位置，导致更多设备受到污染。", "If you move or cut it before sealing is complete, the contaminants inside may get into the room’s air and spread with the air flow to other places, contaminating more equipment."],
	"cx_seal_c": ["处理生物危险品之前，先使用密封袋或者密封盖把危险品封好，确认不会发生泄漏以后，再把整件危险品送到专门的危险品回收口。", "Before handling a biohazard item, seal it with the sealing bag or cap, confirm it will not leak, and then take the whole item to the dedicated hazard recovery mouth."],
	"cx_seal_x": ["生物污染物可以随着空气流动扩散，如果舱室里面还有没有密封的危险品，直接打开舱门或者切开舱壁，就可能让污染物进入隔壁舱室。\n一旦设备受到污染，即使设备本身没有损坏，也需要先经过清洗和消毒才能回收，最终价值会降低 25%。\n所以在拆解受到生物污染的舱室之前，最好先把里面的危险品全部密封好，再继续处理周围的船体结构。", "Biological contaminants can spread with the air flow. If a room still holds unsealed hazardous items, opening its door or cutting its bulkhead directly may let the contaminants into the next room.\nOnce equipment is contaminated, it has to be cleaned and disinfected before recovery even if the equipment itself is undamaged, and its final value is reduced by 25%.\nSo before dismantling a biologically contaminated room, it is best to seal all the hazardous items inside first, and only then deal with the surrounding hull structure."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- systems
	"cx_s_gas": ["舱压", "ROOM PRESSURE"],
	"cx_s_gas_a": ["船上的密封舱室里可能还存有空气或者其他工艺气体，这些气体会让舱室内部保持一定的压力，拆解之前需要先检查。", "Sealed rooms on the ship may still hold air or other process gases. These gases keep the room under some pressure, and it must be checked before dismantling."],
	"cx_s_gas_b": ["如果舱室里面还有较高的气压，直接打开舱门或者切开舱壁，就可能让里面的气体突然喷出，严重时甚至会把舱门、舱壁板和附近的设备一起冲出去。", "If a room still has high pressure, opening its door or cutting its bulkhead directly may make the gas inside burst out suddenly, and in bad cases it throws out the door, the bulkhead plate and nearby equipment together."],
	"cx_s_gas_c": ["拆解密封舱室之前，先通过接口检查内部气压，再连接回收软管，把舱室压力降到 5 kPa 以下，确认泄压完成以后才能打开舱门或者切割舱壁。", "Before dismantling a sealed room, check its internal pressure at a port, then connect the recovery hose and bring the room pressure below 5 kPa. Open the door or cut the bulkhead only after confirming the venting is complete."],
	"cx_s_gas_x": ["舱室里的气压与内部气体的数量、温度和舱室容积有关，可以用公式 pV = nRT 来表示。\n连接回收泵以后，舱室里的气体会逐渐被抽走，内部压力也会随之降低。舱室越大，或者抽气接口越小，完成泄压需要的时间就越长，一些大型舱室可能需要几十秒才能达到安全压力。\n如果直接打开舱门或者切开舱壁，里面的气体就会从开口流向压力较低的一侧。几个原本独立的舱室一旦连通，内部的气压也会相互影响。\n通过回收泵抽走的气体还可以按照回收价值计入合同，所以提前完成气体回收，也能获得额外收入。", "The pressure in a room depends on the amount and temperature of the gas inside and on the room volume, and can be expressed by the formula pV = nRT.\nOnce the recovery pump is connected, the gas in the room is gradually drawn off and the internal pressure falls with it. The larger the room, or the smaller the port, the longer venting takes, and some large rooms may need tens of seconds to reach a safe pressure.\nIf you open the door or cut the bulkhead directly, the gas inside flows through the opening to the lower-pressure side. Once several originally separate rooms are connected, their pressures also affect one another.\nGas drawn off by the recovery pump is also counted into the contract at its recovery value, so recovering the gas early earns extra income."],
	"cx_s_stale": ["过期", "STALE"],
	"cx_s_stale_a": ["检测工具显示的数值只代表测量时的状态。如果后面又对船上的设备进行了操作，之前测到的数值就可能不准确了。", "A value shown by the test tool represents only the state at the time of measurement. If you then operate other equipment on the ship, the value you measured earlier may no longer be accurate."],
	"cx_s_stale_b": ["打开阀门、切断电源或者修改电路连接以后，设备的实际状态可能已经发生变化。如果继续按照之前的检测结果进行拆解，就有可能误判当前的压力或者电力状态。", "After you open a valve, cut a supply or change a circuit connection, the actual state of the equipment may have changed. If you carry on dismantling by the earlier test result, you may misjudge the current pressure or power state."],
	"cx_s_stale_c": ["每次操作设备或者改变连接状态以后，最好重新检测一次，确认当前状态是否安全。已经过期的检测数值会显示成灰色，看到这种情况就需要重新测量。", "After every operation on equipment or change of connection state, it is best to test again and confirm the current state is safe. A stale test value is shown in grey, and when you see that, you need to measure again."],
	"cx_s_stale_x": ["如果舱室压力与上次测量时相比，变化超过 2 kPa 或者 4%，之前的压力读数就会被标记为过期。电路的连接关系发生改变以后，相关的电力检测结果也会失效。\n船上的控制面板和总览屏通常显示的是上一次记录的数据，这些数据也可能已经过期，所以不能完全依靠它们判断当前状态。\n拆解之前，最好使用自己的检测工具重新测量，确认设备当前的实际状态以后再继续操作。", "If the room pressure has changed by more than 2 kPa or 4% since the last measurement, the earlier pressure reading is marked stale. Once the circuit connections change, the related power test results also become invalid.\nControl panels and overview screens on the ship usually show the data from the last record, which may also be stale, so you cannot rely on them entirely to judge the current state.\nBefore dismantling, it is best to measure again with your own test tool, and carry on only after confirming the actual current state of the equipment."],
	"cx_s_power": ["电网与多路电源", "POWER AND ITS SOURCES"],
	"cx_s_power_a": ["船上的发电机、电池和电容都可以为设备提供电力，大部分设备通过船体总线供电，也有一些设备使用独立电源，所以切断主电源以后，船上仍然可能有带电的设备。", "Generators, batteries and capacitors on the ship can all supply power to equipment. Most equipment is powered through the ship’s bus, but some uses an independent supply, so after the main power is cut, there may still be live equipment on the ship."],
	"cx_s_power_b": ["关闭船体主电源以后，备用电池和独立电源可能还在供电，电容里面也可能储存着没有释放的电能。如果直接拆除这些设备或者切断电缆，就有可能产生电弧。", "After the ship’s main power is switched off, backup batteries and independent supplies may still be supplying power, and capacitors may hold energy that has not been released. If you remove this equipment or cut its cables directly, an arc may result."],
	"cx_s_power_c": ["拆解电力设备之前，先查看工程图，确认船上有哪些供电线路和独立电源，再逐个断开电源并完成电容放电。处理完成以后，还需要使用检测工具重新验电，确认没有残余电压才能开始拆解。", "Before dismantling power equipment, check the engineering drawing to confirm which supply lines and independent supplies the ship has, then disconnect each supply in turn and discharge the capacitors. When that is done, test the voltage again with the test tool, and start dismantling only after confirming no residual voltage is left."],
	"cx_s_power_x": ["工程图的电路层会标出每条电缆的连接位置，可以通过这些线路找到对应的电源和设备。\n有些设备使用自己的独立电源，包括无人机电池、舱门备用电源和仪器的不间断电源。这些电源通常只负责附近的设备，关闭船体主开关也不会切断它们的供电。\n如果独立电源连接到了船体总线，还可能通过总线向其他设备供电，所以即使已经关闭主电源，也不能直接认定整条线路都已经断电。\n电压超过 30 V 的设备，在拔除电缆或者进行切割时就可能产生电弧。拆解之前需要检查所有供电线路，断开剩余电源并完成放电，最后重新验电，确认安全以后再继续操作。", "The circuit layer of the engineering drawing marks where each cable connects, and through these lines you can find the matching supplies and equipment.\nSome equipment uses its own independent supply, including drone batteries, door backup supplies and instrument UPS units. These supplies usually power only the equipment nearby, and switching off the ship’s main switch does not cut their supply.\nIf an independent supply is connected to the ship’s bus, it can also feed other equipment through the bus, so even after the main power is off, you cannot assume the whole line is dead.\nEquipment above 30 V can produce an arc when its cable is unplugged or cut. Before dismantling, check all supply lines, disconnect the remaining supplies and discharge, then test the voltage again, and carry on only after confirming it is safe."],
	"cx_s_heat": ["热管线与余热", "HEAT"],
	"cx_s_heat_a": ["发动机、反应堆和加热炉等设备即使已经停止运行，内部的管线和零件也可能保持很高的温度，需要经过一段时间的冷却才能安全拆除。", "Even after equipment such as engines, reactors and furnaces has stopped running, the lines and parts inside may stay very hot, and need some time to cool before they can be removed safely."],
	"cx_s_heat_b": ["如果设备温度还在 60°C 以上，直接使用无人机抓取可能会造成无人机损坏。如果使用不合适的方法快速降温，也可能因为温度变化太大，导致管线或设备出现裂纹。", "If equipment is still above 60°C, grabbing it directly with the drone may damage the drone. If you cool it quickly by an unsuitable method, the temperature change may also be so large that lines or equipment crack."],
	"cx_s_heat_c": ["拆解之前先测量设备温度，确认冷却系统还在正常运行，让设备慢慢降温。等温度降到安全范围以后，再开始拆除管线和其他零件。", "Before dismantling, measure the equipment temperature, confirm the cooling system is still running normally, and let the equipment cool slowly. Once the temperature has dropped to a safe range, start removing the lines and other parts."],
	"cx_s_heat_x": ["真空环境里没有空气对流，设备只能通过热辐射和接触部件之间的热传导慢慢散热。一些温度达到几百度的大型设备，如果只依靠自然冷却，可能需要几个小时才能降到安全温度。\n冷却系统需要有电力供应和足够的冷却液才能正常工作，如果设备还很热就提前切断冷却系统，剩余的热量会很难散出去，冷却时间也会变得更长。所以拆解高温设备时，最好先保持冷却系统运行，等设备充分降温以后再切断电源。", "There is no air convection in vacuum, so equipment can only lose heat slowly by thermal radiation and by conduction between parts in contact. A large piece of equipment at a few hundred degrees may take several hours to fall to a safe temperature by natural cooling alone.\nThe cooling system needs a power supply and enough coolant to work. If you cut the cooling system while the equipment is still hot, the remaining heat is hard to get out and cooling takes even longer. So when dismantling hot equipment, it is best to keep the cooling system running first, and cut the power only after the equipment has cooled fully."],
	"cx_s_cloud": ["推进剂云", "PROPELLANT CLOUD"],
	"cx_s_cloud_a": ["燃料发生泄漏以后，挥发出来的蒸气可能会聚集在舱室里面，或者在船体外面形成一团燃料气体。", "After a fuel leak, the vapour that evaporates may gather inside a room, or form a cloud of fuel gas outside the hull."],
	"cx_s_cloud_b": ["如果燃料蒸气达到能够燃烧的浓度，附近的激光切割就可能将其点燃。如果舱室里面聚集了大量燃料蒸气，还可能发生爆燃，损坏附近的设备。", "If the fuel vapour reaches a concentration that can burn, laser cutting nearby may ignite it. If a large amount of fuel vapour has gathered in a room, it may also deflagrate and damage nearby equipment."],
	"cx_s_cloud_c": ["发现推进剂泄漏以后，先把剩余的燃料回收干净，等泄漏形成的气体充分扩散，确认附近没有危险以后，再继续进行切割。", "After finding a propellant leak, first recover the remaining fuel, wait until the gas from the leak has dispersed fully and you have confirmed there is no danger nearby, and then continue cutting."],
	"cx_s_cloud_x": ["燃料蒸气需要达到一定的浓度才能燃烧，浓度太低或者太高都可能无法点燃。拿肼和氢气来说，肼在空气中的可燃浓度范围约为 4.7%～100%，氢气则约为 4%～75%。\n即使云团中心的燃料浓度太高，外围也可能存在浓度刚好适合燃烧的区域，只要接触到火源，就有可能发生燃烧。\n在真空环境下，泄漏的燃料蒸气会逐渐向周围扩散，浓度也会慢慢降低。如果泄漏发生在有空气的封闭舱室里面，燃料蒸气就可能聚集更长时间，需要先完成通风和气体清理，才能安全进行切割。", "Fuel vapour has to reach a certain concentration to burn, and if it is too low or too high it may not ignite. Take hydrazine and hydrogen: hydrazine’s flammable range in air is about 4.7%–100%, and hydrogen’s is about 4%–75%.\nEven if the fuel concentration at the centre of the cloud is too high, there may be a zone at the edge where the concentration is just right for burning, and if it meets an ignition source, it can burn.\nIn vacuum, leaked fuel vapour gradually spreads outwards and its concentration slowly falls. If the leak is in a closed room with air, the fuel vapour may gather for longer, and you must finish ventilating and clearing the gas before you can cut safely."],
	"cx_s_fire": ["火灾", "FIRE"],
	"cx_s_fire_a": ["燃料需要接触空气中的氧气或者其他氧化剂才能燃烧。如果周围是真空环境，而且没有其他氧化剂，泄漏的燃料一般只会逐渐蒸发、冻结或者向周围扩散。", "Fuel needs oxygen from the air or another oxidiser to burn. If the surroundings are vacuum and there is no other oxidiser, leaked fuel generally just gradually evaporates, freezes or drifts away."],
	"cx_s_fire_b": ["激光切割、电弧、带电电缆产生的火花、短路、高温切口、发动机尾焰和爆炸都可能引燃附近的燃料。\n一旦舱室发生火灾，火焰就可能逐渐蔓延到其他区域。严重时，舱内压力甚至可能上升到原来的 8 倍，导致舱门被气压冲开。", "Laser cutting, arcs, sparks from live cables, short circuits, hot cuts, engine exhaust and explosions can all ignite nearby fuel.\nOnce a room catches fire, the flames may gradually spread to other areas. In serious cases, the pressure in the room can even rise to 8 times the original, so that the door is blown open by the pressure."],
	"cx_s_fire_c": ["使用激光切割工具之前，先把舱室里的空气抽干净，确认内部已经达到真空状态。\n如果舱室已经发生火灾，暂时不要打开舱门，以免外面的空气进入，让火势进一步扩大。保持舱室封闭，等内部氧气消耗到无法维持燃烧时，火焰就会逐渐熄灭。", "Before using the laser, pump the room’s air out and confirm it is at vacuum.\nIf a room is already on fire, keep its door shut so outside air cannot feed the fire. Once the oxygen inside is used up, the flames go out."],
	"cx_s_fire_x": ["燃烧需要燃料、氧气和点火源三个条件，只要缺少其中一个，火焰就无法继续维持。\n在失重环境下，火焰不会像地面上一样向上燃烧，因为这里没有重力造成的自然对流。火焰可能形成一个缓慢扩散的球形区域，主要依靠周围氧气的扩散来维持燃烧。\n如果舱室完全封闭，火焰会持续消耗内部的氧气，等氧气浓度下降到一定程度以后，燃烧就会停止。不过这时候燃料可能还留在舱室里面，如果重新打开舱门，让空气进入，再遇到火花就可能再次起火。\n封闭舱室发生火灾时，燃烧产生的高温还会让内部气体迅速膨胀。如果气体温度上升到几千度，舱内压力就可能增加到原来的数倍，严重时甚至会损坏舱门和周围的船体结构。", "Burning needs three conditions: fuel, oxygen and an ignition source. If any one is missing, the flame cannot be sustained.\nIn weightlessness, flames do not burn upwards as they do on the ground, because there is no natural convection caused by gravity. A flame may form a slowly spreading sphere, sustained mainly by oxygen diffusing in from around it.\nIf the room is completely closed, the fire keeps using up the oxygen inside, and once the oxygen concentration falls to a certain level, burning stops. By then the fuel may still be left in the room, though, and if you open the door again and let air in, a spark may start the fire again.\nWhen a closed room is on fire, the high temperature of the burning also makes the gas inside expand rapidly. If the gas temperature rises to several thousand degrees, the pressure in the room may increase to several times the original, and in serious cases it can even damage the door and the surrounding hull structure."],
	"cx_s_liquid": ["失重液体", "LIQUIDS IN FREE FALL"],
	"cx_s_liquid_a": ["船上的管线或储罐发生泄漏以后，里面的液体会进入失重环境，并在表面张力的作用下形成漂浮的液团。", "After a line or tank on the ship leaks, the liquid inside enters weightlessness and forms floating globules under surface tension."],
	"cx_s_liquid_b": ["泄漏的液体如果接触到还在通电的设备，可能会造成短路。如果泄漏的是燃料，在附近使用激光切割工具还可能引起火灾。温度很低的液体也会对设备造成损伤，严重时甚至会让零件冻裂。", "If leaked liquid touches equipment that is still powered, it may cause a short circuit. If the leaked liquid is fuel, using the laser cutting tool nearby may also start a fire. Very cold liquids can also damage equipment, and in serious cases even freeze-crack parts."],
	"cx_s_liquid_c": ["拆除管线或储罐之前，先把软管连接到对应的接口，将里面剩余的液体抽取干净，确认没有残留液体以后，再开始切割管线或者拆除储罐。", "Before removing a line or tank, connect the hose to the matching port and draw off the liquid left inside. Once you have confirmed no liquid remains, start cutting the line or removing the tank."],
	"cx_s_liquid_x": ["在失重环境下，液体会受到表面张力的影响，逐渐聚集成球形液团。如果没有其他外力影响，这些液团就会沿着原来的运动方向继续漂浮，碰到设备表面以后，可能会溅散成更小的液滴，也可能附着在表面形成一层液膜。\n不同液体泄漏以后还会出现不同的情况。液氢和液氦会在泄漏时迅速汽化一部分，剩余液体也会继续沸腾；水在真空环境下可能在几秒内结成冰球；燃料会逐渐挥发，产生的蒸气如果聚集起来，就可能形成可燃气体区域。钻井泥浆则容易附着在接触到的设备表面，增加后续的清理工作。\n所以拆解装有液体的设备之前，最好先通过接口把液体抽取干净，避免切割过程中发生泄漏。", "In weightlessness, liquid is affected by surface tension and gradually gathers into spherical globules. If no other force acts on them, these globules keep drifting in their original direction of motion, and after they hit an equipment surface, they may splash into smaller droplets, or stick to the surface as a liquid film.\nDifferent liquids also behave differently after leaking. Liquid hydrogen and liquid helium flash part of themselves into vapour as they leak, and the rest of the liquid keeps boiling; water in vacuum may freeze into an ice ball within seconds; fuel gradually evaporates, and if the vapour gathers, it may form a flammable gas zone. Drilling mud tends to stick to whatever equipment surface it touches, adding to the cleaning work afterwards.\nSo before dismantling equipment that holds liquid, it is best to draw the liquid off through a port first, to avoid leaks during cutting."],
	"cx_s_hose": ["回收软管", "RECOVERY HOSE"],
	"cx_s_hose_a": ["回收软管用来抽取船上的气体和液体，将软管连接到对应的接口以后，就可以通过船坞的回收泵，把管线或储罐里面的气体和液体抽取出来。", "The recovery hose draws gas and liquid out of the ship. Once the hose is connected to the matching port, the berth’s recovery pump can draw the gas and liquid out of the line or tank."],
	"cx_s_hose_b": ["如果把软管连接到错误的接口，可能会让不同的回收物混在一起，影响回收处理。有些回收泵在抽取完成以后还继续运行，也可能因为没有液体进入而发生空转，造成设备损坏。", "If you connect the hose to the wrong port, different recovered substances may mix and affect recovery processing. Some recovery pumps also keep running after the draw is finished, and may run dry because no liquid is coming in, causing damage to the equipment."],
	"cx_s_hose_c": ["先确认接口对应的回收物，再连接软管开始抽取。抽取过程中注意查看剩余量，等气体或液体回收到指定数量以后，就可以停止回收并取下软管。", "First confirm what the port recovers, then connect the hose and start drawing. While drawing, watch the remaining amount, and once the gas or liquid has been recovered to the set quantity, you can stop recovery and take the hose off."],
	"cx_s_hose_x": ["一条回收软管每次只能连接一个接口。随着储罐里面的气压或者液位逐渐降低，回收速度也会慢慢下降，如果觉得等待时间太长，可以按住「=」键加快游戏时间。\n回收的气体和液体会按照当前市场价格计入合同收入，所以能回收的材料最好尽量保留下来。遇到危险气体或者液体时，还需要连接对应的专用回收接口，不能直接排放到太空中。", "One recovery hose can connect to only one port at a time. As the pressure or liquid level in the tank gradually falls, the recovery speed also slowly drops, and if the wait feels too long, you can hold the ‘=’ key to speed up game time.\nRecovered gas and liquid are counted into the contract income at the current market price, so keep as much recoverable material as you can. When you meet hazardous gas or liquid, you also need to connect the matching dedicated recovery port, and it cannot be vented straight into space."],
	"cx_s_free": ["脱离与惯性", "FREE PIECES AND INERTIA"],
	"cx_s_free_a": ["当零件的最后一个固定点被拆除以后，零件就会完全脱离船体，开始在失重环境中自由漂浮。", "Once a part’s last fixing point is removed, the part comes completely free of the hull and starts to float freely in weightlessness."],
	"cx_s_free_b": ["零件脱离以后，会继续保持原来的移动速度和旋转状态。如果没有及时控制，零件就可能撞上附近的船体结构或者其他设备，造成不必要的损坏。", "After a part comes free, it keeps its original speed and spin. If you do not control it in time, the part may hit nearby hull structure or other equipment and cause needless damage."],
	"cx_s_free_c": ["拆除最后一个固定点之前，先用抓钩固定住零件。等零件完全脱离船体以后，再慢慢调整它的移动方向，将零件送进回收口。", "Before removing the last fixing point, secure the part with the grapple. Once the part has fully come free of the hull, slowly adjust its direction of motion and send the part into a recovery mouth."],
	"cx_s_free_x": ["在失重环境中，如果没有受到其他外力，零件就会一直保持原来的运动状态。即使只是轻轻推动一下，零件也会继续向前移动，想让它停下来，就需要施加反方向的作用力。\n零件的质量和移动速度都会影响撞击时的动量。一件重 3 吨、以 0.5 m/s 移动的设备，和一件重 1 吨、以 1.5 m/s 移动的设备，具有相同大小的动量，失去控制后都可能造成严重损坏。\n如果零件不小心漂出了船坞范围，船坞边缘的牵引场会逐渐把它拉回来。不过拆解大型设备时，最好还是提前使用抓钩控制，避免零件发生碰撞。", "In weightlessness, if no other force acts on it, a part keeps its original state of motion forever. Even a light push keeps the part moving on, and to stop it you need to apply a force in the opposite direction.\nA part’s mass and its speed both affect its momentum on impact. A 3 t piece of equipment moving at 0.5 m/s and a 1 t piece moving at 1.5 m/s have the same momentum, and either can cause serious damage if it gets out of control.\nIf a part accidentally drifts outside the berth area, the tractor field at the berth edge gradually pulls it back. Even so, when dismantling large equipment, it is best to control it with the grapple beforehand, to avoid collisions."],
	"cx_s_grapple": ["磁力抓钩", "MAGNETIC GRAPPLE"],
	"cx_s_grapple_a": ["磁力抓钩是无人机用来固定和拖动零件的工具，可以在拆解过程中控制零件的移动方向，也能把拆下来的设备送到指定位置。", "The magnetic grapple is the tool the drone uses to hold and drag parts. During dismantling it controls a part’s direction of motion, and also carries removed equipment to the place you choose."],
	"cx_s_grapple_b": ["磁力抓钩有一定的承重限制，如果零件超过了额定质量，就无法正常拖动。如果零件还连接着船体，强行拖动可能会扯断固定锁扣和连接管线，造成设备损坏。", "The magnetic grapple has a load limit. If a part exceeds the rated mass, it cannot be dragged properly. If the part is still connected to the hull, dragging it by force may tear off the locks and connecting lines and damage the equipment."],
	"cx_s_grapple_c": ["使用磁力抓钩之前，先检查零件的质量和剩余固定点，确认零件已经完全脱离船体，并且没有超过抓钩的承重限制以后，再开始拖动。", "Before using the magnetic grapple, check the part’s mass and the fixing points remaining, and start dragging only after you have confirmed the part has fully come free of the hull and does not exceed the grapple’s load limit."],
	"cx_s_grapple_x": ["磁力抓钩默认最多可以拖动 3 吨的零件，升级以后可以提高到 5 吨。\n由于无人机的推力有限，拖动较重的设备时，加速和减速都需要更长时间，所以在接近回收口或者其他船体结构之前，最好提前减速，避免因为来不及停止而发生碰撞。\n如果零件还连接着船体，使用抓钩拖动时，光标会显示剩余的固定点数量。继续增加拉力就可能扯断锁扣或者连接管线，所以最好先把这些连接全部拆除，再使用抓钩搬运零件。", "The magnetic grapple can drag parts of up to 3 t by default, and after an upgrade this rises to 5 t.\nBecause the drone’s thrust is limited, accelerating and braking take longer when dragging heavy equipment, so before you approach a recovery mouth or other hull structure, it is best to start slowing down early, to avoid a collision because you could not stop in time.\nIf a part is still connected to the hull, the cursor shows the number of fixing points left when you drag with the grapple. Increasing the pull further may tear off locks or connecting lines, so it is best to remove all these connections first and then move the part with the grapple."],
	"cx_s_furnace": ["熔炉与废料口", "THE FURNACE"],
	"cx_s_furnace_a": ["船坞底部设有专门回收废金属的熔炉入口，拆下来的金属废料可以直接送进去熔炼，处理完成后会按照回收的金属重量结算报酬。", "At the bottom of the berth there is a furnace mouth made for recovering scrap metal. Scrap metal removed from the ship can be sent straight in for melting, and after processing you are paid by the weight of metal recovered."],
	"cx_s_furnace_b": ["不要把危险品或者还带有电压、压力的设备送进熔炉，这些东西在高温下可能发生爆炸。\n完整设备也不建议直接送进去，因为熔炉只会按照废金属的价格结算，原本还能正常使用的设备就卖不出完整回收的价格了。", "Never send hazardous items, or equipment still carrying voltage or pressure, into the furnace: they may explode in the heat.\nDon’t send whole equipment in either. The furnace pays only the scrap-metal price, so working equipment loses its full-recovery price."],
	"cx_s_furnace_c": ["先确认准备回收的材料只有普通金属，没有残留的危险物品。然后在距离熔炉入口大约 6–8 m 的位置，用抓钩将废料对准下方的长条形入口，调整好方向后送进去就可以了。", "First make sure the material to be recovered is only ordinary metal with no hazardous items left. Then, from about 6–8 m away from the furnace mouth, use the grapple to line the scrap up with the long, narrow opening below, and send it in once its direction is right."],
	"cx_s_furnace_x": ["废金属进入熔炉入口以后，会先经过下方的料仓压实，再由螺旋给料机送进真空感应炉进行熔炼。\n熔炉内部的坩埚以每分钟 45 转的速度旋转，产生大约 1.4 g 的离心加速度，让熔融金属保持在炉衬附近。炉体外侧还安装了水冷铜线圈，线圈通电以后会产生交变磁场，使金属内部形成涡流并逐渐升温。电流在金属内部的集肤深度可以用公式 δ = 503 × √(ρ/μf) 计算。\n当炉内温度达到 1640°C 后，熔融金属就会被倒入水冷铜锭模，冷却成型后作为钢锭回收。\n整个熔炼过程需要在真空环境下进行，所以船坞已经为熔炉准备了相应的真空系统，不需要额外调整外部压力。", "After scrap metal enters the furnace mouth, it is first compacted in the bunker below, and then a screw feeder sends it into a vacuum induction furnace to be melted.\nThe crucible inside the furnace spins at 45 revolutions per minute, producing a centrifugal acceleration of about 1.4 g that keeps the molten metal against the lining. Water-cooled copper coils are fitted around the outside of the furnace body, and when the coils are energised they produce an alternating magnetic field, which sets up eddy currents inside the metal and gradually heats it. The skin depth of the current in the metal can be calculated with the formula δ = 503 × √(ρ/μf).\nWhen the temperature in the furnace reaches 1640°C, the molten metal is poured into water-cooled copper ingot moulds, and after cooling and setting it is recovered as steel ingots.\nThe whole melting process has to take place in vacuum, so the berth has already provided the furnace with a matching vacuum system, and you need not adjust any external pressure."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth": ["设备回收口", "EQUIPMENT BAY"],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_a": ["船坞里专门用来回收完整设备的回收口，拆下来的设备需要从下方送进去，才能按照设备的完整价值进行回收。", "The recovery mouth in the berth made for whole equipment. Removed equipment must be fed in from below to be recovered at its full value."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_b": ["如果设备在拆解过程中受到撞击或者切割损坏，回收价格就会按照受损程度降低。如果设备内部还有电力或者残留液体，直接送进回收口还可能引发事故。", "If equipment is knocked or damaged by cutting during dismantling, the recovery price drops according to the damage. If the equipment still holds power or leftover liquid inside, sending it straight into the recovery mouth may also cause an accident."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_c": ["回收设备之前，先切断电源，排空内部的液体，再拔掉连接的线路。确认设备已经安全以后，尽量保持设备完整，再用抓钩把它送进回收口。", "Before recovering equipment, cut its power, drain the liquid inside and unplug the connected lines. Once the equipment is confirmed safe, keep it whole as far as you can, and then send it into the recovery mouth with the grapple."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_x": ["设备的回收价格按照原本价值乘以当前成色计算。如果设备在拆解过程中受到撞击、过热、短路或者污染，成色就会下降，最后能够拿到的回收金额也会减少。\n如果合同要求回收指定设备，就必须把这些设备完整送进回收口，才能满足合同要求。\n当设备距离回收口太远时，回收口的接收环会向设备所在的位置移动，方便你把设备送进去。", "The recovery price of equipment is its original value multiplied by its current condition. If equipment is knocked, overheated, short-circuited or contaminated during dismantling, its condition drops, and the recovery payment you finally get is smaller.\nIf a contract requires recovery of named equipment, those items must be sent whole into the recovery mouth to meet the contract requirement.\nWhen equipment is too far from the recovery mouth, the mouth’s receiving ring moves towards where the equipment is, so it is easier to send it in."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth": ["危险品回收口", "HAZARD MOUTH"],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_a": ["船坞里专门用来回收危险品的地方，燃料罐、电池、火工品和放射源等物品都需要送到这里处理。", "The place in the berth made for recovering hazardous items. Fuel tanks, batteries, pyrotechnics and radioactive sources all need to be taken here for handling."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_b": ["危险品不能直接送进熔炉，如果把燃料罐或者其他危险物品送进去，可能会引发爆炸，也可能造成熔炉污染。", "Hazardous items must not be sent straight into the furnace. If a fuel tank or another hazardous item is sent in, it may explode, and may also contaminate the furnace."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_c": ["拆解过程中，如果光标指向的物品显示为「危险品」，就需要把它送进危险品回收口，不要送到普通的设备回收口或者熔炉里。", "During dismantling, if the item the cursor points at is shown as ‘hazard’, it must go into the hazard mouth, not the ordinary equipment recovery mouth or the furnace."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_x": ["危险品会按照危险处理津贴计算回收收入，不会按照普通金属的价格结算，所以需要把它们单独送到危险品回收口。\n危险品回收口的入口比较小，运送的时候需要慢慢调整位置和方向，确认对准以后再把物品送进去。\n如果你拖着危险品靠近熔炉，系统也会显示提醒，避免因为送错回收位置而发生事故。", "Hazardous items are paid as hazard-handling allowance, not at the price of ordinary metal, so they need to be taken separately to the hazard mouth.\nThe opening of the hazard mouth is fairly small, so when carrying an item you need to adjust its position and direction slowly, and send it in once it is lined up.\nIf you drag a hazardous item near the furnace, the system also shows a warning, to avoid an accident from sending it to the wrong recovery point."],
	"cx_s_field": ["牵引场", "TRACTOR FIELD"],
	"cx_s_field_a": ["船坞开放区域边缘安装了牵引力场，可以把漂出泊位的零件和设备逐渐拉回来，防止它们继续向外漂移。", "Tractor fields are fitted along the edges of the berth’s open areas. They gradually pull back parts and equipment that have drifted out of the bay, and stop them drifting further out."],
	"cx_s_field_b": ["牵引场只能改变零件的移动方向，无法直接让零件停下来。如果零件漂出去的时候速度太快，即使被牵引场拉了回来，也可能继续撞上船体或者附近的设备，造成损坏。", "The tractor field can only change a part’s direction of motion, and cannot stop the part directly. If a part drifts out too fast, even once it is pulled back by the field, it may still hit the hull or nearby equipment and cause damage."],
	"cx_s_field_c": ["拆除零件的最后一个固定点之前，最好先用抓钩固定住零件，避免零件失去控制。不要完全依赖牵引场，等零件漂出去以后再处理。", "Before removing a part’s last fixing point, it is best to secure the part with the grapple first, so it does not get out of control. Do not rely entirely on the tractor field and deal with the part only after it has drifted out."],
	"cx_s_field_x": ["船坞采用半开放式结构，底部设有作业平台，周围安装了塔架和悬臂，上方和右侧则保持开放，方便大型船体和拆解下来的设备进出。\n牵引场主要在船坞内部边框以外的区域发挥作用，零件漂出去的距离越远，受到的牵引力就越大，最终会被逐渐拉回泊位附近。\n如果后续扩建船坞，牵引场的作用范围也会跟着扩大，边界会移动到新建船坞的最外侧，确保扩建后的开放区域仍然受到牵引场保护。", "The berth has a half-open structure, with a work platform at the bottom, towers and booms around it, and the top and right sides left open so that large hulls and removed equipment can go in and out.\nThe tractor field mainly acts in the area outside the berth’s inner frame. The further out a part drifts, the stronger the pull on it, and in the end it is gradually pulled back to the bay.\nIf the berth is extended later, the field’s range grows with it, and the boundary moves to the outermost edge of the newly built berth, so the open area after the extension is still covered by the field."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext": ["船坞扩建", "BERTH EXTENSION"],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_a": ["购买船坞扩建项目以后，施工队会直接在现有泊位旁边进行建设，按照实际的在轨施工流程安装新的桁架、平台和其他设施。", "After you buy a berth extension, the construction crew builds right next to the existing bay, installing new trusses, platforms and other facilities in the way real in-orbit construction works."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_b": ["扩建施工期间，正在施工的区域会暂时封闭。如果有零件或者设备进入施工区域，周围的牵引场就会把它们推开，避免影响正在进行的安装工作。", "During the extension work, the area under construction is temporarily closed. If parts or equipment enter the work area, the tractor field around it pushes them away, so they do not interfere with the installation under way."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_c": ["你可以留在现场观看整个施工过程，也可以按任意键跳过，直接等到船坞扩建完成。", "You can stay on site to watch the whole construction, or press any key to skip it and wait until the berth extension is finished."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_x": ["船坞扩建会按照实际的在轨施工流程进行。施工开始前，系统会先隔离施工区域，然后由拖船把装有折叠桁架的货箱运送到指定位置。\n桁架通过铰接结构从储存筒内逐节展开，每节长度为 0.6 m。施工设备会在横向支撑杆展开并锁定以后，再继续安装下一节，直到整个桁架达到设计长度。\n安装模块的时候，会先用机械钩爪固定接口，再使用 M20、10.9 级高强度螺栓进行连接，每颗螺栓的预紧力为 125 kN。完成固定以后，施工设备还会使用电子束焊接技术处理连接处的焊缝。由于电子束焊接需要真空环境，而船坞本身就位于太空中，所以可以直接进行焊接。\n所有结构安装完成以后，还需要进行压力测试和承重测试。管路会使用氦气加压到正常工作压力的 1.5 倍，检查有没有泄漏，新安装的平台则需要承受设计载荷的 1.25 倍，测试时的最大挠度不能超过跨度的 1/800。\n通过这些测试以后，施工队才会进行最后的设备调试和验收，确认没有问题后，新的船坞区域就可以正式投入使用。\n如果扩建后的船坞需要停靠更高的船只，施工队还会增加塔架的高度，同时降低底部平台的位置，为大型船体留出足够的空间。", "A berth extension follows real in-orbit construction. The work area is isolated first, then a tug brings in the crates of folded truss.\nThe truss unfolds from its canister one hinged 0.6 m section at a time; each next section goes on only after the cross braces have opened and locked, until the truss reaches its design length.\nModules are held by mechanical claws, then joined with M20 grade 10.9 high-strength bolts at 125 kN preload each, and the seams are electron-beam welded. That welding needs vacuum, which space already provides.\nThe lines are then pressurised with helium to 1.5 times working pressure and leak-checked, and the new platform must carry 1.25 times its design load with no more than 1/800 of the span in deflection.\nAfter final commissioning and acceptance, the new berth area goes into use.\nFor a taller ship, the crew also raises the tower and lowers the bottom platform to make room for the hull."],
	"cx_s_blueprint": ["工程图", "THE DRAWING"],
	"cx_s_blueprint_a": ["工程图记录了船只原本的设计结构，包括舱室分布、管路走向、电路连接和各个设备的固定位置，拆解的时候可以用来查看船体内部的布置。", "The engineering drawing records the ship’s original design structure, including the room layout, line routes, circuit connections and the fixing position of each piece of equipment, and can be used to look at the layout inside the hull when dismantling."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_b": ["工程图记录的是船只最初的设计情况，但船只在使用过程中可能经历过改装、维修或者事故，所以图纸上的结构不一定和现在的船体完全一致。", "The engineering drawing records the ship’s original design, but the ship may have been refitted, repaired or in an accident during its service, so the structure on the drawing may not match the current hull exactly."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_c": ["拆解之前可以先查看工程图，确认设备的位置和管线的连接方式。不过实际操作的时候，还是要通过现场检查来确认设备当前的状态，不能完全按照图纸判断。", "Before dismantling you can look at the engineering drawing first to confirm the positions of equipment and how lines are connected. In actual work, though, you still need to check the equipment’s current state on site, and cannot judge entirely by the drawing."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_x": ["按下 Tab 键就可以打开工程图，查看船体内部的结构，包括盖板后面安装了哪些设备、阀门连接着哪条管线，以及各个设备从哪里获得电力。\n不过工程图通常不会记录船只后来发生的变化。如果船只曾经进行过改装或者维修，内部就可能出现额外安装的电源、已经堵塞的接口，或者重新修补过的管路。\n这些变化都需要在拆解现场进行检查，尤其是涉及电路和压力管线的时候，最好先测量实际状态，再决定怎么拆除。", "Press the Tab key to open the engineering drawing and see the structure inside the hull, including what equipment sits behind the covers, which line a valve is connected to, and where each piece of equipment gets its power.\nHowever, the engineering drawing usually does not record later changes to the ship. If the ship was refitted or repaired, there may be an extra power supply, a blocked port or a repaired line inside.\nThese changes all have to be checked on site during dismantling. Especially where circuits and pressure lines are involved, it is best to measure the actual state first, and then decide how to remove it."],
	"cx_s_scope": ["分段与抢救合同", "PART-SHIP CONTRACTS"],
	"cx_s_scope_a": ["这类合同只要求你拆除船体的指定区域，或者回收几件指定的设备，不需要把整艘船全部拆完。", "This kind of contract asks you to dismantle only a specified area of the hull, or to recover a few named pieces of equipment, and you do not need to dismantle the whole ship."],
	"cx_s_scope_b": ["合同只允许你处理指定范围内的零件，如果拆除了范围以外的结构，或者在操作过程中造成损坏，都会被视为违反合同，需要从报酬中扣除相应的费用。", "The contract allows you to handle only the parts inside the specified scope. If you remove structures outside the scope, or cause damage during the work, it counts as a breach of contract and the matching cost is deducted from your payment."],
	"cx_s_scope_c": ["开始拆解之前，先查看界面上标记的合同范围，确认哪些区域和设备可以处理。范围以外的部分尽量不要碰，避免因为误拆或者损坏而被扣钱。", "Before dismantling, check the contract scope marked on the screen to confirm which areas and equipment you may handle. Try not to touch anything outside the scope, so you are not charged for wrongly removing or damaging it."],
	"cx_s_scope_x": ["分段拆解合同只会收购指定区段内的零件，船体里面剩余的气体和液体不属于收购范围，所以即使把它们回收下来，也不会计入合同收入。\n抢救合同则按照指定设备支付固定报酬，只要把合同要求的设备全部送进回收口，就可以直接完成任务，剩下的船体会由拖船负责运走，不需要继续拆解。\n拆解时可以通过光标确认零件是否属于合同范围，如果光标指向的零件显示「范围外」，就说明合同没有授权拆除这个零件，最好保留原样。", "A section dismantling contract buys only the parts inside the specified section. The gas and liquid left in the hull are not within the purchase scope, so even if you recover them, they are not counted into the contract income.\nA salvage contract pays a fixed fee for the named equipment. As soon as all the equipment the contract asks for has been sent into the recovery mouth, the task is complete, and the rest of the hull is towed away by a tug, so you need not dismantle any further.\nWhen dismantling, you can use the cursor to check whether a part is within the contract scope. If the part under the cursor shows ‘out of scope’, the contract does not authorise removing this part, and it is best left as it is."],
	"cx_s_hauler": ["搬运无人机", "HAULING DRONE"],
	"cx_s_hauler_a": ["船坞悬臂上安装的辅助搬运设备，可以自动把你标记好的零件运送到对应的回收口，省去手动搬运的过程。", "A helper handling machine fitted on the berth boom. It automatically carries the parts you have marked to the matching recovery mouth, saving you the manual carrying."],
	"cx_s_hauler_b": ["搬运无人机只会按照你的标记执行任务，不会主动检查零件是否安全。即使零件内部还有残留液体，或者设备尚未断电，无人机也会直接进行搬运，可能在运输过程中发生事故。", "The hauling drone only carries out your marks and does not check on its own whether a part is safe. Even if the part still holds leftover liquid, or the equipment has not been de-energised, the drone moves it anyway, and an accident may happen in transit."],
	"cx_s_hauler_c": ["标记零件之前，先检查并处理好内部的电力和液体等危险，确认零件已经可以安全回收以后，再点击鼠标右键进行标记，让无人机负责搬运。", "Before marking a part, check and deal with dangers inside such as power and liquid, and mark the part with a right click only after confirming it is safe to recover, to let the drone carry it."],
	"cx_s_hauler_x": ["搬运无人机会按照你标记零件的先后顺序安排运输任务，并自动规划搬运路线，选择对应的回收口。\n有了无人机以后，你就不用每次都亲自把零件拖到回收口了，不过无人机不会替你判断零件是否已经处理安全，也不会检查零件应该如何分类回收。\n所以在标记之前，你仍然需要确认零件已经完成断电、排液等必要处理，并检查回收目标是否正确，之后再交给无人机搬运。", "The hauling drone arranges its transport jobs in the order you marked the parts, plans its own carrying routes automatically, and chooses the matching recovery mouth.\nWith the drone, you no longer have to drag every part to a recovery mouth yourself. However, the drone does not judge for you whether a part has been made safe, and does not check how a part should be sorted for recovery.\nSo before marking, you still need to confirm that the part has had the necessary handling such as power-off and draining, and check that the recovery target is right, and only then hand it to the drone to carry."],
	"cx_s_impact": ["撞击", "IMPACT"],
	"cx_s_impact_a": ["在失重环境中，漂浮的零件、无人机或者整段船体，都有可能在移动过程中撞上附近的设备或其他船体结构。", "In weightlessness, floating parts, the drone or a whole section of hull may hit nearby equipment or other hull structure as they move."],
	"cx_s_impact_b": ["发生撞击以后，游戏会根据碰撞时的速度变化和零件的易损程度，降低双方的完好度。精密设备比较容易受到损坏，即使碰撞速度不快，也可能造成很大的损失。", "After an impact, the game lowers the condition of both sides according to the change in speed at the collision and how easily each part is damaged. Precision equipment is easily damaged, and even a slow collision can cause great loss."],
	"cx_s_impact_c": ["使用抓钩拖运零件的时候，尽量控制移动速度，接近目标位置之前就提前减速。尤其是搬运大型设备时，要避免零件脱离控制后继续漂移。", "When towing parts with the grapple, keep your speed under control and start slowing down before you reach the target position. Especially when carrying large equipment, do not let a part get out of control and keep drifting."],
	"cx_s_impact_x": ["撞击造成的损坏主要取决于碰撞前后的速度变化（Δv），以及零件本身的易损程度。\n同样是以 1 m/s 的速度发生碰撞，普通钢结构通常不会受到太大影响，但光学玻璃、芯片等精密设备就可能出现严重损坏，甚至直接失去回收价值。\n拖运重型设备的时候，还要注意它们的惯性。设备的质量越大，想要让它停下来就越困难。如果发现自己来不及减速，直接松开抓钩只会让情况更加危险，因为设备还会保持原来的动量继续移动，直到受到其他外力影响。\n所以搬运大型零件时，最好提前减速，并且一直保持抓钩连接，直到设备安全进入回收区域。", "The damage an impact causes mainly depends on the change in speed (Δv) before and after the collision, and on how easily the part is damaged.\nIn a collision at the same 1 m/s, ordinary steel structure is usually not much affected, but precision equipment such as optical glass and chips may be seriously damaged, and may even lose all recovery value.\nWhen towing heavy equipment, also watch its inertia. The greater the mass of the equipment, the harder it is to stop. If you find you cannot slow down in time, simply releasing the grapple only makes things more dangerous, because the equipment keeps its original momentum and carries on moving until some other force acts on it.\nSo when carrying large parts, it is best to slow down early and keep the grapple attached until the equipment is safely inside the recovery area."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: power
	"cx_swb": ["配电盘", "SWITCHBOARD"],
	"cx_swb_a": ["配电盘负责把船上的电力分配到不同设备和线路，内部装有母排、仪表和一排断路器，可以分别控制各条线路的供电。", "A switchboard distributes the ship’s power to different equipment and lines. Inside it are busbars, meters and a row of circuit breakers, which control the supply to each line separately."],
	"cx_swb_b": ["配电盘连接着船上的多条供电线路，只要还有一路电源没有切断，内部就可能仍然带电。即使已经关闭了所有断路器，也不能直接拆除配电盘。", "A switchboard is connected to many of the ship’s supply lines, and as long as one supply is not cut, the inside may still be live. Even after all the circuit breakers are switched off, the switchboard cannot be removed directly."],
	"cx_swb_c": ["拆除配电盘之前，先切断船上所有的电源，再通过配电盘上的验电点检查电压。确认读数已经降到 0 V 以后，才能开始拆解。", "Before removing a switchboard, cut all the ship’s supplies first, then check the voltage at the switchboard’s test point. Start dismantling only after the reading has dropped to 0 V."],
	"cx_swb_x": ["配电盘的上半部分是三相母排室，负责连接和分配电力。下半部分分成多个区域，每个区域都安装了仪表板和断路器，供电电缆则通过底部的电缆密封板接入。\n需要注意的是，断路器通常只能切断通往设备的负载侧线路。如果母排上游还有任何一路电源没有关闭，配电盘内部就仍然可能带电，所以不能只看断路器是否关闭，还要检查所有电源有没有彻底断开。\n带电拆解配电盘非常危险，如果工具导致母排之间发生短路，就可能产生温度高达上万摄氏度的电弧，严重损坏周围设备。\n拆解之前一定要完成断电和验电，确认电压为 0 V 以后再动手。", "The upper half of a switchboard is the three-phase busbar chamber, which connects and distributes power. The lower half is divided into several sections, each fitted with a meter panel and circuit breakers, and the supply cables come in through the cable gland plate at the bottom.\nNote that a circuit breaker can usually cut only the load-side line to the equipment. If any supply upstream of the busbar has not been switched off, the inside of the switchboard may still be live, so do not go by whether the breakers are off alone, but also check that all supplies are completely disconnected.\nDismantling a switchboard while live is very dangerous. If a tool shorts the busbars together, it may produce an arc at temperatures of over ten thousand degrees Celsius, seriously damaging the surrounding equipment.\nAlways complete the power-off and the voltage test before dismantling, and start work only after confirming the voltage is 0 V."],
	"cx_battery": ["电池组", "BATTERY PACK"],
	"cx_battery_a": ["船上的电池组由多个串联的电芯模块组成，内部还安装了汇流排、冷却板和电池管理板，主要负责储存电能，并在需要的时候为船上设备供电。", "The ship’s battery pack is made of several cell modules in series, and inside it also has busbars, cooling plates and a battery management board. It mainly stores electrical energy and supplies the ship’s equipment when needed."],
	"cx_battery_b": ["电池组即使已经关闭了外部电源，内部仍然储存着大量电能。切断电源只能让电池停止向外供电，无法消除电芯内部的能量，如果直接切割或者拆开电池组，就可能引发短路甚至起火。", "Even with the external supply switched off, a battery pack still stores a great deal of energy inside. Cutting the connection only stops the battery supplying power outward and cannot remove the energy inside the cells, and cutting or opening the pack directly may cause a short circuit or even a fire."],
	"cx_battery_c": ["拆除电池组之前，先关闭对应的隔离开关，再拔掉连接到船体的输出电缆。确认电池组已经与船体电路断开以后，将整组电池完整拆下来，送进危险品回收口处理。", "Before removing a battery pack, switch off its isolator first, then unplug the output cable connected to the hull. Once the pack is confirmed disconnected from the ship’s circuits, take the whole pack off intact and send it to the hazard mouth for handling."],
	"cx_battery_x": ["一组容量为 50 kWh 的锂电池，在充满电以后可以储存约 180 MJ 的能量，即使已经切断了外部电源，这些能量也仍然保存在电芯内部。\n如果拆解时刺穿电芯，或者让内部电路发生短路，就可能引发热失控。在严重的情况下，电芯温度可能在几秒内升高到 600°C 以上，同时释放大量可燃气体，甚至引燃附近的其他电芯。\n电池组的主接触器一般安装在模块的一端，断开以后可以停止向外部设备供电，但电池内部的正负极之间仍然存在电压。\n所以拆解电池组的时候，一定要先断开隔离开关和输出电缆，之后再将整个电池组送去回收，不要直接切割内部结构。", "A lithium battery pack with a capacity of 50 kWh can store about 180 MJ of energy when fully charged, and even after the external supply is cut, this energy is still kept inside the cells.\nIf a cell is punctured during dismantling, or the internal circuit is shorted, thermal runaway may result. In serious cases the cell temperature can rise above 600°C within seconds, releasing a lot of flammable gas and even igniting other cells nearby.\nThe pack’s main contactor is usually fitted at one end of the module. Once opened, it stops supplying power to external equipment, but there is still voltage between the pack’s own positive and negative terminals.\nSo when dismantling a battery pack, always disconnect the isolator and the output cable first, and then send the whole pack for recovery, and do not cut the internal structure directly."],
	"cx_cap": ["电容组", "CAPACITOR BANK"],
	"cx_cap_a": ["电容组由多个电容罐、汇流排和放电电阻组成，主要用来储存电能，在发射系统等设备需要大量电力的时候，可以在短时间内释放储存的能量。", "A capacitor bank is made of several capacitor cans, busbars and a discharge resistor. It mainly stores electrical energy, and can release the stored energy in a short time when equipment such as launch systems needs a lot of power."],
	"cx_cap_b": ["即使已经切断了船体电源，电容组内部也可能保留着很高的电压。如果没有提前放电就直接拆解，工具接触到带电部位时可能产生电弧，造成严重损坏。", "Even after the ship’s power is cut, a capacitor bank may keep a very high voltage inside. If you dismantle it without discharging first, a tool touching a live part may produce an arc and cause serious damage."],
	"cx_cap_c": ["拆除电容组之前，先找到对应的放电接口，使用放电装置把剩余电压降到 0 V，再通过验电点确认没有残余电压。完成放电和验电以后，才能开始拆解。", "Before removing a capacitor bank, find its discharge port, use the discharge device to bring the remaining voltage down to 0 V, and then confirm at the test point that no residual voltage is left. Start dismantling only after discharging and testing are done."],
	"cx_cap_x": ["电容组储存的能量可以通过 E = ½CV² 计算，其中 C 是电容，V 是电压。一组电容为 0.1 F、电压为 400 V 的设备，就可以储存 8 kJ 的能量，而大型发射系统使用的电容组，储存的能量甚至可以达到兆焦级别。\n电容组和普通用电设备有所不同，关闭电源以后，已经储存的电能不会立即消失，必须通过放电才能降低内部电压。\n放电电阻可以让电容组逐渐释放电能，并将这些能量转化成热量。放电速度取决于电阻和电容形成的 RC 时间常数，通常经过大约五个时间常数以后，剩余电压就会降到初始值的 1% 以下。\n所以即使船上的电源已经全部关闭，也要单独检查电容组的电压，确认完成放电以后再进行拆解。", "The energy a capacitor bank stores can be calculated with E = ½CV², where C is the capacitance and V is the voltage. A unit of 0.1 F at 400 V can store 8 kJ of energy, and the capacitor banks used by large launch systems can store energy even on the megajoule scale.\nA capacitor bank differs from ordinary electrical equipment: after the power is switched off, the energy already stored does not vanish at once, and it has to be discharged to bring the internal voltage down.\nA discharge resistor lets the capacitor bank release its energy gradually and turns that energy into heat. The discharge speed depends on the RC time constant formed by the resistor and the capacitor, and usually after about five time constants the remaining voltage drops below 1% of its initial value.\nSo even when all the ship’s power is off, check the capacitor bank’s voltage separately, and dismantle it only after confirming the discharge is complete."],
	"cx_gen": ["发电机组", "GENERATING SET"],
	"cx_gen_a": ["发电机组通过发动机带动发电机运转，为船上的设备提供电力。整套机组还安装了散热器、励磁机和控制屏，用来维持发电机的正常运行。", "A generator set uses an engine to drive a generator and supplies power to the ship’s equipment. The whole set also has a radiator, an exciter and a control panel, which keep the generator running properly."],
	"cx_gen_b": ["发电机停止运行以后，出线端仍然可能带电。如果船上的其他电源还连接着供电总线，电流就可能通过总线反向进入发电机的线路，所以不能只看发动机有没有停止运行。", "After a generator stops running, its output terminals may still be live. If other supplies on the ship are still connected to the supply bus, current may flow back through the bus into the generator’s lines, so do not go only by whether the engine has stopped."],
	"cx_gen_c": ["拆除发电机组之前，先确认发动机已经完全停止运行，再断开连接供电总线的输出线路。完成断电以后，还需要检查出线端的电压，确认没有残余电压后再进行拆解。", "Before removing a generator set, first confirm the engine has stopped completely, then disconnect the output line to the supply bus. After the power is cut, also check the voltage at the output terminals, and dismantle only after confirming no residual voltage."],
	"cx_gen_x": ["发电机内部的转子装有凸极磁极，定子槽内则安装了用于发电的绕组。发动机带动转子旋转以后，发电机就可以产生电力。\n即使已经关闭了励磁系统，转子内部仍然可能保留一定的剩余磁性。如果转子继续旋转，发电机就可能产生几十伏的电压，所以停机以后还要等待转子完全停止，并检查线路是否带电。\n一套发电机组通常重达 1–3 吨，底座上还安装了减振器，用来减少运行时产生的振动。固定螺栓一般集中在机组底座上，拆解时需要先找到这些连接位置。\n由于整套设备的重量比较大，拆除底座螺栓之前，最好先用抓钩固定住机组，避免最后一个固定点松开以后，发电机组失去控制并撞上附近的设备。", "Inside the generator, the rotor carries salient magnetic poles, and the stator slots hold the windings used to generate power. Once the engine drives the rotor round, the generator can produce electricity.\nEven with the excitation system switched off, the rotor may keep some residual magnetism. If the rotor keeps turning, the generator may produce tens of volts, so after shutdown you also need to wait until the rotor has stopped completely and check whether the lines are live.\nA generator set usually weighs 1–3 t, and the base also carries anti-vibration mounts to reduce vibration while running. The fixing bolts are generally concentrated on the base of the set, and you need to find these connection points first when dismantling.\nBecause the whole unit is heavy, before removing the base bolts it is best to secure the set with the grapple first, so that once the last fixing point is loose, the generator set does not get out of control and hit nearby equipment."],
	"cx_panel": ["控制箱", "CONTROL ENCLOSURE"],
	"cx_panel_a": ["安装在墙上的电气控制箱，外面有箱门和指示灯观察窗，里面装着端子排，电缆通过格兰头接入箱体。", "An electrical control box mounted on a wall. It has a door and an indicator viewing window on the outside, terminal blocks inside, and cables enter the box through glands."],
	"cx_panel_b": ["控制箱虽然不大，但可能连接了好几路电源。就算断开了其中一路，其他线路也可能还带着电。", "A control box is not large, but it may be connected to several supplies. Even if one of them is disconnected, other lines may still be live."],
	"cx_panel_c": ["先对照工程图，找到所有接入控制箱的电源线路，把每一路电源都断开并确认没有电压以后，再开始拆除控制箱。", "First check the engineering drawing to find all the supply lines coming into the control box, disconnect every supply and confirm there is no voltage, and then start removing the control box."],
	"cx_panel_x": ["控制箱里面一般装着继电器、PLC 和端子排，这些设备本身的回收价值不算高，但连接的线路比较多。最好在拆除控制箱之前就把所有进线处理好，这样拆下来以后也不用再花时间逐一查找线路。", "A control box generally holds relays, a PLC and terminal blocks. The recovery value of this equipment is not high, but it has many connected lines. It is best to deal with all the incoming lines before removing the control box, so that you need not spend time looking for the lines one by one after it is removed."],
	"cx_junction": ["接线盒", "JUNCTION BOX"],
	"cx_junction_a": ["接线盒一般装在电缆连接的位置，盒盖四角有固定螺钉，内部有接地螺柱，电缆通过格兰头接入和引出。", "A junction box is usually fitted where cables connect. The lid has fixing screws at the four corners, there is an earth stud inside, and cables enter and leave through glands."],
	"cx_junction_b": ["多条电缆会在这里连接和分支，接线盒上通常还设有验电点或放电点。拆除之前要确认所有相关线路都已经断电。", "Several cables connect and branch here, and the junction box usually also has a test point or discharge point. Before removal, confirm that all the related lines are de-energised."],
	"cx_junction_c": ["先找到接线盒对应的验电点和放电点，按照操作要求完成验电和放电，确认安全以后，再处理与它连接的设备。", "First find the test point and discharge point for the junction box, complete the voltage test and discharge as required, and after confirming it is safe, deal with the equipment connected to it."],
	"cx_junction_x": ["接线盒主要用来连接和分配电缆线路，一台设备的电源可能要经过好几个接线盒才能接到供电端。如果不清楚设备的电源从哪里接入，可以先找到对应的接线盒，再沿着电缆逐段往回查找，这样通常更容易找到供电线路。", "A junction box is mainly used to connect and distribute cable lines, and the supply of one piece of equipment may pass through several junction boxes before it reaches the supply end. If you do not know where a piece of equipment’s power comes in, first find the matching junction box and trace back along the cable section by section, which usually makes it easier to find the supply line."],
	"cx_transformer": ["变压器", "TRANSFORMER"],
	"cx_transformer_a": ["这是一台干式变压器，主要由三柱铁芯、高低压绕组和外部的夹紧框架组成，铁芯和绕组都固定在框架里面。", "This is a dry-type transformer. It mainly consists of a three-limb core, high- and low-voltage windings and an outer clamping frame, and the core and windings are fixed inside the frame."],
	"cx_transformer_b": ["变压器的高低压两侧都可能带电，即使高压侧已经断开，如果低压侧还有电源接入，变压器仍然可能把低压升成高压，所以不能只断开其中一侧。", "Both the high-voltage and low-voltage sides of a transformer may be live. Even if the high-voltage side is disconnected, if a supply is still connected on the low-voltage side, the transformer may step the low voltage up to high voltage, so you cannot disconnect only one side."],
	"cx_transformer_c": ["拆除之前，要把高压侧和低压侧的电源全部断开，分别验电并确认没有电压，完成必要的隔离和放电以后，再开始拆除。", "Before removal, disconnect all the supplies on both the high-voltage and low-voltage sides, test each for voltage and confirm there is none, and start removal after the necessary isolation and discharge are done."],
	"cx_transformer_x": ["变压器通过高低压绕组的匝数比例来改变电压。拿匝数比为 10:1 的变压器来说，如果从低压侧接入 400 V，高压侧就可能产生约 4 kV 的电压。\n干式变压器通常比较重，其中铁芯占了很大一部分重量。拆除的时候可以根据夹紧框架的结构，把铁芯和其他部件分开处理，方便后续搬运。", "A transformer changes voltage through the turns ratio of its high- and low-voltage windings. Take a transformer with a turns ratio of 10:1: if 400 V is fed in from the low-voltage side, the high-voltage side may produce about 4 kV.\nA dry-type transformer is usually heavy, and the core makes up a large part of the weight. When removing it, you can use the structure of the clamping frame to separate the core from the other parts, which makes later carrying easier."],
	"cx_inverter": ["逆变器", "INVERTER"],
	"cx_inverter_a": ["逆变器内部主要装着 IGBT 功率模块、散热器、直流母线电容和输出电抗器，这些部件共同负责把直流电转换成电机需要的交流电。", "An inverter mainly contains IGBT power modules, a heat sink, DC-link capacitors and an output choke. Together these parts convert DC into the AC that a motor needs."],
	"cx_inverter_b": ["逆变器断开电源以后，内部的直流母线电容可能还存有高压电，需要经过几分钟才能逐渐放电。即使设备已经停止运行，也不能直接拆除。", "After an inverter is disconnected from the power, the DC-link capacitors inside may still hold high voltage, and take a few minutes to discharge gradually. Even if the equipment has stopped running, it must not be removed directly."],
	"cx_inverter_c": ["先断开逆变器的所有输入电源，等待电容完成放电，必要时通过指定的放电点进行放电。确认直流母线没有残余电压以后，再开始拆除设备。", "First disconnect all the inverter’s input supplies and wait for the capacitors to discharge, and if needed discharge them through the designated discharge point. Start removing the equipment only after confirming the DC bus has no residual voltage."],
	"cx_inverter_x": ["逆变器通过 IGBT 模块的快速开关，把直流电转换成交流电，用来控制电机运行。内部的直流母线电容负责储存电能，让供电电压保持稳定。\n这类设备的直流母线电压经常达到 600–800 V，即使已经断开电源，电容里也可能残留危险电压。设备通常装有泄放电阻，但一般需要等待几分钟才能完成放电，具体时间要看设备型号，拆除前仍然需要实际测量确认。", "An inverter converts DC into AC by fast switching of its IGBT modules, and uses it to control motor running. The DC-link capacitors inside store the electrical energy and keep the supply voltage steady.\nThe DC bus voltage of this kind of equipment often reaches 600–800 V, and even after the supply is disconnected, a dangerous voltage may remain in the capacitors. The equipment usually has bleed resistors, but it generally takes a few minutes to finish discharging, and the exact time depends on the model, so you still need to measure and confirm before removal."],
	"cx_fuelcell": ["燃料电池", "FUEL CELL STACK"],
	"cx_fuelcell_a": ["燃料电池内部有上百片双极板，整组电池由两端的端板和拉杆固定在一起，旁边还配有鼓风机和加湿器，用来维持电池运行时需要的空气供应和湿度。", "Inside a fuel cell there are hundreds of bipolar plates. The whole stack is held together by end plates and tie rods at the two ends, and beside it are a blower and a humidifier that keep up the air supply and humidity the cell needs while running."],
	"cx_fuelcell_b": ["只要内部还有氢气和氧气，燃料电池就可能继续发电。即使已经断开了主电源线路，电池本身也可能带电，里面残留的氢气还有泄漏和起火的危险。", "As long as hydrogen and oxygen remain inside, a fuel cell can keep generating power. Even after the main supply line is disconnected, the cell itself may be live, and the hydrogen left inside can leak and catch fire."],
	"cx_fuelcell_c": ["拆除之前，先断开燃料电池自己的电源开关，关闭燃料供应阀门，再按照设备要求排出内部残留的氢气。确认燃料供应已经隔离、内部没有危险的氢气残留，并完成验电以后，才能开始拆除。", "Before removal, switch off the fuel cell at its own power switch, shut the fuel supply valve, then vent the hydrogen left inside as the equipment requires. Start removal only after confirming the fuel supply is isolated, no dangerous hydrogen remains inside, and the voltage test is done."],
	"cx_fuelcell_x": ["燃料电池通过氢气和氧气发生电化学反应来产生电能，每片电池工作时的电压大约是 0.7 V，几百片串联起来以后，总电压就可能达到几百伏。\n即使关闭了燃料阀门，电池内部仍然可能残留氢气。如果氢气泄漏到舱室里面，浓度达到空气体积的 4% 到 75% 时就可能燃烧，而且只需要很小的点火能量就能引燃，所以拆除之前一定要确认氢气已经安全排出。", "A fuel cell produces electricity through an electrochemical reaction between hydrogen and oxygen. Each cell works at about 0.7 V, and with several hundred in series the total voltage can reach several hundred volts.\nEven with the fuel valve closed, hydrogen may remain inside the cell. If hydrogen leaks into a room and its concentration reaches 4% to 75% of the air by volume, it can burn, and a very small ignition energy is enough to light it, so always confirm the hydrogen has been safely vented before removal."],
	"cx_charger": ["充电桩", "CHARGING STATION"],
	"cx_charger_a": ["充电桩主要用来给无人机或车辆充电，通常配有充电枪头和连接线缆，可以将外部电源接入需要充电的设备。", "A charging unit is mainly used to charge drones or vehicles. It usually comes with a charging connector and cable, and can feed an external supply into the equipment to be charged."],
	"cx_charger_b": ["充电桩连接着充电设备时，充电线缆的两端都可能带电。即使已经断开充电桩的电源，被充电设备内部的电池也可能还有电压。", "While a charging unit is connected to equipment being charged, both ends of the charging cable may be live. Even after the charging unit’s supply is disconnected, the battery inside the equipment being charged may still have voltage."],
	"cx_charger_c": ["先关闭充电开关，断开充电桩的供电并确认已经停止充电，再按照要求拔下充电线缆。确认连接已经断开以后，才能继续处理被充电的设备。", "First switch off the charging switch, disconnect the charging unit’s supply and confirm charging has stopped, then unplug the charging cable as required. Carry on with the equipment that was being charged only after confirming the connection is cut."],
	"cx_charger_x": ["充电桩从供电总线获取电能，再通过充电线缆把电能输送给连接的设备。如果设备内部装有电池，即使充电桩已经断电，电池本身仍然储存着电能，所以拔掉充电线缆以后，设备的电池一侧也可能继续带电，拆除时需要单独检查。", "A charging unit takes power from the supply bus and sends it to the connected equipment through the charging cable. If the equipment has a battery inside, that battery still stores energy even after the charging unit loses power, so after the charging cable is unplugged, the battery side of the equipment may remain live, and it needs to be checked separately during removal."],
	"cx_dump_res": ["泄能电阻", "DUMP RESISTOR"],
	"cx_dump_res_a": ["泄能电阻由一排排反复折叠的不锈钢电阻带组成，连接在超导磁体的泄能回路上，主要用来消耗磁体储存的能量。", "A dump resistor is made of rows of stainless steel resistor ribbon folded back and forth. It is connected to the dump circuit of a superconducting magnet and mainly consumes the energy the magnet has stored."],
	"cx_dump_res_b": ["磁体泄能时，大量电能会通过电阻转化成热量，满负荷运行时，电阻带甚至会被加热到发红。如果提前拆除泄能电阻，磁体就会失去正常的泄能通道，可能造成严重事故。", "When a magnet dumps its energy, a great deal of electrical energy is turned into heat in the resistor, and at full load the resistor ribbon can even be heated until it glows red. If the dump resistor is removed too early, the magnet loses its normal dump path, which may cause a serious accident."],
	"cx_dump_res_c": ["先确认磁体已经完成泄能，等回路电流降到安全范围，并按照要求完成隔离、验电和放电以后，才能拆除泄能电阻及其连接的母排。", "First confirm the magnet has finished dumping its energy and the circuit current has dropped to a safe range, and complete the isolation, voltage test and discharge as required, and only then remove the dump resistor and the busbars connected to it."],
	"cx_dump_res_x": ["磁体泄能时，线圈中的电流会经过泄能电阻逐渐减小，计算公式为 I = I₀·e^(−t/τ)，其中 τ = L/R。电阻越大，电流下降得越快，但泄能时产生的电压也会更高，可以用 U = I·R 计算。在大型超导磁体中，几十吉焦的储能可能在几十秒内转化成热量，电阻带的温度也可能升高到几百度。", "When a magnet dumps its energy, the current in the coil gradually falls through the dump resistor, calculated as I = I₀·e^(−t/τ), where τ = L/R. The larger the resistance, the faster the current falls, but the voltage produced during the dump is also higher, and can be calculated as U = I·R. In a large superconducting magnet, tens of gigajoules of stored energy may be turned into heat within tens of seconds, and the temperature of the resistor ribbon may also rise to several hundred degrees."],
	"cx_slip_ring": ["滑环", "SLIP RING"],
	"cx_slip_ring_a": ["滑环由安装在旋转部分的一组铜环和固定部分的电刷组成，主要用来给不断旋转的居住环供电，让居住环在转动的时候也能正常使用电力。", "A slip ring is made of a set of copper rings on the rotating part and brushes on the fixed part. It mainly supplies power to a habitat ring that keeps rotating, so the habitat ring can use electricity normally while it turns."],
	"cx_slip_ring_b": ["如果居住环还在通电，就直接启动刹车，电机在减速时产生的回馈电流可能会经过滑环。电流过大时，滑环内部可能出现电弧，严重时还会烧坏铜环和电刷。", "If you start the brake while the habitat ring is still powered, the regenerated current the motor produces while slowing down may pass through the slip ring. If the current is too large, an arc may form inside the slip ring, and in serious cases it burns out the copper rings and brushes."],
	"cx_slip_ring_c": ["先断开居住环上的用电负载，确认相关电路已经安全隔离以后，再启动制动系统，让居住环逐渐停止旋转。", "First disconnect the electrical loads on the habitat ring, and after confirming the related circuits are safely isolated, start the braking system and let the habitat ring gradually stop rotating."],
	"cx_slip_ring_x": ["滑环依靠电刷与铜环之间的接触来传输电流，即使居住环一直旋转，也能保持电力连接。不过电刷能够承受的电流密度有限，如果回馈电流过大，接触位置就可能产生电弧，在铜环表面留下烧蚀和凹坑。滑环还是这座旋转居住环唯一的供电通路，一旦损坏，整个居住环就可能失去电力供应。", "A slip ring carries current through contact between the brushes and the copper rings, so the electrical connection holds even while the habitat ring keeps rotating. However, the current density the brushes can bear is limited, and if the regenerated current is too large, an arc may form at the contact point and leave burn marks and pits on the copper ring surface. The slip ring is also the only supply path for this rotating habitat ring, and if it is damaged, the whole habitat ring may lose its power supply."],
	"cx_tray": ["电缆桥架", "CABLE TRAY"],
	"cx_tray_a": ["安装在顶板下方的梯式电缆桥架，里面铺设着成捆的电缆，附近通常还安装着照明灯具和消防喷头。", "A ladder-type cable tray mounted under the deckhead, with bundles of cable laid in it, and lamps and fire sprinklers usually fitted nearby."],
	"cx_tray_b": ["桥架里面可能有多条不同的供电线路，只要其中还有一根电缆带电，就不能直接切割整捆电缆，否则可能造成短路或触电事故。", "A tray may hold several different supply lines, and as long as one cable in it is still live, you cannot cut the whole bundle directly, or it may cause a short circuit or an electric shock."],
	"cx_tray_c": ["先找到桥架内所有电缆对应的电路，逐一断开电源并确认没有电压以后，再拆除电缆和桥架。", "First find the circuits that all the cables in the tray belong to, disconnect each supply and confirm there is no voltage, and then remove the cables and the tray."],
	"cx_tray_x": ["电缆桥架本身只是用来固定和支撑电缆的金属结构，真正需要注意的是里面的线路。动力电缆、信号电缆和控制电缆可能铺设在同一座桥架里，所以拆除之前要按照工程图逐一确认每条线路的连接情况，完成必要的断电和安全检查以后，再进行拆除。", "The cable tray itself is only a metal structure that holds and supports the cables, and what really needs care is the lines inside. Power cables, signal cables and control cables may be laid in the same tray, so before removal, check the connections of every line against the engineering drawing, and remove them after the necessary power-off and safety checks."],
	"cx_module": ["可更换单元（ORU）", "ORBITAL REPLACEMENT UNIT"],
	"cx_module_a": ["可更换单元是一种可以整体拆卸和更换的密封设备箱，外面装有两个方便抓握的把手，通过自锁螺钉固定在安装位置上，背面还有可以直接插拔的连接接头。", "A replaceable unit is a sealed equipment box that can be removed and replaced as a whole. It has two easy-to-grip handles on the outside, is held in place by captive screws, and has plug-in connectors on the back that can be pulled out directly."],
	"cx_module_b": ["设备背面的接头直接连接着安装背板，如果还没有解除固定就强行拔出，可能会损坏背板上的接头，影响后续设备的安装和使用。", "The connectors on the back of the equipment connect straight into the mounting backplane. If you pull it out by force before releasing it, you may damage the connectors on the backplane, affecting later installation and use of equipment."],
	"cx_module_c": ["先断开设备电源，确认安全以后，再松开固定设备的自锁螺钉，握住把手将整个单元拔出来，尽量保持设备和接头的完整。", "First disconnect the equipment’s power, and once it is safe, loosen the captive screws that hold the equipment, grip the handles and pull the whole unit out, keeping the equipment and its connectors intact as far as possible."],
	"cx_module_x": ["ORU采用的是航天器上常见的整体更换设计，宇航员即使戴着厚重的手套，也能通过把手和自锁螺钉完成拆装，部分设备还可以直接由机械臂操作。由于不需要拆开内部零件，整个单元就能取下来，所以这类设备通常比较容易拆卸，只要没有损坏，完整回收的价值也比较高。", "The ORU uses the whole-unit replacement design common on spacecraft. Even an astronaut in thick gloves can fit and remove it with the handles and captive screws, and some units can also be handled directly by a mechanical arm. Because the internal parts need not be taken apart, the whole unit can be lifted out, so this kind of equipment is usually fairly easy to remove, and if it is undamaged, its value when recovered whole is also fairly high."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: fluids, gases, heat
	"cx_pump": ["离心泵组", "CENTRIFUGAL PUMP SET"],
	"cx_pump_a": ["离心泵组一般由泵壳、轴承架、联轴器和电机组成，这些部件都安装在同一个底座上。泵壳通常采用蜗壳结构，用来输送管道里的液体。", "A centrifugal pump set generally consists of a pump casing, a bearing frame, a coupling and a motor, all mounted on the same baseplate. The pump casing is usually a volute, used to move the liquid in the line."],
	"cx_pump_b": ["泵组虽然已经停止运行，但进出口管道里可能还存有液体，电机也可能没有断电。直接切断管道会造成液体泄漏，带电拆除电线还可能产生电弧。", "Although the pump set has stopped running, the inlet and outlet lines may still hold liquid, and the motor may not be de-energised. Cutting a line directly causes a liquid leak, and removing the wires while live may also produce an arc."],
	"cx_pump_c": ["先切断电机电源，再通过排放口把泵组和连接管道里的液体排空，确认没有残余压力以后，断开电缆和进出口管道，最后把整套泵组从底座上拆下来。", "First cut the motor’s power, then drain the liquid in the pump set and the connected lines through the drain, confirm there is no residual pressure, disconnect the cable and the inlet and outlet lines, and finally take the whole pump set off its baseplate."],
	"cx_pump_x": ["离心泵通过电机带动叶轮旋转，让液体向泵壳外侧流动，再利用蜗壳把液体的部分流动速度转化成压力。运行时需要有液体提供冷却和润滑，如果泵内没有液体还继续运转，机械密封可能在几十秒内就因为过热而损坏。完整泵组的回收价值通常比直接拆成废金属高得多。", "A centrifugal pump has a motor turn an impeller, which throws the liquid towards the outside of the pump casing, and the volute then turns part of the liquid’s speed into pressure. While running it needs liquid for cooling and lubrication, and if the pump keeps running with no liquid inside, the mechanical seal may be damaged by overheating within tens of seconds. A whole pump set is usually worth much more when recovered than when broken down into scrap metal."],
	"cx_hx": ["管壳式换热器", "SHELL-AND-TUBE HEAT EXCHANGER"],
	"cx_hx_a": ["管壳式换热器里面装着一组换热管，一种液体从管子内部流过，另一种液体则从管子外面的壳体空间流过。两种液体通过管壁传递热量，正常情况下不会直接混合。", "A shell-and-tube heat exchanger holds a bundle of heat exchange tubes. One liquid flows through the inside of the tubes, and another flows through the shell space outside the tubes. The two liquids pass heat through the tube walls, and normally do not mix directly."],
	"cx_hx_b": ["换热器内部有两套独立的液体管路，分别叫作管程和壳程。就算其中一侧已经排空，另一侧也可能还存有液体和压力，如果直接拆除管道，就可能造成液体泄漏。", "A heat exchanger has two independent sets of liquid lines inside, called the tube side and the shell side. Even if one side has been emptied, the other side may still hold liquid and pressure, and removing the pipes directly may cause a liquid leak."],
	"cx_hx_c": ["先分别检查管程和壳程，确认两侧都已经隔离并完成泄压，再把内部残留的液体全部排空。确认安全以后，逐一拆除连接的管道，最后再拆下整台换热器。", "First check the tube side and the shell side separately, confirm both sides are isolated and vented, and then drain all the liquid left inside. Once it is safe, remove the connected pipes one by one, and finally take off the whole heat exchanger."],
	"cx_hx_x": ["换热器内部装有折流板，可以改变壳程液体的流动方向，让液体反复经过换热管束，提高热量传递的效率。由于管程和壳程的压力、温度以及内部介质可能各不相同，拆除时需要把四个管口分别检查和处理，不能因为其中一侧已经排空，就认为整台换热器都已经安全。", "A heat exchanger has baffles inside which change the flow direction of the shell-side liquid and make it cross the tube bundle repeatedly, raising the efficiency of heat transfer. Because the pressure, temperature and medium inside the tube side and the shell side may all differ, the four nozzles need to be checked and handled separately when removing it, and you cannot assume the whole heat exchanger is safe just because one side has been emptied."],
	"cx_radiator": ["散热板", "RADIATOR PANEL"],
	"cx_radiator_a": ["散热板的两端装有集管，中间排列着大量冷却液流道管。冷却液经过这些管道时，会把热量传递到散热板表面，再通过热辐射把热量排放到太空中。", "A radiator panel has headers at both ends and a large number of coolant flow tubes arranged in between. As coolant passes through these tubes, it passes heat to the panel surface, and the heat is then radiated into space."],
	"cx_radiator_b": ["散热板的管道里可能还存有冷却液，刚停止运行时，板面温度也可能很高。如果还没有完成冷却就直接收拢或者拆除，散热板可能因为受热不均而发生变形。", "The tubes of a radiator panel may still hold coolant, and just after it stops running, the panel surface may also be very hot. If you fold or remove it before it has cooled, the radiator panel may deform from uneven heating."],
	"cx_radiator_c": ["先让冷却回路继续运行一段时间，等散热板的温度降下来以后，再把管道里的冷却液排空。确认温度和管道状态都正常以后，就可以拆除散热板了。", "First let the cooling loop keep running for a while, and once the radiator panel’s temperature has dropped, drain the coolant out of the tubes. After confirming the temperature and the state of the tubes are both normal, you can remove the radiator panel."],
	"cx_radiator_x": ["太空中没有空气，散热板只能依靠热辐射把热量排出去，散热功率可以用 P = εσAT⁴ 计算。在理想条件下，温度为 300 K 的散热板，每平方米大约能辐射 400 W 的热量，所以航天器通常需要安装面积很大的散热板。\n散热板本身比较薄，重量也比较轻，一般通过铰链固定在支撑吊杆上。拆卸和搬运的时候要控制好力度，避免把板面或者连接部位弄坏。", "There is no air in space, so a radiator panel can only shed heat by thermal radiation, and the radiated power can be calculated as P = εσAT⁴. Under ideal conditions, a panel at 300 K radiates about 400 W of heat per square metre, which is why spacecraft usually need radiator panels of large area.\nThe panel itself is fairly thin and light, and is generally held on its supporting boom by hinges. When removing and moving it, control your force, so you do not damage the panel surface or the connection points."],
	"cx_chiller": ["制冷机组", "CHILLER"],
	"cx_chiller_a": ["制冷机组主要由压缩机、冷凝器、膨胀阀和蒸发器组成，这些设备通过管道连接起来，形成一套完整的制冷系统，负责给货舱或其他设备降温。", "A chiller set consists mainly of a compressor, a condenser, an expansion valve and an evaporator. They are joined by pipes into a complete refrigeration system that cools cargo holds and other equipment."],
	"cx_chiller_b": ["有些货舱和设备需要一直保持低温，如果提前关闭制冷机组，或者在拆除过程中损坏了制冷管道，原本冷却的区域就会逐渐升温，里面的货物和设备可能因此受损。", "Some cargo holds and equipment must be kept cold all the time. If you switch off the chiller set too early, or damage the refrigeration lines during removal, the area that was cooled gradually warms up, and the cargo and equipment inside may be damaged."],
	"cx_chiller_c": ["拆除之前，先确认制冷机组还连接着哪些货舱或设备。如果这些地方仍然需要保持低温，就先接通船坞的临时供冷系统，或者把需要冷藏的货物处理好，确认不再需要原来的制冷机组以后，再停止运行并准备拆除。", "Before removal, check which cargo holds or equipment the chiller set still serves. If they must stay cold, connect the berth’s temporary cooling first or deal with the chilled cargo; stop and remove the set only once it is no longer needed."],
	"cx_chiller_x": ["制冷机组通过制冷剂循环来转移热量。制冷剂在蒸发器里吸收热量并蒸发成气体，经过压缩机压缩以后，再进入冷凝器释放热量，重新变成液体，随后经过膨胀阀降压，继续下一轮循环。拆除时还要通过储液罐的回收接口，把管道里的制冷剂回收到专用容器中，不能直接排放到外部环境。", "A chiller set moves heat by circulating a refrigerant. The refrigerant absorbs heat in the evaporator and evaporates into gas, is compressed by the compressor, then enters the condenser, gives off heat and becomes liquid again, and then drops in pressure through the expansion valve and goes on to the next cycle. When removing it, you also need to use the recovery port of the receiver to recover the refrigerant in the lines into a dedicated container, and it cannot be vented directly into the outside environment."],
	"cx_freezer": ["超低温冷柜", "ULTRA-LOW FREEZER"],
	"cx_freezer_a": ["这种冷柜主要用来保存需要低温储存的样品和药品，内部温度通常保持在 −80 °C 左右。冷柜配有保温门、温度控制器和压缩机舱，可以长时间维持内部的低温环境。", "This kind of freezer is mainly used to store samples and medicines that need low-temperature storage, and its internal temperature is usually kept at about −80 °C. The freezer has an insulated door, a temperature controller and a compressor bay, and can keep the low temperature inside for a long time."],
	"cx_freezer_b": ["冷柜断电以后，内部温度会慢慢升高。有些样品对储存温度要求很严格，只要温度超过规定范围，就可能失去使用价值。", "After a freezer loses power, the temperature inside slowly rises. Some samples have strict storage temperature requirements, and as soon as the temperature goes beyond the set range, they may lose their value."],
	"cx_freezer_c": ["如果冷柜里面还有需要低温保存的样品，就保持供电，把整台冷柜送到设备回收口。如果准备断电拆除，需要先检查内部有没有必须继续冷藏的物品，确认可以断电以后再进行拆除。", "If the freezer still holds samples that must be kept cold, keep it powered and send the whole freezer to the equipment recovery mouth. If you plan to cut the power and remove it, first check whether anything inside must stay refrigerated, and remove it only after confirming the power can be cut."],
	"cx_freezer_x": ["保温性能较好的冷柜在断电以后，内部温度通常每小时会上升几度，具体速度取决于冷柜的保温性能和外部温度。如果打开柜门，温度上升的速度还会明显加快。很多低温样品都有严格的温度限制，只要储存过程中超过规定温度，即使后来重新冷冻，也可能无法继续使用，所以完整保存的冷链样品通常有更高的回收价值。", "A freezer with good insulation usually warms by a few degrees per hour after losing power, and the exact speed depends on its insulation performance and the outside temperature. If the door is opened, the temperature rises noticeably faster. Many low-temperature samples have strict temperature limits, and once they exceed the set temperature in storage, they may be unusable even if frozen again later, so cold-chain samples kept intact usually have a higher recovery value."],
	"cx_env": ["空气处理机", "AIR HANDLING UNIT"],
	"cx_env_a": ["空气处理机由进风阀、过滤器、冷却盘管、离心风机和送风箱组成，这些部件按照空气流动的方向依次安装在机组内部。", "An air handling unit consists of an intake damper, a filter, a cooling coil, a centrifugal fan and a discharge plenum, installed inside the unit one after another in the direction of the air flow."],
	"cx_env_b": ["冷却盘管里面可能还留有冷却液，接水盘里也可能有积水。风机通过供电总线连接电源，拆除之前需要确认电源已经断开。", "The cooling coil may still hold coolant, and the drain pan may hold standing water. The fan is connected to its power through the supply bus, so you need to confirm the power is disconnected before removal."],
	"cx_env_c": ["先断开风机电源，再把冷却盘管里的液体排空，确认处理完成以后，就可以拆除连接的风管和底座固定螺栓。", "First disconnect the fan’s power, then drain the liquid out of the cooling coil, and once that is done, you can remove the connected ducts and the base fixing bolts."],
	"cx_env_x": ["空气处理机负责让舱室里的空气不断循环，同时进行降温和除湿，通常也是舱室里体积比较大的设备之一。内部各个部件按照空气流动的方向排列，方便空气依次经过过滤器和冷却盘管。需要注意的是，空气处理机不负责控制舱室的整体气压，如果要给舱室泄压，还得通过专门的舱室接口操作。", "An air handling unit keeps the air in a room circulating while also cooling and drying it, and is usually one of the larger pieces of equipment in a room. Its internal parts are arranged along the direction of the air flow, so that the air passes through the filter and the cooling coil in turn. Note that the air handling unit does not control the overall pressure of the room, and to vent a room, you still have to use the room’s own dedicated port."],
	"cx_duct_fan": ["风道轴流风机", "AXIAL DUCT FAN"],
	"cx_duct_fan_a": ["安装在通风管道里的轴流风机，主要由电机、叶轮和导流叶片组成，用来推动空气沿着管道流动。", "An axial fan fitted in a ventilation duct, consisting mainly of a motor, an impeller and guide vanes, used to drive air along the duct."],
	"cx_duct_fan_b": ["如果没有切断电源就拆除接线盒，可能会产生电弧。风机断电以后，叶轮也可能还在继续转动，直接拆除容易发生意外。", "If you remove the terminal box without cutting the power, an arc may be produced. After the fan loses power, the impeller may also still be turning, and removing it directly easily leads to an accident."],
	"cx_duct_fan_c": ["先切断风机电源，确认线路没有电压，再等待叶轮完全停止转动，最后拆除连接法兰，把风机从管道上卸下来。", "First cut the fan’s power and confirm the line has no voltage, then wait until the impeller has stopped turning completely, and finally remove the connecting flanges and take the fan off the duct."],
	"cx_duct_fan_x": ["风机断电以后，叶轮不会立即停止，还会因为惯性继续转动一段时间。如果周围是真空环境，没有空气阻力，叶轮减速的速度就会更慢，所以拆除之前一定要确认叶轮已经完全停止转动。", "After a fan loses power, the impeller does not stop at once, and keeps turning for a while by inertia. In vacuum there is no air resistance, so the impeller slows down even more slowly, and before removal you must confirm the impeller has stopped turning completely."],
	"cx_filter": ["过滤器", "CARTRIDGE FILTER"],
	"cx_filter_a": ["过滤器里面装着折叠式滤芯，外壳上有进出口、压差表和排放阀，主要用来过滤管道里的杂质和污染物。", "A filter holds a pleated element, and the housing has an inlet, an outlet, a differential pressure gauge and a drain valve. It is mainly used to filter impurities and contaminants out of the line."],
	"cx_filter_b": ["滤芯使用一段时间以后，会积累大量过滤下来的污染物，其中可能含有有毒物质，甚至带有放射性，拆除的时候要特别注意。", "After an element has been in use for a while, it collects a lot of the contaminants it has filtered out, which may contain toxic substances and may even be radioactive, so take special care when removing it."],
	"cx_filter_c": ["先关闭过滤器连接的管路，确认内部已经卸压，再通过排放阀排空残留物。遇到受到污染的滤芯，要做好密封处理，然后送到危险品回收口。", "First close the line the filter is connected to, confirm the pressure inside has been relieved, and then drain the residue through the drain valve. A contaminated element must be sealed, and then sent to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_filter_x": ["压差表可以显示滤芯进出口之间的压力差，滤芯里面积累的杂质越多，流体通过时受到的阻力就越大，压差通常也会随之增加。隔离舱、核设施和生物舱里的过滤器还可能残留危险物质，所以拆卸下来的滤芯也要按照危险品处理。", "The differential pressure gauge shows the pressure difference between the element’s inlet and outlet. The more impurities collect in the element, the greater the resistance to the fluid passing through, and the differential pressure usually rises with it. Filters in isolation rooms, nuclear facilities and biological bays may also hold hazardous substances, so removed elements must also be handled as hazardous items."],
	"cx_trap": ["疏水器", "CONDENSATE TRAP"],
	"cx_trap_a": ["这是一种倒置浮桶式疏水器，安装在蒸汽管路上，主要用来排出管道里积存的冷凝水，同时尽量减少蒸汽流失。", "This is an inverted-bucket steam trap fitted on a steam line. It is mainly used to discharge condensate that collects in the line, while losing as little steam as possible."],
	"cx_trap_b": ["疏水器连接着蒸汽管路，内部可能还有高温蒸汽和残余压力。就算已经停止供汽，也不能直接拆除。", "A steam trap is connected to a steam line, and may still hold high-temperature steam and residual pressure inside. Even if the steam supply has stopped, it cannot be removed directly."],
	"cx_trap_c": ["拆除之前先检查疏水器和管路的温度，再把内部压力释放干净，确认温度和压力都已经降到安全范围以后，才能开始拆除。", "Before removal, first check the temperature of the steam trap and the line, then release the pressure inside completely, and start removal only after confirming that the temperature and pressure have both dropped to a safe range."],
	"cx_trap_x": ["普通倒置浮桶式疏水器利用浮力控制阀门，浮桶里充满蒸汽时会上浮并关闭阀门，冷凝水进入以后，浮桶会逐渐下沉，让阀门重新打开。\n不过在失重环境下，普通浮桶无法依靠浮力正常工作，所以船上的疏水器都经过了专门改造，主要利用管路之间的压力差和流体流动来排出冷凝水。", "An ordinary inverted-bucket steam trap uses buoyancy to control a valve. When the bucket is full of steam, it floats up and closes the valve, and once condensate enters, the bucket gradually sinks and opens the valve again.\nIn weightlessness, however, an ordinary bucket cannot work by buoyancy, so the steam traps on the ship have all been specially modified, and mainly use the pressure difference between lines and the flow of the fluid to discharge condensate."],
	"cx_manifold": ["阀组（总管）", "VALVE MANIFOLD"],
	"cx_manifold_a": ["一根总管连接着多条支管，每条支管上都有独立的隔离阀，可以分别控制各条管路的流通。", "One header pipe connects to several branch pipes, and each branch has its own isolating valve, which can control the flow in each line separately."],
	"cx_manifold_b": ["每条支管里输送的介质和内部压力可能都不一样，如果直接拆除总管，里面残留的液体或气体就可能从多个接口同时泄漏出来。", "The medium and internal pressure in each branch may differ, and if you remove the header directly, the liquid or gas left inside may leak out of several ports at once."],
	"cx_manifold_c": ["先把每条支管的隔离阀逐一关闭，再排空管道里剩余的介质，确认所有管路都没有压力以后，才能开始拆除总管。", "First close the isolating valve of each branch one by one, then drain the medium left in the lines, and start removing the header only after confirming that no line has any pressure."],
	"cx_manifold_x": ["阀组可以让一台泵同时连接多个储罐，通过各条支管上的阀门来控制输送方向。如果其他储罐的阀门没有关闭，抽取其中一个储罐时，就可能连带抽走其他储罐里的介质。如果里面装着不同的物料，还可能在总管中发生混合，所以操作之前一定要确认各条支管的阀门状态。", "A valve manifold lets one pump connect to several tanks at once, and the valves on the branches control the direction of transfer. If the valves of the other tanks have not been closed, drawing from one tank may also draw the contents of the others. If they hold different materials, they may also mix in the header, so always confirm the valve state of every branch before operating."],
	"cx_aux": ["调节阀", "CONTROL VALVE"],
	"cx_aux_a": ["调节阀由球形阀体、阀盖、膜片执行器和定位器组成，可以根据控制信号自动调整阀门的开度，控制管道内的流量。", "A control valve consists of a globe valve body, a bonnet, a diaphragm actuator and a positioner. It adjusts its opening automatically according to a control signal, controlling the flow in the line."],
	"cx_aux_b": ["执行器失去气源或电源后，阀门会自动移动到预设的故障位置，有些会完全打开，有些会完全关闭，具体要看阀门的设置。", "When the actuator loses its air or power supply, the valve automatically moves to its preset fail position. Some open fully and some close fully, depending on how the valve is set."],
	"cx_aux_c": ["不要直接用调节阀隔离管道，拆卸之前要先关闭手动隔离阀，确认管道已经完成隔离和泄压后才能动手。", "Do not use a control valve directly to isolate a line. Before removal, close the manual isolating valves first, and start work only after confirming the line has been isolated and depressurised."],
	"cx_aux_x": ["调节阀通过控制信号连续调整阀门开度，阀芯本身存在间隙，关闭以后也可能发生泄漏，所以不能用来代替专门的隔离阀。故障开（FO）型调节阀在触发预设的故障动作时，会自动移动到全开位置。", "A control valve adjusts its opening continuously according to the control signal, and its trim has clearances, so it may leak even when closed, and cannot take the place of a proper isolating valve. A fail-open (FO) control valve moves automatically to the fully open position when its preset failure action is triggered."],
	"cx_relief": ["安全阀", "PRESSURE RELIEF VALVE"],
	"cx_relief_a": ["当储气罐里面的压力超过规定值时，安全阀就会自动打开，把多余的气体排出去，等压力降下来以后再关闭。", "When the pressure in a gas tank goes above the set value, the relief valve opens automatically and vents the excess gas, and closes again once the pressure has dropped."],
	"cx_relief_b": ["如果安全阀结冰或者被杂物堵住，罐内的气体就没办法正常排出。一旦压力继续升高，整个储气罐都有可能发生爆炸。", "If the relief valve freezes or is blocked by debris, the gas in the tank cannot be vented properly. If the pressure keeps rising, the whole gas tank may explode."],
	"cx_relief_c": ["先检查储气罐的温度和压力，如果发现安全阀已经结冰，就需要按照操作规程进行解冻处理。如果压力仍然过高，可以通过专门的接口进行抽气泄压。", "First check the gas tank’s temperature and pressure. If you find the relief valve frozen, it must be thawed following the operating procedure. If the pressure is still too high, you can pump it down and relieve it through a dedicated port."],
	"cx_relief_x": ["安全阀是防止储气罐超压的重要保护装置，开启压力通常按照容器的设计压力设定，一般在设计压力的 1.0～1.1 倍范围内。安全阀打开以后会持续排气，直到压力降低到规定的回座压力才会重新关闭。低温储气罐在排气时，排出的冷气可能让阀门出口附近结冰，严重时还会形成冰塞，影响正常泄压。", "The relief valve is an important protective device that stops a gas tank from over-pressurising. Its opening pressure is usually set by the vessel’s design pressure, generally within 1.0–1.1 times the design pressure. Once the relief valve opens, it keeps venting until the pressure falls to the specified reseat pressure, and only then closes again. When a cryogenic gas tank vents, the cold gas it releases may freeze the area near the valve outlet, and in serious cases it forms an ice plug that stops normal pressure relief."],
	"cx_pipe": ["管路", "PIPE RUN"],
	"cx_pipe_a": ["这是一段连接着法兰的管道，外面包着保温材料，并通过吊架固定在船体结构上。", "This is a length of pipe with flanges connected to it, wrapped in insulation material and held to the hull structure by hangers."],
	"cx_pipe_b": ["如果管道里面还有液体，直接切开就可能发生泄漏。如果里面装的是易燃物质，切割时还可能喷出可燃液体或气体，引发火灾。", "If the pipe still holds liquid, cutting it directly may cause a leak. If it holds something flammable, cutting may also spray out flammable liquid or gas and start a fire."],
	"cx_pipe_c": ["先关闭管道上下游的阀门，再通过低处的排放口把内部液体排空。确认没有残留压力以后，就可以拆卸法兰，把整段管道取下来。", "First close the valves upstream and downstream of the pipe, then drain the liquid inside through the low-point drain. Once you have confirmed there is no residual pressure, you can unbolt the flanges and take off the whole length of pipe."],
	"cx_pipe_x": ["相比直接切割管道，拆卸法兰可以保留完整的管道结构，只需要松开连接处的螺栓，就能把整段管道拆下来回收。不过在失重环境下，管道里面残留的液体不会因为打开排放口就自动流出去，需要使用抽液设备才能排空。", "Compared with cutting the pipe, unbolting the flanges keeps the pipe structure whole, and you only need to loosen the bolts at the joints to take the whole length off for recovery. In weightlessness, however, the liquid left in the pipe does not flow out by itself just because the drain is opened, and it needs a liquid-pumping device to be emptied."],
	"cx_hpu": ["液压站", "HYDRAULIC POWER UNIT"],
	"cx_hpu_a": ["液压站主要由油箱、电机泵、蓄能器、电磁阀组和压力表组成，负责给船上的液压设备提供动力。", "A hydraulic power unit consists mainly of an oil reservoir, a motor-pump, accumulators, a solenoid valve block and a pressure gauge, and powers the ship’s hydraulic equipment."],
	"cx_hpu_b": ["蓄能器里面储存着高压液压油，即使已经切断电源，内部也可能保留很高的压力。如果这时候直接切断管道，高压液压油就可能从切口喷射出来，十分危险。", "The accumulators store high-pressure hydraulic oil, and even after the power is cut, they may keep a very high pressure inside. If you cut a line at this point, the high-pressure hydraulic oil may spray out of the cut, which is very dangerous."],
	"cx_hpu_c": ["先打开泄压阀，把蓄能器里面的压力释放掉，确认压力表已经降到 0，而且设备没有残留压力以后，再开始拆卸连接管道和液压机构。", "First open the relief valve and release the pressure in the accumulators. After confirming the pressure gauge has dropped to 0 and the equipment holds no residual pressure, start removing the connected lines and the hydraulic mechanisms."],
	"cx_hpu_x": ["液压系统的工作压力经常超过 20 MPa，一个容量为 20 L 的蓄能器，在 20 MPa 的压力下可能储存约 200 kJ 的能量，具体数值取决于蓄能器的工作条件。即使关闭了电机，只要内部还有压力，液压缸、夹钳和机械臂就可能突然动作，所以拆卸之前一定要把残留压力释放干净，并确认机械部件已经固定好。", "The working pressure of a hydraulic system often exceeds 20 MPa, and a 20 L accumulator at 20 MPa may store about 200 kJ of energy, with the exact value depending on the accumulator’s working conditions. Even with the motor switched off, as long as pressure remains inside, hydraulic cylinders, clamps and mechanical arms may suddenly move, so always release the residual pressure completely before removal, and confirm the mechanical parts have been secured."],
	"cx_actuator": ["直线作动器", "LINEAR ACTUATOR"],
	"cx_actuator_a": ["直线作动器由电机、传动皮带、滚珠丝杠和推杆组成，可以把电机的旋转运动转换成推杆的直线运动，用来推动或者调整设备的位置。", "A linear actuator consists of a motor, a drive belt, a ball screw and a push rod. It converts the motor’s rotary motion into straight-line motion of the push rod, used to push or adjust the position of equipment."],
	"cx_actuator_b": ["如果作动器还在通电，拆断控制线路时就可能导致推杆突然移动。如果它正在支撑其他设备，而这些设备又没有固定好，就可能在推杆移动后直接掉下来。", "If an actuator is still powered, cutting its control line may make the push rod suddenly move. If it is supporting other equipment that has not been secured, that equipment may drop straight down once the rod moves."],
	"cx_actuator_c": ["拆卸之前，先用锁定装置固定推杆，并把它支撑的设备固定好。确认这些部件不会突然移动以后，再切断电源，开始拆卸作动器。", "Before removal, first fix the push rod with the locking device, and secure the equipment it supports. After confirming these parts will not suddenly move, cut the power and start removing the actuator."],
	"cx_actuator_x": ["滚珠丝杠的传动效率很高，除了能够把电机的旋转运动转换成直线推力，外部负载也可能反过来推动丝杠旋转。如果作动器没有安装制动装置，即使切断了电源，推杆仍然可能在负载作用下发生移动。一些用于调整精密镜片位置的作动器还会配备专门的锁定机构，防止断电以后出现位置偏移。", "A ball screw has very high drive efficiency. As well as converting the motor’s rotary motion into straight-line thrust, an external load can also drive the screw round in reverse. If the actuator has no brake, even after the power is cut, the push rod may still move under the load. Some actuators used to adjust the position of precision mirrors are also fitted with dedicated locking mechanisms, to stop the position shifting after power-off."],
	"cx_gastank": ["气瓶", "GAS CYLINDER"],
	"cx_gastank_a": ["这是一种用来储存高压气体的气瓶，顶部装有瓶阀和控制手轮，瓶身上的颜色标记可以帮助工作人员辨认里面储存的气体种类。", "This is a cylinder for storing high-pressure gas. It has a cylinder valve and a control handwheel on top, and the colour marks on the body help crew identify the kind of gas stored inside."],
	"cx_gastank_b": ["气瓶里面储存着大量高压气体，如果直接切割瓶身，就可能导致气瓶爆裂。即使没有发生爆裂，泄漏的气体也可能迅速扩散到舱室里面。如果瓶阀被撞断，高压气体会从瓶口猛烈喷出，甚至可能推动整个气瓶高速飞出去。", "A cylinder holds a lot of high-pressure gas, and cutting the body directly may burst it. Even if it does not burst, the leaked gas may spread quickly into the room. If the cylinder valve is knocked off, the high-pressure gas shoots violently out of the neck, and may even push the whole cylinder off at high speed."],
	"cx_gastank_c": ["如果气瓶的密封状态完好，可以直接把整瓶送到设备回收口。如果需要排放里面的气体，就通过气瓶的 -V 接口进行泄压，确认压力已经释放以后再继续处理，千万不要直接切割瓶身。", "If the cylinder’s seal is intact, you can send the whole cylinder straight to the equipment recovery mouth. If you need to vent the gas inside, relieve it through the cylinder’s -V port, and carry on only after confirming the pressure has been released. Never cut the body directly."],
	"cx_gastank_x": ["一只容量为 50 L、内部压力达到 200 bar 的气瓶，大约储存着 1.5 MJ 的压缩能量，具体数值会受到气体种类和温度的影响。如果瓶阀突然断裂，高压气体会产生很大的反冲力，足以让没有固定好的气瓶高速移动。氧气瓶还需要特别注意，因为高浓度氧气会让周围的可燃材料更容易起火，而且燃烧速度也会明显加快。", "A cylinder of 50 L capacity with an internal pressure of 200 bar stores about 1.5 MJ of compression energy, and the exact value is affected by the kind of gas and its temperature. If the cylinder valve suddenly breaks off, the high-pressure gas produces a large recoil, enough to send an unsecured cylinder moving at high speed. Oxygen cylinders need special care, because high-concentration oxygen makes the surrounding combustible materials catch fire more easily, and also makes them burn noticeably faster."],
	"cx_fueltank": ["推进剂 / 工艺储罐", "PROPELLANT TANK"],
	"cx_fueltank_a": ["这是一种用来储存推进剂或其他工艺液体的压力容器，通常横放在鞍座上，内部安装了防止液体晃动的隔板，顶部还有管道接口和液位计。", "This is a pressure vessel for storing propellant or other process liquids. It usually lies on its side on saddles, has baffles inside to stop the liquid sloshing, and has pipe connections and a level gauge on top."],
	"cx_fueltank_b": ["如果储罐里面还有液体或者残留压力，直接切割就可能引发爆炸。如果储存的是易燃燃料，泄漏后还可能形成可燃气云，一旦遇到火花就有发生火灾或爆炸的危险。", "If the tank still holds liquid or residual pressure, cutting it directly may cause an explosion. If it stores flammable fuel, the leak may also form a flammable gas cloud, and if it meets a spark, there is a danger of fire or explosion."],
	"cx_fueltank_c": ["先通过回收接口把储罐里面的液体抽走，再释放罐顶残留的气体压力。确认储罐已经排空并完成泄压以后，就可以把整个储罐拆下来，送到危险品回收口处理。", "First draw the liquid out of the tank through the recovery port, then release the residual gas pressure at the top of the tank. After confirming the tank has been emptied and depressurised, you can take the whole tank off and send it to the hazard mouth for handling."],
	"cx_fueltank_x": ["储罐顶部通常会留出一部分气体空间，利用气体压力维持罐内压力，让液体能够正常进入输送泵。抽取液体时，需要通过增压系统维持压力，或者在允许的情况下补充气体，避免罐内压力降得太低。在真空环境下，如果只抽取液体却没有及时补充气体，罐内外的压力差就可能让储罐发生变形，严重时甚至会被压瘪。", "A tank usually leaves some gas space at the top, which keeps the pressure in the tank up so that the liquid can enter the transfer pump normally. When drawing off liquid, you need to keep the pressure up with the pressurisation system, or add gas where allowed, so that the pressure in the tank does not fall too low. In vacuum, if you draw off only liquid and do not add gas in time, the pressure difference between inside and outside the tank may deform the tank, and in serious cases even crush it."],
	"cx_sphere_tank": ["球形压力罐", "SPHERICAL TANK"],
	"cx_sphere_tank_a": ["这是一种用来储存高压气体或推进剂的球形储罐，罐体中间有一圈焊缝，外侧装有固定用的安装耳，顶部还有加注阀。罐内的推进剂管理叶片可以帮助液体流向出口。", "This is a spherical tank for storing high-pressure gas or propellant. There is a girth weld around the middle of the tank, mounting tabs on the outside for fixing it, and a fill valve on top. The propellant management vanes inside the tank help the liquid flow towards the outlet."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_b": ["球形压力罐通常需要承受很高的内部压力，如果还没有泄压就直接切割，罐内的高压气体可能会突然喷出，严重时甚至会导致整个罐体爆裂。", "A spherical pressure tank usually has to bear very high internal pressure, and if you cut it before it is depressurised, the high-pressure gas inside may suddenly burst out, and in serious cases the whole tank may rupture."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_c": ["先检查压力罐的内部压力，再通过专门的接口进行泄压。等压力降到安全范围以后，就可以拆卸外侧的安装耳，将整个压力罐完整取下来。", "First check the internal pressure of the pressure tank, then relieve it through the dedicated port. Once the pressure has dropped to a safe range, you can unbolt the mounting tabs on the outside and take the whole pressure tank off intact."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_x": ["在材料和壁厚相同的情况下，理想薄壁球罐的承压能力大约是圆筒形罐体的两倍，所以高压气体和推进剂经常会储存在球形压力罐里。由于失重环境下的液体不会自然沉到罐底，罐内还装有推进剂管理叶片，可以利用毛细作用让液体集中到出口附近，方便后续输送。", "With the same material and wall thickness, an ideal thin-walled spherical tank can bear about twice the pressure of a cylindrical tank, so high-pressure gas and propellant are often stored in spherical pressure tanks. Because liquid in weightlessness does not settle at the bottom of the tank by itself, the tank also has propellant management vanes, which use capillary action to gather the liquid near the outlet and make later transfer easier."],
	"cx_cryotank": ["低温储罐", "CRYOGENIC TANK"],
	"cx_cryotank_a": ["低温储罐主要用来储存液氢、液氮和液化天然气等需要低温保存的液体。储罐内部有一层真空夹套，可以减少外界热量进入，让里面的液体保持在很低的温度。", "A cryogenic tank is mainly used to store liquids that must be kept cold, such as liquid hydrogen, liquid nitrogen and liquefied natural gas. Inside the tank there is a vacuum jacket, which reduces heat coming in from outside and keeps the liquid at a very low temperature."],
	"cx_cryotank_b": ["即使有保温层，外界的热量还是会慢慢进入储罐，导致里面的液体不断蒸发，罐内压力也会随之升高。如果安全阀因为结冰而无法正常泄压，压力继续升高以后，就有可能发生爆罐。", "Even with insulation, heat from outside still slowly enters the tank, so the liquid inside keeps evaporating and the pressure in the tank rises with it. If the relief valve is frozen and cannot relieve the pressure properly, the pressure keeps rising and the tank may burst."],
	"cx_cryotank_c": ["先保持制冷系统正常运行，再通过专门的接口抽出罐内的液体和气体，让内部压力逐渐降低。确认储罐已经排空并完成泄压以后，再关闭制冷系统，切断相关电源。", "First keep the refrigeration system running normally, then draw the liquid and gas out of the tank through the dedicated port, so that the internal pressure gradually falls. After confirming the tank has been emptied and depressurised, switch off the refrigeration system and cut the related power."],
	"cx_cryotank_x": ["在正常大气压下，液氢的沸点约为 −253°C，液氮的沸点约为 −196°C。只要有热量进入储罐，就会有一部分液体蒸发成气体，而这些气体在常温常压下的体积可以达到原来液体体积的几百倍。如果气体没有及时排出，罐内压力就会不断升高。真空夹套一旦破损，外界进入的热量可能增加十倍，液体的蒸发速度也会明显加快。", "At normal atmospheric pressure, liquid hydrogen boils at about −253°C and liquid nitrogen at about −196°C. Whenever heat gets into the tank, some of the liquid evaporates into gas, and at normal temperature and pressure this gas can take up several hundred times the volume of the original liquid. If the gas is not vented in time, the pressure in the tank keeps rising. Once the vacuum jacket is damaged, the heat coming in from outside may increase tenfold, and the liquid evaporates noticeably faster."],
	"cx_water": ["水箱", "WATER TANK"],
	"cx_water_a": ["这是船上用来储存水的容器，水箱上装有人孔、通气管和液位镜，内部还有防晃板，可以减少船体移动时水的晃动。", "This is a container on the ship for storing water. The water tank has a manway, a vent pipe and a level sight glass, and anti-slosh baffles inside that reduce water sloshing when the hull moves."],
	"cx_water_b": ["如果水箱里面还有水，直接切开就会造成泄漏。在失重环境下，流出来的水会漂浮在空中，一旦接触附近的带电设备，就可能引发短路。", "If the water tank still holds water, cutting it open directly causes a leak. In weightlessness, the water that comes out floats in the air, and if it touches live equipment nearby, it may cause a short circuit."],
	"cx_water_c": ["先通过出水阀或者专门的接口，把水箱里面的水全部抽出来，确认水箱已经排空以后，再拆卸外部连接件，将整个水箱取下来。", "First draw all the water out of the tank through the outlet valve or a dedicated port, and after confirming the tank has been emptied, remove the external connections and take off the whole tank."],
	"cx_water_x": ["水如果直接暴露在真空环境中，就会因为压力突然降低而迅速沸腾，同时蒸发还会带走大量热量，让剩余的水逐渐结冰，形成漂浮的冰块。这些冰块还会继续缓慢升华，所以直接切开水箱会损失不少水。水在船上属于有回收价值的资源，哪怕只有几立方米，也能按照合同价格卖出一笔钱。", "If water is exposed directly to vacuum, it boils rapidly because the pressure suddenly drops, and the evaporation also carries away a lot of heat, so the remaining water gradually freezes into floating blocks of ice. These blocks of ice also keep slowly subliming, so cutting the tank open directly loses quite a lot of water. Water on a ship is a resource with recovery value, and even a few cubic metres can be sold at the contract price for a sum of money."],
	"cx_extinguisher": ["灭火瓶", "FIRE SUPPRESSION BOTTLE"],
	"cx_extinguisher_a": ["这是一种船上使用的灭火装置，瓶内储存着灭火剂，外面装有释放头、压力表和电磁启动器，可以在发生火灾时释放灭火剂。", "This is a fire-fighting device used on the ship. The bottle stores extinguishing agent, and on the outside there are a discharge head, a pressure gauge and a solenoid actuator, so the agent can be released in the event of a fire."],
	"cx_extinguisher_b": ["灭火瓶本身属于高压容器，如果电磁启动器还连接着电源，拆卸时就有可能意外触发，导致瓶内的灭火剂突然喷出。如果瓶内还有压力，直接切割瓶体也可能造成爆裂。", "The extinguisher bottle is itself a high-pressure vessel. If the solenoid actuator is still connected to power, it may be triggered by accident during removal, and the agent in the bottle suddenly sprays out. If the bottle still holds pressure, cutting the body directly may also make it burst."],
	"cx_extinguisher_c": ["发生火灾时，可以使用灭火瓶进行灭火。如果暂时不需要使用，就先断开电磁启动器的电源，再把整个灭火瓶拆卸下来，送到危险品回收口处理。", "In a fire, you can use the extinguisher bottle to put it out. If it is not needed for now, first disconnect the solenoid actuator’s power, then take the whole extinguisher bottle off and send it to the hazard mouth for handling."],
	"cx_extinguisher_x": ["船上的灭火系统通常使用二氧化碳、哈龙替代灭火剂或者泡沫。二氧化碳释放到密闭舱室以后，可以降低空气中的氧气浓度，让火焰无法继续燃烧，不过舱室里的气体也会因此混入大量二氧化碳，不能再按照普通空气回收，而且人员继续留在里面还可能发生窒息。有些旧船上的灭火瓶可能已经用完了，拆卸前可以先查看压力表，确认瓶内是否还有压力。", "The ship’s fire-fighting systems usually use carbon dioxide, halon substitutes or foam. After carbon dioxide is released into a closed room, it lowers the oxygen concentration in the air so that flames cannot keep burning, but the gas in the room then also contains a lot of carbon dioxide, and can no longer be recovered as ordinary air, and anyone who stays inside may suffocate. The extinguisher bottles on some old ships may already be used up, so before removal you can check the pressure gauge first to confirm whether the bottle still holds pressure."],
	"cx_o2cab": ["应急氧气柜", "EMERGENCY OXYGEN CABINET"],
	"cx_o2cab_a": ["柜子里面放着两只高压氧气瓶，还有配套的减压器和呼吸面罩，外面装着一扇玻璃门，遇到紧急情况时可以打开使用。", "Inside the cabinet there are two high-pressure oxygen cylinders with a matching regulator and breathing masks, and a glass door on the front that can be opened for use in an emergency."],
	"cx_o2cab_b": ["氧气瓶里面储存着高压纯氧，如果在附近使用激光切割设备，一旦氧气发生泄漏，就可能让周围的可燃物更容易起火，火势也会迅速扩大。", "The oxygen cylinders hold high-pressure pure oxygen. If you use laser cutting equipment nearby and the oxygen leaks, the surrounding combustible materials may catch fire more easily, and the fire spreads quickly."],
	"cx_o2cab_c": ["先关闭两只氧气瓶的阀门，确认没有氧气泄漏以后，再把整个氧气柜拆卸下来，送到危险品回收口进行处理。", "First close the valves of both oxygen cylinders, and after confirming no oxygen is leaking, take the whole oxygen cabinet off and send it to the hazard mouth for handling."],
	"cx_o2cab_x": ["氧气本身不会燃烧，但它能够帮助其他物质燃烧，而且氧气浓度越高，燃烧通常就会越剧烈。沾有油脂的材料、织物甚至细小的金属碎屑，在高浓度氧气环境下都可能更容易被点燃，所以拆卸氧气柜时，要特别注意附近有没有高温设备和可能产生火花的工具。", "Oxygen itself does not burn, but it helps other substances burn, and the higher the oxygen concentration, the more violent the burning usually is. Materials stained with grease, fabric and even tiny metal swarf can all be ignited more easily in a high-concentration oxygen environment, so when removing an oxygen cabinet, take special care about hot equipment nearby and tools that may produce sparks."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber": ["CO₂ 洗涤器", "CO₂ SCRUBBER"],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_a": ["这套设备用来清除舱内空气中的二氧化碳，里面装着两个使用胺类吸收剂或沸石的处理罐，还有负责切换气流的阀门和维持空气循环的鼓风机。", "This equipment removes carbon dioxide from the air in the cabin. It holds two treatment canisters that use an amine absorbent or zeolite, plus valves that switch the air flow and a blower that keeps the air circulating."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_b": ["吸收罐里面积累了大量二氧化碳，其中一条再生管道还直接连接着外部真空环境。如果没有关闭阀门就直接拆卸，可能造成二氧化碳泄漏，或者让舱内空气通过管道流失。", "The absorber canisters have collected a lot of carbon dioxide, and one regeneration line is connected directly to the outside vacuum. If you remove it without closing the valves, carbon dioxide may leak, or the cabin air may be lost through the line."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_c": ["先切断洗涤器的电源，关闭连接两个吸收罐的切换阀门，确认管道已经隔离、内部压力也恢复安全以后，再开始拆卸设备。", "First cut the scrubber’s power and close the switching valves that connect the two absorber canisters. Start removing the equipment only after confirming the lines are isolated and the internal pressure is back to a safe level."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_x": ["洗涤器里面的两个吸收罐会交替工作，一个负责吸收舱内空气中的二氧化碳，另一个则通过连接真空的管道，把之前吸收的二氧化碳排出去，让吸收材料恢复使用能力。如果空气中的二氧化碳浓度超过 1%，人就可能出现头痛等不适症状，浓度超过 5% 时还会有严重的生命危险，所以这套设备对密闭舱室的空气循环非常重要。", "The two absorber canisters in the scrubber work in turns. One absorbs the carbon dioxide in the cabin air, while the other releases the carbon dioxide it absorbed earlier through the line connected to vacuum, so the absorbent can be used again. If the carbon dioxide concentration in the air goes above 1%, people may suffer discomfort such as headaches, and above 5% there is serious danger to life, so this equipment is very important for the air circulation of a closed room."],
	"cx_psa": ["变压吸附分离器", "PRESSURE-SWING ADSORPTION"],
	"cx_psa_a": ["这套设备由两根吸附塔和上下两组切换阀门组成，可以利用内部的分子筛，从混合气体中分离出需要的气体。", "This equipment consists of two adsorber columns and an upper and a lower set of switching valves. It uses the molecular sieve inside to separate the gas you need from a mixed gas."],
	"cx_psa_b": ["吸附塔内部可能还存有高压气体，而且分离出来的气体可能是纯氧、纯氮或者氢气。如果直接拆卸，残留的气体可能会从接口喷出。氢气容易燃烧，纯氧会加剧燃烧，纯氮泄漏则可能造成缺氧窒息。", "The adsorber columns may still hold high-pressure gas, and the separated gas may be pure oxygen, pure nitrogen or hydrogen. If you remove them directly, the residual gas may shoot out of the ports. Hydrogen burns easily, pure oxygen makes burning fiercer, and a leak of pure nitrogen may cause suffocation from lack of oxygen."],
	"cx_psa_c": ["先关闭进气阀门，停止向设备输送气体，再通过泄压接口排出吸附塔里面的残余压力。确认两根吸附塔都已经完成泄压以后，再拆卸连接部件。", "First close the feed valve to stop gas going into the equipment, then release the residual pressure in the adsorber columns through the relief port. Remove the connected parts only after confirming both columns have been depressurised."],
	"cx_psa_x": ["吸附塔内部装有分子筛，在较高压力下，分子筛会吸附混合气体中的某些分子，等压力降低以后，又会释放之前吸附的气体。两根吸附塔交替进行加压和减压，就能持续分离出需要的气体。需要注意的是，纯氮一旦大量泄漏到密闭空间，就可能挤走原本的氧气，而且人体通常不会提前察觉缺氧，严重时会直接失去意识。", "The adsorber columns contain a molecular sieve. At higher pressure, the sieve adsorbs certain molecules from the mixed gas, and when the pressure drops, it releases the gas it adsorbed earlier. With the two columns taking turns to pressurise and depressurise, the equipment can keep separating out the gas you need. Note that once a large amount of pure nitrogen leaks into a closed space, it can push out the original oxygen, and people usually do not notice the lack of oxygen beforehand, and in serious cases lose consciousness at once."],
	"cx_electrolyser": ["电解制氧机", "WATER ELECTROLYSER"],
	"cx_electrolyser_a": ["这套设备由电解槽、氢氧气液分离器、循环泵和整流器组成，通过电解水来生产氧气，同时还会产生氢气。", "This equipment consists of an electrolyser stack, hydrogen and oxygen gas-liquid separators, a circulation pump and a rectifier. It produces oxygen by electrolysing water, and also produces hydrogen."],
	"cx_electrolyser_b": ["设备里面同时有氢气、氧气和高压电，如果气体发生泄漏，氢气和氧气就可能混合在一起。一旦遇到电火花或者高温，就有可能发生爆炸。", "The equipment holds hydrogen, oxygen and high-voltage power at the same time. If gas leaks, the hydrogen and oxygen may mix together, and if the mixture meets an electric spark or high temperature, it may explode."],
	"cx_electrolyser_c": ["先切断设备电源，确认电解槽已经停止运行，再通过各自的排气接口，分别排空氢气和氧气。等两侧都完成泄压以后，再开始拆卸设备。", "First cut the equipment’s power and confirm the electrolyser stack has stopped running, then vent the hydrogen and the oxygen separately through their own vent ports. Start removing the equipment only after both sides have been depressurised."],
	"cx_electrolyser_x": ["电解制氧机通过电流把水分解成氢气和氧气，每消耗 1 kg 水，大约可以产生 1.24 m³ 氢气和 0.62 m³ 氧气，耗电量约为 5 kWh。氢气和氧气的体积比例达到 2:1 时，正好符合完全反应所需的比例，这种混合气体通常被称为爆鸣气，遇到火源就可能发生非常剧烈的爆炸。", "An electrolyser oxygen generator uses electric current to split water into hydrogen and oxygen. For every 1 kg of water consumed, it produces about 1.24 m³ of hydrogen and 0.62 m³ of oxygen, using about 5 kWh of electricity. When the volume ratio of hydrogen to oxygen reaches 2:1, it exactly matches the ratio needed for complete reaction, and this mixed gas is usually called detonating gas, which can explode very violently if it meets a source of ignition."],
	"cx_humidifier": ["加湿器", "STEAM HUMIDIFIER"],
	"cx_humidifier_a": ["这是一台电极式加湿器，里面装着用来加热水的电极筒，外面连接着进水阀、排水阀和蒸汽软管，旁边还有一个负责控制设备运行的控制盒。", "This is an electrode humidifier. It holds an electrode cylinder for heating water, the outside is connected to a fill valve, a drain valve and a steam hose, and beside it is a control box that controls how the equipment runs."],
	"cx_humidifier_b": ["加湿器运行时，电极会直接通电加热筒内的水。如果没有切断电源就进行拆卸，可能发生触电事故，而且筒内的热水和蒸汽也容易造成烫伤。", "While the humidifier runs, its electrodes pass current directly through the water in the cylinder to heat it. If you remove it without cutting the power, an electric shock may occur, and the hot water and steam in the cylinder can also easily scald."],
	"cx_humidifier_c": ["先切断加湿器的电源，确认设备已经停止运行，再把筒内的热水排出去。等设备冷却并确认内部没有残留压力以后，就可以开始拆卸了。", "First cut the humidifier’s power and confirm the equipment has stopped running, then drain the hot water out of the cylinder. Once the equipment has cooled and you have confirmed no pressure remains inside, you can start removing it."],
	"cx_humidifier_x": ["电极式加湿器通过让电流直接经过水来产生热量，把水加热到沸腾以后，再利用产生的蒸汽增加空气湿度。水的导电性会影响加热功率，导电性越强，在相同电压等条件下通常就会产生越大的电流。即使已经切断电源，筒内的水也不会马上冷却，所以拆卸之前还需要确认水温，避免被残留的热水烫伤。", "An electrode humidifier makes heat by passing current directly through the water, and after heating the water to boiling, it uses the steam produced to raise the humidity of the air. The conductivity of the water affects the heating power, and the stronger the conductivity, the larger the current usually is under the same voltage and other conditions. Even after the power is cut, the water in the cylinder does not cool at once, so before removal you also need to check the water temperature, to avoid being scalded by the hot water left inside."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser": ["紫外消毒器", "UV STERILISER"],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_a": ["这是一台用紫外线给水消毒的设备，外面是不锈钢外壳，内部装有紫外灯管，还有用来检测紫外线强度的传感器和控制灯管工作的镇流器。", "This is equipment that disinfects water with ultraviolet light. It has a stainless steel casing outside, a UV lamp tube inside, and also a sensor that detects the UV intensity and a ballast that controls the lamp."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_b": ["紫外灯管里面含有汞，外面的石英套管也比较容易破碎。如果直接切割设备，里面的水可能会泄漏，灯管破碎后还可能释放有毒的汞蒸气。", "The UV lamp tube contains mercury, and its outer quartz sleeve breaks fairly easily. If you cut the equipment directly, the water inside may leak, and if the lamp breaks, it may also release toxic mercury vapour."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_c": ["先切断设备电源，再把内部的水全部排空。确认设备已经断电、没有残留液体以后，就可以把整台消毒器拆下来，送到设备回收口。", "First cut the equipment’s power, then drain all the water inside. After confirming the power is off and no liquid remains, you can take the whole steriliser off and send it to the equipment recovery mouth."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_x": ["紫外消毒器主要利用波长约为 254 纳米的紫外线破坏微生物的 DNA，让它们失去正常繁殖的能力。设备内部的灯管通常含有少量汞，如果拆卸时不小心打碎灯管，汞就可能释放到周围环境中，所以回收时要尽量保持灯管和石英套管完整。", "A UV steriliser mainly uses ultraviolet light with a wavelength of about 254 nanometres to damage the DNA of microorganisms, so they lose the ability to reproduce normally. The lamp tube inside the equipment usually contains a small amount of mercury, and if you accidentally break the lamp during removal, the mercury may be released into the surroundings, so when recovering it, keep the lamp tube and the quartz sleeve intact as far as possible."],
	"cx_separator_3ph": ["三相分离器", "THREE-PHASE SEPARATOR"],
	"cx_separator_3ph_a": ["三相分离器是一种卧式容器，内部装有堰板，可以把混合在一起的油、水和气体分离开来，再通过各自的出口排出去。", "A three-phase separator is a horizontal vessel with a weir inside. It separates mixed oil, water and gas, and discharges each through its own outlet."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_b": ["即使设备已经停止运行，容器内部也可能残留一定的压力，而且里面还可能存有油、水和气体。如果直接拆开，残留的压力和介质就有可能从开口处喷出来。", "Even after the equipment has stopped running, some pressure may remain inside the vessel, and it may also still hold oil, water and gas. If you open it directly, the residual pressure and contents may shoot out of the opening."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_c": ["拆卸之前，先通过顶部的泄压接口把容器内部的压力降下来，再分别打开油、水和气体对应的排放接口，确认三路都已经排空以后，才能开始拆卸。", "Before removal, first bring down the pressure inside the vessel through the relief port at the top, then open the drain ports for oil, water and gas separately, and start removal only after confirming all three have been emptied."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_x": ["地面上的三相分离器主要利用重力进行分离，油、水和气体的密度不同，经过一段时间后就会逐渐分开。船上的分离设备则通常会利用旋流或者离心力来完成分离，这样可以减少对重力沉降的依赖，也能让设备做得更加紧凑。", "On the ground, a three-phase separator separates mainly by gravity: oil, water and gas have different densities, and gradually separate after some time. Separating equipment on a ship usually uses swirl or centrifugal force instead, which reduces the reliance on gravity settling and also lets the equipment be made more compact."],
	"cx_coriolis": ["科氏流量计", "CORIOLIS FLOW METER"],
	"cx_coriolis_a": ["科氏流量计安装在管路上，内部有两根弯曲的测量管。设备运行时，激振器会让测量管持续振动，通过检测振动的变化，就能计算出流过管路的流体质量。", "A Coriolis flow meter is fitted on a line and has two bent measuring tubes inside. While the equipment runs, an exciter keeps the measuring tubes vibrating, and by detecting changes in the vibration, it can calculate the mass of fluid flowing through the line."],
	"cx_coriolis_b": ["流量计本身就是管路的一部分，如果直接拆卸，就相当于把整条管路从中间断开。如果管道里面还有压力或者残留液体，拆开法兰时就可能发生喷溅或泄漏。", "The flow meter is itself part of the line, and removing it directly amounts to breaking the whole line in the middle. If the pipe still holds pressure or leftover liquid, splashing or leaking may happen when the flanges are opened."],
	"cx_coriolis_c": ["拆卸之前，先关闭并隔离流量计所在的管路，确认内部已经完成泄压和排空，再松开连接法兰，将流量计拆卸下来。", "Before removal, first close and isolate the line the flow meter is on, confirm it has been depressurised and drained, then loosen the connecting flanges and take the flow meter off."],
	"cx_coriolis_x": ["流体经过正在振动的测量管时，会受到科里奥利力的影响，使测量管两端的振动产生相位差。流量计通过检测这个相位差，就能计算出实际的质量流量，部分高精度型号的测量精度可以达到 0.1% 左右，不过价格通常也比较高。", "When fluid passes through the vibrating measuring tubes, it is acted on by the Coriolis force, which makes the vibration at the two ends of the tubes differ in phase. By detecting this phase difference, the flow meter can calculate the actual mass flow, and some high-precision models reach a measuring accuracy of around 0.1%, though they are usually quite expensive."],
	"cx_level_radar": ["雷达液位计", "RADAR LEVEL GAUGE"],
	"cx_level_radar_a": ["雷达液位计安装在储罐顶部，由伸进罐内的喇叭形天线和外部的电子测量装置组成，可以用来测量储罐里面还剩下多少液体。", "A radar level gauge is fitted on top of a tank. It consists of a horn antenna reaching into the tank and electronic measuring equipment outside, and can measure how much liquid is left in the tank."],
	"cx_level_radar_b": ["液位计直接安装在储罐的接口上，如果罐内还有压力，拆卸液位计就相当于打开了一个没有封闭的罐口，里面残留的气体或者液体可能会突然喷出来。", "The level gauge is mounted directly on a tank connection. If the tank still holds pressure, removing the gauge amounts to opening an unsealed tank mouth, and the gas or liquid left inside may suddenly shoot out."],
	"cx_level_radar_c": ["拆卸之前，先通过液位计查看储罐里面还剩下多少液体，等罐内液体排空、压力完全释放，并确认设备已经处于安全状态以后，再拆卸液位计。", "Before removal, first use the level gauge to see how much liquid is left in the tank, and remove the gauge only after the liquid in the tank has been emptied, the pressure fully released, and the equipment confirmed to be in a safe state."],
	"cx_level_radar_x": ["雷达液位计通过天线向液面发射电磁波，再根据电磁波反射回来所花费的时间计算液位高度。在失重环境下，液体很难保持平整的液面，所以船上的液位计通常需要经过特殊设计和数据处理，才能估算出罐内的平均液位。", "A radar level gauge sends electromagnetic waves to the liquid surface through the antenna, and calculates the level height from the time the waves take to reflect back. In weightlessness, liquid can hardly keep a flat surface, so a gauge on a ship usually needs a special design and data processing to estimate the average level in the tank."],
	"cx_gauge_box": ["载荷传感器（应变片）", "LOAD CELL"],
	"cx_gauge_box_a": ["载荷传感器里面装有金属箔应变片，这些应变片固定在能够轻微变形的弹性体上，可以通过测量变形程度，判断设备结构目前承受了多大的力。", "A load sensor holds metal foil strain gauges, fixed on an elastic body that can deform slightly. By measuring how much it deforms, it can tell how much force the equipment structure is currently bearing."],
	"cx_gauge_box_b": ["如果传感器显示的载荷数值很高，就说明这部分结构还在承受较大的拉力或者压力。这时候直接切割或者拆卸，原本受到约束的部件可能会突然弹开，甚至造成附近的零件移位。", "If the load value shown by the sensor is high, this part of the structure is still bearing a large tension or compression. If you cut or remove it at this point, parts that were held under restraint may suddenly spring off, and even shift nearby parts."],
	"cx_gauge_box_c": ["拆卸之前，先查看载荷传感器的读数，确认这部分结构还有没有承受较大的力。如果读数仍然很高，就需要先卸除载荷，等数值降低到安全范围，并确认结构已经稳定以后，再开始拆卸。", "Before removal, first read the load sensor to see whether this part of the structure is still bearing a large force. If the reading is still high, you need to take the load off first, and start removal only after the value has dropped to a safe range and the structure is confirmed stable."],
	"cx_gauge_box_x": ["金属箔应变片受到拉伸或者压缩时，电阻会发生细微变化，惠斯通电桥可以把这些变化转换成电压信号，再由仪表计算出对应的载荷。承重结构、拉杆和铰链上安装的载荷传感器，可以帮助你判断哪些部件仍然处于受力状态，避免在拆卸时突然释放积累的弹性力。", "When a metal foil strain gauge is stretched or compressed, its resistance changes slightly. A Wheatstone bridge converts these changes into a voltage signal, and the instrument then calculates the matching load. Load sensors fitted on load-bearing members, tie rods and hinges can help you judge which parts are still under force, so that stored elastic force is not suddenly released during removal."],
	"cx_insp": ["现场仪表与传感器", "FIELD INSTRUMENTS"],
	"cx_insp_a": ["现场仪表和传感器安装在设备的不同位置，包括带有显示窗口的仪表、传感器节点和探测头。通过这些设备，可以查看管路压力、温度以及电路的运行状态。", "Field instruments and sensors are fitted at different positions on the equipment, including instruments with display windows, sensor nodes and detector heads. Through them you can check line pressure, temperature and the running state of circuits."],
	"cx_insp_b": ["仪表和传感器本身通常没有太大的危险，但它们经常直接连接着带压管路或者带电设备。如果没有提前处理，就直接拆卸，可能会造成气体泄漏，或者接触到仍然带电的线路。", "Instruments and sensors are usually not very dangerous themselves, but they are often connected directly to a pressurised line or live equipment. If you remove one without dealing with that first, gas may leak, or you may touch a line that is still live."],
	"cx_insp_c": ["拆卸之前，先查看仪表上的读数，确认设备目前的运行状态，再根据仪表连接的管路或者电路进行处理。如果管路还有压力，就需要先泄压；如果连接着带电线路，就需要先切断电源并确认断电，之后才能开始拆卸。", "Before removal, first read the instrument to confirm the equipment’s current running state, then deal with the line or circuit the instrument is connected to. If the line still has pressure, relieve it first; if it is connected to a live circuit, cut the power and confirm it is off, and only then start removal."],
	"cx_insp_x": ["现场仪表可以帮助你了解飞船各个设备目前的状态。控制面板上记录的可能是之前保存的数据，而现场仪表显示的是测量位置当前的数值。只要仪表还在正常工作，你就可以直接查看最新读数，判断设备的实际情况。", "Field instruments help you see the current state of the ship’s various equipment. What a control panel records may be earlier saved data, while a field instrument shows the current value at its measuring position. As long as the instrument is still working normally, you can read the latest value directly and judge the real condition of the equipment."],
	"cx_screw_comp": ["螺杆压缩机", "TWIN-SCREW COMPRESSOR"],
	"cx_screw_comp_a": ["里面有一对相互啮合的阴阳转子，还有电机、油分离器和油冷却器。", "It contains a pair of meshing male and female rotors, a motor, an oil separator and an oil cooler."],
	"cx_screw_comp_b": ["排气端和油分离器里面可能还留有高压气体，润滑油的温度也可能很高，直接拆卸会有危险。", "The discharge end and the oil separator may still hold high-pressure gas, and the lubricating oil may also be very hot, so removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_screw_comp_c": ["先关闭压缩机，等内部压力完全释放以后，再把润滑油排干净，确认没有残余压力后才能开始拆卸。", "First switch the compressor off, and once the internal pressure has been fully released, drain the lubricating oil, and start removal only after confirming there is no residual pressure."],
	"cx_screw_comp_x": ["电机带动两根螺旋转子转动，通过转子之间不断缩小的空间，把吸入的气体逐渐压缩，再从排气端送出去。氦压缩机主要负责给低温系统提供高压氦气，由于氦气价格很高，拆卸之前还得把里面的氦气回收好。", "The motor turns two helical rotors, and through the shrinking space between the rotors, the gas drawn in is gradually compressed and then sent out of the discharge end. A helium compressor mainly supplies high-pressure helium to a cryogenic system, and because helium is expensive, the helium inside must also be recovered before removal."],
	"cx_axial_comp": ["轴流压缩机", "AXIAL COMPRESSOR"],
	"cx_axial_comp_a": ["压缩机内部装着一排排交替排列的动叶片和静叶片，外面的机匣从前往后逐渐收窄。", "Inside the compressor there are rows of rotor blades and stator vanes arranged alternately, and the casing outside narrows gradually from front to back."],
	"cx_axial_comp_b": ["设备停机以后，内部转子可能还在继续转动，进气口也可能仍然连接着工艺气管道，拆卸前需要确认。", "After the equipment stops, the rotor inside may still be turning, and the inlet may also still be connected to the process gas line, so check before removal."],
	"cx_axial_comp_c": ["等转子完全停止转动，再确认进口管道已经隔离，完成以后才能开始拆卸。", "Wait until the rotor has stopped turning completely, then confirm the inlet line has been isolated, and only after that start removal."],
	"cx_axial_comp_x": ["气体每经过一级压缩，压力一般会提高到原来的 1.2～1.4 倍。叶片尖端的运动速度可以达到每秒几百米，如果叶片在高速转动时断裂，碎片就可能高速飞出，非常危险。", "Each stage of compression generally raises the gas pressure to 1.2–1.4 times what it was. The blade tips can move at several hundred metres per second, and if a blade breaks while spinning at high speed, the fragments may fly out at high speed, which is very dangerous."],
	"cx_turboexpander": ["透平膨胀机", "TURBOEXPANDER"],
	"cx_turboexpander_a": ["膨胀透平和制动压缩机安装在同一根转轴上，转轴由气体轴承支撑，设备运行时两边会一起转动。", "The expansion turbine and the brake compressor are mounted on the same shaft, which is supported by gas bearings, and the two sides turn together while the equipment runs."],
	"cx_turboexpander_b": ["这台设备运行时的转速可以达到每分钟几万转，内部还有温度很低的工艺气体。停机以后，设备内部可能仍然存在低温和残余压力，直接拆卸会有危险。", "While running, this equipment can reach several tens of thousands of revolutions per minute, and it holds process gas at a very low temperature. After it stops, low temperature and residual pressure may remain inside, and removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_turboexpander_c": ["先停止设备运行，等内部温度恢复到安全范围，再把剩余压力释放干净，确认转子已经完全停止转动以后，才能开始拆卸。", "First stop the equipment and wait until its internal temperature has returned to a safe range, then release the remaining pressure completely, and start removal only after confirming the rotor has stopped turning completely."],
	"cx_turboexpander_x": ["高压气体经过透平膨胀时，会带动叶轮转动并向外输出机械功，同时降低自身的温度，所以这种设备经常用在低温制冷和气体液化系统中。部分小型透平膨胀机的转速甚至可以超过每分钟 10 万转。", "When high-pressure gas expands through the turbine, it turns the impeller and puts out mechanical work, while its own temperature drops. This kind of equipment is therefore often used in cryogenic refrigeration and gas liquefaction systems. The rotation speed of some small turboexpanders can even exceed 100,000 revolutions per minute."],
	"cx_turbo_pump": ["分子泵", "TURBOMOLECULAR PUMP"],
	"cx_turbo_pump_a": ["分子泵内部装着一层层交替排列的转子叶片和定子叶片，运行时转子会高速旋转，让进入泵内的气体分子逐渐向出口方向移动。", "A molecular pump holds layers of rotor blades and stator blades arranged alternately. While running, the rotor spins at high speed and moves the gas molecules that enter the pump gradually towards the outlet."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_b": ["分子泵运行时的转速可以达到每分钟几万转，如果外部空气突然大量进入，可能会导致转子受损，严重时甚至会损坏整个泵体。", "A molecular pump can run at several tens of thousands of revolutions per minute, and if a large amount of outside air suddenly enters, the rotor may be damaged, and in serious cases the whole pump body may be wrecked."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_c": ["先关闭分子泵，等待内部转子完全停止转动，再按照操作要求缓慢放气，确认泵内压力恢复正常以后，才能拆卸连接法兰。", "First switch the molecular pump off and wait until the rotor inside has stopped turning completely, then vent the gas slowly as the operating requirements say, and unbolt the connecting flanges only after confirming the pressure in the pump is back to normal."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_x": ["分子泵通过高速旋转的叶片推动气体分子，叶片尖端的运动速度可以接近气体分子的热运动速度。这种泵需要在较低的气体压力下运行，还得配合前级泵一起使用。关闭设备以后，转子通常还需要几分钟才能完全停止转动。", "A molecular pump pushes gas molecules with blades spinning at high speed, and the speed of the blade tips can approach the thermal speed of the gas molecules. This kind of pump has to run at low gas pressure, and must be used together with a backing pump. After the equipment is switched off, the rotor usually still needs a few minutes to stop turning completely."],
	"cx_scroll_pump": ["涡旋泵", "SCROLL PUMP"],
	"cx_scroll_pump_a": ["泵的内部装着两个互相嵌套的螺旋盘，其中一个固定不动，另一个围绕固定螺旋盘做公转运动，通过不断缩小气体所在的空间来输送气体。", "Inside the pump there are two interleaved spiral scrolls. One is fixed, and the other orbits around the fixed scroll, moving gas by continually shrinking the space the gas occupies."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_b": ["这台泵输送的可能是价格昂贵的氦-3和氦-4混合气体，如果直接拆开管道，里面的气体就可能泄漏，造成不必要的损失。", "What this pump moves may be an expensive mixture of helium-3 and helium-4, and if you open the line directly, the gas inside may leak out and cause needless loss."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_c": ["拆卸之前，先把循环管道里的混合气体回收到储气容器中，确认回收完成以后，再停止设备运行并进行拆卸。", "Before removal, first recover the mixed gas in the circulation line into a gas storage vessel, and stop the equipment and remove it only after confirming recovery is complete."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_x": ["涡旋泵通过两个螺旋盘之间的相对运动来输送气体，运行时不需要使用润滑油接触气体，所以能够避免油污污染。稀释制冷机需要不断循环氦-3和氦-4混合气体，这种无油设计正好适合这种用途。", "A scroll pump moves gas through the relative motion of two spiral scrolls, and while running it does not need lubricating oil in contact with the gas, so it avoids oil contamination. A dilution refrigerator needs a helium-3 and helium-4 mixture circulating continuously, and this oil-free design suits that use exactly."],
	"cx_dry_cooler": ["干式冷却器", "DRY COOLER"],
	"cx_dry_cooler_a": ["这台设备装有 V 形排列的翅片盘管和一排散热风机，运行时风机会让空气经过盘管，把内部冷却液的热量带走。", "This equipment has finned coils arranged in a V and a row of cooling fans. While running, the fans draw air across the coils and carry away the heat of the coolant inside."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_b": ["盘管和连接管道里面可能还存有大量冷却液，如果没有提前排空，拆卸时就可能发生泄漏。", "The coils and the connected pipes may still hold a lot of coolant, and if it has not been drained beforehand, it may leak during removal."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_c": ["先关闭设备并隔离冷却液回路，再把盘管和管道里面剩余的冷却液排放干净，确认没有残余压力以后才能开始拆卸。", "First switch the equipment off and isolate the coolant circuit, then drain the coolant left in the coils and pipes, and start removal only after confirming there is no residual pressure."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_x": ["干式冷却器利用空气带走冷却液的热量，整个过程不需要通过蒸发水来散热。不过在没有空气的真空环境里，风机就起不到散热作用，只能依靠表面向外辐射热量，所以飞船上的干式冷却器一般安装在有空气的舱室里。", "A dry cooler uses air to carry away the heat of the coolant, and the whole process does not need water to be evaporated to shed heat. In the vacuum, where there is no air, however, the fans have no cooling effect, and heat can only be radiated away from the surface, so the dry coolers on a ship are generally fitted in rooms that hold air."],
	"cx_cdu": ["冷却液分配单元", "COOLANT DISTRIBUTION UNIT"],
	"cx_cdu_a": ["这套设备由板式换热器、两台循环泵、过滤器、膨胀罐和控制器组成，主要负责给机柜提供冷却液，并把设备运行时产生的热量传递到主冷却回路。", "This equipment consists of a plate heat exchanger, two circulation pumps, a filter, an expansion vessel and a controller. It mainly supplies coolant to the cabinets and passes the heat produced while the equipment runs on to the main cooling loop."],
	"cx_cdu_b": ["这套设备连接着整排机柜的冷却管道，内部可能还有大量冷却液和残余压力，如果直接拆卸，就可能造成冷却液泄漏。", "This equipment is connected to the coolant pipes of a whole row of cabinets, and may still hold a lot of coolant and residual pressure, and removing it directly may cause a coolant leak."],
	"cx_cdu_c": ["先停止循环泵运行并切断设备电源，再隔离对应的冷却回路，把管道和设备内部的冷却液排放干净，确认压力已经释放以后才能开始拆卸。", "First stop the circulation pumps and cut the equipment’s power, then isolate the matching cooling circuit and drain the coolant out of the pipes and the equipment, and start removal only after confirming the pressure has been released."],
	"cx_cdu_x": ["冷却液分配单元通过板式换热器，把机房主冷却回路和机柜内部的二次冷却回路分隔开，两边的冷却液不会直接混合，但热量仍然可以通过换热器传递。一台冷却液分配单元通常可以为数百千瓦的计算设备提供冷却服务。", "A coolant distribution unit uses a plate heat exchanger to separate the machine room’s main cooling loop from the secondary cooling loop inside the cabinets. The coolant on the two sides does not mix directly, but heat can still pass through the heat exchanger. One coolant distribution unit can usually provide cooling for computing equipment of several hundred kilowatts."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: propulsion
	"cx_eng_core": ["液体火箭发动机", "LIQUID ROCKET ENGINE"],
	"cx_eng_core_a": ["发动机主要由涡轮泵、燃气发生器、喷注器和带有再生冷却通道的燃烧室组成，这些部件连接在一起，负责输送推进剂并产生推力。", "An engine consists mainly of a turbopump, a gas generator, an injector and a combustion chamber with regenerative cooling channels. These parts are joined together and are responsible for delivering propellant and producing thrust."],
	"cx_eng_core_b": ["发动机停机以后，输送管道和燃烧室的冷却通道里可能还残留着推进剂。有些推进剂带有毒性，还有一些接触氧化剂以后就会自行燃烧，拆卸时需要特别注意。", "After an engine stops, propellant may still remain in the feed lines and in the cooling channels of the combustion chamber. Some propellants are toxic, and some ignite by themselves on contact with an oxidiser, so take special care during removal."],
	"cx_eng_core_c": ["先关闭推进剂主阀，通过排放口排空管道和冷却通道里残留的推进剂，确认已经完成排空和安全隔离以后，再开始拆卸发动机的推力架。", "First close the main propellant valves, drain the propellant left in the lines and cooling channels through the drains, and after confirming draining and safe isolation are complete, start removing the engine’s thrust frame."],
	"cx_eng_core_x": ["发动机工作时，燃料会先经过燃烧室壁内部的冷却通道，带走一部分热量以后再进入喷注器，所以即使发动机已经停机，冷却通道里也可能残留推进剂。肼类推进剂具有毒性，部分肼类燃料与特定氧化剂接触后还会自行燃烧。火箭发动机通常也是船上重量较大、价值较高的设备之一，拆卸时经常需要沿着法兰连接的位置分段处理。", "While the engine works, the fuel first passes through the cooling channels inside the combustion chamber wall, carries away part of the heat, and then enters the injector, so even after the engine stops, propellant may remain in the cooling channels. Hydrazine propellants are toxic, and some hydrazine fuels ignite by themselves on contact with certain oxidisers. A rocket engine is also usually one of the heavier and more valuable pieces of equipment on a ship, and when removing it, you often have to handle it in sections along the flange connections."],
	"cx_engine_s": ["挤压式小发动机", "PRESSURE-FED ENGINE"],
	"cx_engine_s_a": ["这种小型发动机依靠贮箱内部的气体压力，把推进剂送进燃烧室，主要由阀门、喷注头、燃烧室和喷管组成。", "This small engine relies on the gas pressure inside the tank to send propellant into the combustion chamber, and consists mainly of valves, an injector head, a combustion chamber and a nozzle."],
	"cx_engine_s_b": ["发动机停机以后，贮箱内部可能还保留着很高的压力，如果直接打开阀门，里面的推进剂就可能突然喷出来。", "After the engine stops, the tank may still hold very high pressure, and if you open a valve directly, the propellant inside may suddenly shoot out."],
	"cx_engine_s_c": ["先关闭推进剂供应阀门，按照规定排放贮箱内部的增压气体，确认压力已经降到安全范围，并且管道内没有残留的危险压力以后，再开始拆卸发动机。", "First close the propellant supply valves, vent the pressurant gas in the tank as the rules require, and start removing the engine only after confirming the pressure has dropped to a safe range and no dangerous residual pressure remains in the lines."],
	"cx_engine_s_x": ["这种发动机不需要使用涡轮泵，直接利用贮箱里的气体压力输送推进剂，所以整体结构比较简单，运行起来也比较可靠。不过贮箱需要承受较高的内部压力，对结构强度的要求也更高。小型飞船、着陆器和作业艇经常会使用这类发动机。", "This kind of engine needs no turbopump and moves propellant directly with the gas pressure in the tank, so its overall structure is fairly simple and it is fairly reliable to run. However, the tank has to bear high internal pressure, which also demands more structural strength. Small ships, landers and work tugs often use this kind of engine."],
	"cx_nozzle": ["喷管", "NOZZLE"],
	"cx_nozzle_a": ["钟形喷管主要由加强环、冷却管和喉部集管组成，整体呈现向外扩张的形状，用来让发动机产生的高温燃气加速排出。", "A bell nozzle consists mainly of stiffening rings, coolant tubes and a throat manifold. Its overall shape flares outwards, and it lets the high-temperature gas produced by the engine be expelled at high speed."],
	"cx_nozzle_b": ["喷管的体积很大，但外壁比较薄，搬运过程中受到碰撞就可能发生变形。内部的冷却管里也可能残留着冷却液，拆卸前需要检查。", "A nozzle is very large but its outer wall is fairly thin, so it may deform if it is knocked while being moved. The coolant tubes inside may also hold leftover coolant, which must be checked before removal."],
	"cx_nozzle_c": ["先把冷却管里残留的液体排放干净，再沿着法兰连接的位置拆卸喷管。搬运时要尽量放慢速度，避免喷管与周围的设备发生碰撞。", "First drain the liquid left in the coolant tubes, then unbolt the nozzle at the flange connection. Move it as slowly as you can, so the nozzle does not collide with the equipment around it."],
	"cx_nozzle_x": ["喷管通过让高温燃气不断膨胀，把燃气的一部分热能转化成高速运动的动能。对于适合真空环境的喷管来说，出口面积与喉部面积的比值越大，通常就能获得更高的比冲。部分真空喷管的扩张比可以超过 100，喷管壁也会做得很薄，所以拆卸和搬运时都需要格外小心。", "A nozzle lets the hot gas keep expanding and turns part of the gas’s heat energy into high-speed kinetic energy. For a nozzle suited to vacuum, the larger the ratio of exit area to throat area, the higher the specific impulse usually obtained. The expansion ratio of some vacuum nozzles can exceed 100, and the nozzle wall is also made very thin, so take extra care when removing and moving it."],
	"cx_rcs_quad": ["姿控推力器组", "RCS THRUSTER QUAD"],
	"cx_rcs_quad_a": ["一个安装座上装着四个小型推力器，每个推力器都配有电磁阀，组件内部还装有用于维持工作温度的加热片。", "Four small thrusters are fitted on one mounting block, each with a solenoid valve, and the assembly also holds heater pads that keep the working temperature."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_b": ["如果电磁阀还连接着电源，拆卸时意外触发就可能让推力器突然喷射。管道里面也可能残留推进剂，需要确认安全以后才能拆卸。", "If the solenoid valves are still connected to power, accidental triggering during removal may make a thruster suddenly fire. The lines may also hold leftover propellant, so removal must wait until it is confirmed safe."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_c": ["先切断推力器的电源，再关闭推进剂贮箱的阀门，通过排放口排空管道里残留的推进剂，确认管路已经没有压力以后，再开始拆卸推力器组。", "First cut the thrusters’ power, then close the valves of the propellant tank, drain the propellant left in the lines through the drain, and start removing the thruster cluster after confirming the lines have no pressure."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_x": ["使用单组元肼推进剂的推力器，会让肼经过内部的催化床，通过分解反应产生高温气体，再从喷口排出产生推力，单个推力器通常能提供几十牛到几百牛的推力。加热片负责让催化床保持在合适的工作温度，方便推力器在需要时正常启动。", "A thruster using monopropellant hydrazine passes the hydrazine through an internal catalyst bed, produces hot gas by a decomposition reaction, and sends it out of the nozzle to make thrust. One thruster can usually provide tens to hundreds of newtons of thrust. The heater pad keeps the catalyst bed at the right working temperature, so the thruster starts normally when needed."],
	"cx_turbopump": ["涡轮泵", "TURBOPUMP"],
	"cx_turbopump_a": ["燃料泵和氧化剂泵安装在同一根转轴上，中间装有一组涡轮，工作时由涡轮带动两侧的泵一起转动。", "The fuel pump and the oxidiser pump are mounted on the same shaft, with a turbine between them, and while working, the turbine drives the pumps on both sides round together."],
	"cx_turbopump_b": ["燃料和氧化剂都经过这台设备，停机以后，两侧的泵壳里可能还残留着推进剂。如果拆卸时发生泄漏，两种推进剂接触后就可能引起燃烧或爆炸。", "Both fuel and oxidiser pass through this equipment, and after it stops, propellant may remain in the casings of the pumps on both sides. If a leak happens during removal, the two propellants may burn or explode when they meet."],
	"cx_turbopump_c": ["拆卸之前，要分别排空燃料泵和氧化剂泵里的残留推进剂，确认两侧都已经排空并完成隔离以后，才能开始拆卸。", "Before removal, drain the residual propellant in the fuel pump and the oxidiser pump separately, and start removal only after confirming both sides have been drained and isolated."],
	"cx_turbopump_x": ["涡轮泵的体积虽然不大，功率却很高，一台只有几十公斤重的设备就能输出几兆瓦的功率，转速也能达到每分钟几万转。燃料和氧化剂之间依靠轴封隔离，一旦轴封损坏，两种推进剂就可能混合，严重时会直接引起爆炸。", "A turbopump is not large, but its power is very high: a unit weighing only a few tens of kilograms can put out several megawatts, at several tens of thousands of revolutions per minute. The fuel and oxidiser are kept apart by shaft seals, and once a shaft seal is damaged, the two propellants may mix, and in serious cases this causes an explosion directly."],
	"cx_apu": ["辅助动力装置", "AUXILIARY POWER UNIT"],
	"cx_apu_a": ["由小型燃气轮机、齿轮箱和发电机组成，可以在主发动机关闭时独立运行。", "It consists of a small gas turbine, a gearbox and a generator, and can run independently while the main engines are shut down."],
	"cx_apu_b": ["燃油管路里可能还有残留燃油，发电机也可能带电，直接拆卸会有危险。", "There may be fuel left in the fuel lines, and the generator may also be live, so removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_apu_c": ["拆卸之前，先关闭燃油供应，切断电源，再把管路里剩余的燃油排空，确认安全以后才能开始拆卸。", "Before removal, first shut off the fuel supply and cut the power, then drain the fuel left in the lines, and start removal only after confirming it is safe."],
	"cx_apu_x": ["APU 本身就是一台小型涡轮发动机，在主发动机没有运行的时候，它可以独立提供电力和气源，让飞机上的部分设备继续工作。", "An APU is itself a small turbine engine. While the main engines are not running, it can supply power and an air source on its own, so some equipment on the aircraft keeps working."],
	"cx_ntr_core": ["核热火箭堆芯", "NUCLEAR THERMAL ROCKET CORE"],
	"cx_ntr_core_a": ["由六角形燃料元件、铍反射层和控制鼓组成，反应堆通过核裂变产生高温，将氢气加热后从喷管喷出，为火箭提供推力。", "It consists of hexagonal fuel elements, a beryllium reflector and control drums. The reactor produces high temperature by nuclear fission, heats hydrogen, and expels it from the nozzle to give the rocket thrust."],
	"cx_ntr_core_b": ["反应堆关闭以后，堆芯仍然有很强的辐射，而且还会持续产生热量。在游戏中，如果使用激光切割到堆芯，就会直接引发核爆。", "After the reactor is shut down, the core still gives off strong radiation, and keeps producing heat. In the game, if you cut into the core with the laser, it causes a nuclear explosion directly."],
	"cx_ntr_core_c": ["拆卸时要待在辐射屏蔽区域内，等待堆芯充分冷却，再将控制鼓锁定，确认安全以后，把整个堆芯吊运出去。", "When removing it, stay inside the radiation shielded area, wait until the core has cooled fully, then lock the control drums, and after confirming it is safe, lift the whole core out."],
	"cx_ntr_core_x": ["核热火箭利用核裂变产生的热量，将氢气加热到 2500 K 以上，再通过喷管高速排出。它的比冲可以达到约 900 秒，差不多是普通化学火箭的两倍。反应堆关闭以后，堆芯还会产生衰变热，初期大约相当于满功率运行时的 1%，随后会随着时间逐渐降低。", "A nuclear thermal rocket uses the heat from nuclear fission to heat hydrogen to above 2500 K, and then expels it at high speed through a nozzle. Its specific impulse can reach about 900 seconds, roughly twice that of an ordinary chemical rocket. After the reactor is shut down, the core still produces decay heat, which at first is about 1% of the heat at full-power running, and then gradually falls with time."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: computing, sensing
	"cx_nav_rack": ["设备机架", "EQUIPMENT RACK"],
	"cx_nav_rack_a": ["标准的 19 英寸设备机架，里面装着配线架、交换机、服务器，最下面还有一台 UPS 不间断电源。", "A standard 19-inch equipment rack holding a patch panel, switches and servers, with a UPS (uninterruptible power supply) at the very bottom."],
	"cx_nav_rack_b": ["底部的 UPS 有独立供电能力，就算切断了主电源，机架里面的设备也可能继续带电。", "The UPS at the bottom has its own independent power. Even if the main supply is cut, the equipment in the rack may still be live."],
	"cx_nav_rack_c": ["先断开 UPS 的电源输出，确认设备断电以后，再拔掉连接线，把整个机架拆下来。", "First disconnect the UPS power output and confirm the equipment is dead. Then unplug the connecting cables and remove the whole rack."],
	"cx_nav_rack_x": ["UPS 平时会给内部电池充电，主电源断开以后，就能立即使用电池继续供电，一般可以维持几分钟到几小时。机架里的数据设备通常比较值钱，尽量保持完整，整套拆下来能卖得更贵。", "A UPS normally keeps its internal battery charged. When the main supply is disconnected, it switches to the battery at once and can usually keep running for anywhere from a few minutes to a few hours. Data equipment in a rack is generally valuable, so keep it intact: removing the whole rack sells for more."],
	"cx_nav": ["航电单元", "AVIONICS UNIT"],
	"cx_nav_a": ["一种机载电子设备，前面有显示屏、控制旋钮和两个把手，后面还有连接插头。", "An onboard electronics unit with a display, control knobs and two handles on the front, and connector plugs at the back."],
	"cx_nav_b": ["航电单元比较值钱，受到撞击后容易损坏。如果没有断开电源就直接拔掉插头，还可能损坏内部电路。", "Avionics units are fairly valuable and are easily damaged by impact. If the plugs are pulled out without cutting the power first, the internal circuits may also be damaged."],
	"cx_nav_c": ["先切断电源，再拔掉连接插头。拆卸的时候注意不要碰撞，尽量保持设备完整，最后送到设备回收口。", "First cut the power, then pull out the connector plugs. Avoid knocks while removing it, keep the unit intact, and finally send it to the equipment mouth."],
	"cx_nav_x": ["航电单元通常按照 ARINC 等航空标准设计，可以直接更换整个设备。前面板有两个方便拆装的把手，后面的接口可以直接对准机架插入，不需要单独连接每根线。", "Avionics units are usually built to aviation standards such as ARINC, so the whole unit can be replaced in one piece. The front panel has two handles for easy fitting and removal, and the rear connectors slot straight into the rack, so each wire does not need to be connected separately."],
	"cx_console": ["操作台", "OPERATOR CONSOLE"],
	"cx_console_a": ["一套完整的操作台，由底座、桌面、倾斜安装的显示面板、键盘和操纵杆组成。", "A complete console made up of a pedestal, a desktop, a sloped display panel, a keyboard and a joystick."],
	"cx_console_b": ["屏幕上显示的数据可能已经过期，设备的实际状态可能和显示结果不同，不能只看屏幕就判断设备是否安全。", "The data on the screen may be out of date, and the actual state of the equipment may differ from what is displayed. You cannot judge whether the equipment is safe from the screen alone."],
	"cx_console_c": ["先用检测工具确认设备的实际状态，不要完全相信屏幕上的数据。确认安全并切断电源以后，再把整个操作台拆下来。", "First use a measuring tool to confirm the actual state of the equipment, and do not fully trust the data on the screen. Once it is confirmed safe and the power is cut, remove the whole console."],
	"cx_console_x": ["操作台主要用来查看设备状态和发送控制指令，屏幕上显示的是传感器上一次传回的数据。如果传感器已经停止工作，或者通讯出现故障，屏幕上的数据就可能一直不更新。", "A console is mainly used to view equipment status and send control commands. The screen shows the data the sensors last reported. If a sensor has stopped working, or there is a communication fault, the data on the screen may never update."],
	"cx_blackbox": ["黑匣子（飞行记录仪）", "FLIGHT RECORDER"],
	"cx_blackbox_a": ["船上的飞行记录仪，外面有一层坚固的保护外壳，还装有水下定位信标和连接插头。", "The ship’s flight recorder, with a tough protective casing, an underwater locator beacon and a connector plug."],
	"cx_blackbox_b": ["有些合同要求完整回收黑匣子，如果拆卸时把它切坏了，就可能违反合同要求。", "Some contracts require the black box to be returned intact. If it is cut during removal, this may breach the contract."],
	"cx_blackbox_c": ["先松开固定螺栓，再把整个黑匣子拆下来，保持设备完整，送到设备回收口。", "First undo the fixing bolts, then remove the whole black box, keep the unit intact, and send it to the equipment mouth."],
	"cx_blackbox_x": ["黑匣子内部的存储器经过特殊保护，可以承受高达 3,400 g 的冲击，还能在 1,100℃ 的高温下坚持一小时。它保存着事故发生前的飞行数据，如果想知道这艘船以前出了什么事，可以从这里找到线索。", "The memory inside a black box is specially protected. It can withstand an impact of up to 3,400 g and survive an hour at 1,100 °C. It stores the flight data from before the accident, so if you want to know what happened to this ship, you can find clues here."],
	"cx_imu": ["惯性基准单元", "INERTIAL MEASUREMENT UNIT"],
	"cx_imu_a": ["用来测量飞船转动和加速度的精密设备，内部装有三个不同方向的环形激光陀螺和加速度计，底部还有减振装置。", "A precision unit for measuring the ship’s rotation and acceleration. Inside are three ring laser gyros facing different directions and accelerometers, with vibration isolators at the bottom."],
	"cx_imu_b": ["这套设备非常精密，价格也比较高。拆卸时如果受到撞击，内部的测量装置可能会失准，影响回收价值。", "This unit is very precise and fairly expensive. If it is knocked during removal, the measuring parts inside may go out of calibration, which reduces its recovery value."],
	"cx_imu_c": ["先切断电源，再松开固定装置，把整个惯性基准单元拆下来。搬运时尽量避免碰撞，保持设备完整。", "First cut the power, then release the fixings and remove the whole inertial reference unit. Avoid knocks while carrying it and keep the unit intact."],
	"cx_imu_x": ["环形激光陀螺利用两束反向传播的激光之间的频率差来测量转动，这种原理叫作萨格纳克效应。由于内部没有需要转动的机械部件，测量精度通常比较高。", "A ring laser gyro measures rotation using the frequency difference between two laser beams travelling in opposite directions. This principle is called the Sagnac effect. Because there are no rotating mechanical parts inside, its measuring accuracy is usually high."],
	"cx_star_tracker": ["星敏感器", "STAR TRACKER"],
	"cx_star_tracker_a": ["星敏感器由遮光罩、光学头和电子箱组成，通过拍摄星空来确定飞船当前的姿态。", "A star tracker is made up of a sun baffle, an optical head and an electronics box. It works out the ship’s current attitude by photographing the stars."],
	"cx_star_tracker_b": ["光学头很容易受到污染，拆卸时如果发生碰撞，也可能损坏里面的精密部件。", "The optical head is easily contaminated, and a knock during removal may also damage the precision parts inside."],
	"cx_star_tracker_c": ["切割时尽量离星敏感器远一点，避免损坏光学头，拆卸时要把整套设备完整取下来。", "When cutting, stay well away from the star tracker to avoid damaging the optical head, and remove the whole unit intact."],
	"cx_star_tracker_x": ["星敏感器会拍摄星空，再把照片里的星点位置和星表进行比对，从而计算出飞船的姿态，精度最高可以达到角秒级。前面的长遮光罩可以挡住太阳和其他明亮天体产生的散光，避免影响测量结果。", "A star tracker photographs the sky, then compares the positions of the stars in the picture with a star catalogue to calculate the ship’s attitude, with an accuracy of down to the arcsecond level. The long baffle at the front blocks stray light from the sun and other bright bodies, so it does not affect the measurement."],
	"cx_radar": ["抛物面天线", "DISH ANTENNA"],
	"cx_radar_a": ["一套大型天线设备，由反射面、馈源支架、副反射面和控制转动方向的方位轴、俯仰轴组成。", "A large antenna assembly made up of a reflector, feed supports, a subreflector, and an azimuth axis and an elevation axis that control its pointing direction."],
	"cx_radar_b": ["天线的反射面面积很大，而且比较薄，受到碰撞后很容易变形。发射机内部还可能存在高压电，拆卸前需要注意。", "The antenna reflector has a large area and is fairly thin, so it deforms easily when hit. The transmitter may also carry high voltage, so take care before removal."],
	"cx_radar_c": ["先断开发射机的电源，确认断电以后，再把整套天线拆下来。搬运的时候尽量放慢速度，避免反射面受到碰撞。", "First disconnect the transmitter’s power and confirm it is dead, then remove the whole antenna. Move it as slowly as you can when carrying it, so the reflector is not knocked."],
	"cx_radar_x": ["天线通过抛物面反射信号，对反射面的形状要求很高，误差一般要控制在波长的 1/16 以内。拿 X 波段来说，允许的误差大约只有 2 毫米。如果反射面发生变形，天线就只能按照废铝的价格回收了。", "The antenna reflects signals with a parabolic surface, so the shape of the reflector has to be very accurate, with the error generally kept within 1/16 of the wavelength. For X band, the permitted error is only about 2 mm. If the reflector is deformed, the antenna can only be recovered at the price of scrap aluminium."],
	"cx_xray_scanner": ["X 光扫描仪", "X-RAY SCANNER"],
	"cx_xray_scanner_a": ["用来检查物品内部结构的扫描设备，主要由 X 光发生器、探测器阵列、铅帘和传送带组成。", "A scanning unit for inspecting the internal structure of objects, made up mainly of an X-ray generator, a detector array, lead curtains and a conveyor belt."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_b": ["X 光发生器工作时会产生射线，内部还有高压电源。即使已经切断电源，电容器里也可能残留高压电。", "The X-ray generator emits radiation while running and contains a high-voltage supply. Even after the power is cut, the capacitors may still hold a high voltage."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_c": ["先切断设备电源，等待高压电容完成放电，确认没有残余电压以后，再开始拆卸。", "First cut the power to the unit and wait for the high-voltage capacitors to finish discharging. Start removal only after you have confirmed there is no residual voltage."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_x": ["X 光管会用 100～300 kV 的高压加速电子，让电子撞击内部靶材产生 X 射线。切断电源后，X 射线就会停止产生，但高压电容里可能还有电，所以拆卸前一定要完成放电。", "An X-ray tube uses a high voltage of 100–300 kV to accelerate electrons into an internal target, which produces X-rays. Once the power is cut, X-ray production stops, but the high-voltage capacitors may still hold a charge, so they must be discharged before removal."],
	"cx_biometric": ["生物识别终端", "BIOMETRIC PANEL"],
	"cx_biometric_a": ["用于控制门锁的身份验证设备，上面装有掌纹识别器、虹膜摄像头、输入键盘和显示门锁状态的指示灯。", "An identity verification unit that controls a door lock. It has a palm print reader, an iris camera, an input keypad and indicator lights showing the lock state."],
	"cx_biometric_b": ["门锁可能接有独立的备用电源，就算关闭了终端的电源，门锁也可能继续通电。", "The door lock may be wired to a separate backup power supply, so even if the terminal’s power is switched off, the lock may still be live."],
	"cx_biometric_c": ["先检查门锁连接了哪些电源，确认所有供电线路的状态以后，再处理门锁和终端。", "First check which power supplies the door lock is connected to, and confirm the state of every supply line. Only then deal with the lock and the terminal."],
	"cx_biometric_x": ["生物识别终端负责验证身份，真正控制门锁的是电磁铁或电机。有些门锁断电后会自动打开，有些则会保持锁定，具体要看它采用哪种设计。拆卸前最好先确认清楚，避免断电以后打不开门。", "The biometric terminal verifies identity, while what actually operates the door lock is a solenoid or motor. Some locks open automatically when power is lost, while others stay locked, depending on the design used. It is best to confirm this before removal, so the door cannot be left impossible to open after the power is cut."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: machinery
	"cx_hook": ["吊钩组", "HOOK BLOCK"],
	"cx_hook_a": ["吊钩组由夹板、滑轮、旋转接头和带有安全扣的吊钩组成，主要用来吊起和搬运重物。", "A hook block is made up of cheek plates, sheaves, a swivel and a hook with a safety latch. It is mainly used to lift and carry heavy loads."],
	"cx_hook_b": ["如果钢丝绳还处于绷紧状态，直接拆卸吊钩组可能会让钢丝绳突然弹回，伤到附近的人员。", "If the wire rope is still taut, removing the hook block directly may make the rope spring back suddenly and injure people nearby."],
	"cx_hook_c": ["先确认吊钩没有吊着重物，再松开绞车刹车，让钢丝绳慢慢放松，确认没有拉力以后再拆卸吊钩组。", "First confirm the hook is not carrying a load, then release the winch brake and let the wire rope slacken slowly. Remove the hook block only after confirming there is no tension."],
	"cx_hook_x": ["吊钩组利用多个滑轮来减小吊起重物时需要的拉力，承重的绳段越多，通常就越省力。不过钢丝绳在绷紧时会发生轻微拉伸，内部也会储存一定的弹性能，所以拆卸前一定要把拉力卸掉。", "A hook block uses several sheaves to reduce the pulling force needed to lift a load. The more rope segments carry the load, the less force is usually needed. However, a wire rope stretches slightly when taut and stores some elastic energy inside, so the tension must always be released before removal."],
	"cx_reel": ["绞盘与卷筒", "WINCH AND REEL"],
	"cx_reel_a": ["一种用来收放缆绳的设备，主要由卷筒、两侧的法兰、轮毂和带式刹车组成，卷筒上还缠绕着钢缆。", "A unit for paying out and hauling in cable, made up mainly of a drum, flanges on both sides, a hub and a band brake, with steel cable wound on the drum."],
	"cx_reel_b": ["钢缆受到拉力时会一直绷紧，如果这时候直接拆卸卷筒轴，卷筒可能突然转动或者甩出去，附近的设备也可能被损坏。", "A steel cable stays taut while it is under tension. If you remove the drum shaft at this point, the drum may suddenly turn or be thrown out, and nearby equipment may be damaged."],
	"cx_reel_c": ["先卸掉钢缆上的拉力，确认张力表已经归零，再拔出刹车销，最后拆卸卷筒轴。", "First take the tension off the steel cable and confirm the tension gauge has returned to zero. Then pull out the brake pins, and finally remove the drum shaft."],
	"cx_reel_x": ["钢缆受到拉力后会储存一部分弹性能，可以用公式 F²L/(2EA) 计算。拿一根承受几十千牛拉力的长钢缆来说，如果突然松开，释放的能量足以损坏设备，所以拆卸之前一定要查看张力表，确认钢缆已经不再受力。", "A steel cable under tension stores some elastic energy, which can be calculated with the formula F²L/(2EA). Take a long steel cable carrying a force of several tens of kilonewtons: if it is suddenly released, the energy let out is enough to damage equipment. So always check the tension gauge before removal and confirm the cable is no longer under load."],
	"cx_arm": ["机械臂", "MANIPULATOR ARM"],
	"cx_arm_a": ["机械臂由底座转台、肩部关节、大臂、小臂、液压油缸和末端夹爪组成，可以通过关节活动来调整夹爪的位置。", "A mechanical arm is made up of a base turntable, a shoulder joint, an upper arm, a lower arm, hydraulic cylinders and an end gripper. The position of the gripper is adjusted by moving the joints."],
	"cx_arm_b": ["机械臂折叠起来以后，液压系统和关节内部可能还存有压力。如果直接拆卸枢轴，机械臂可能突然弹开，伤到附近的人员。", "Once a mechanical arm is folded, there may still be pressure in the hydraulics and inside the joints. If a pivot is removed directly, the arm may suddenly spring open and injure people nearby."],
	"cx_arm_c": ["先释放蓄能器里的压力，再拆除各个关节的锁销，确认机械臂不会突然移动以后，最后拆卸枢轴。", "First release the pressure in the accumulator, then remove the locking pin of each joint. After confirming the arm cannot move suddenly, remove the pivots last."],
	"cx_arm_x": ["机械臂收起来以后，各个关节可能还承受着液压压力或预紧力，就算已经关闭电源，这些力量也不会立即消失。拆卸时要先释放储存的能量，再解除关节锁定，最后才能拆除连接结构。", "When a mechanical arm is folded, its joints may still be under hydraulic pressure or preload. Even if the power is already off, these forces do not disappear at once. When removing it, release the stored energy first, then release the joint locks, and only then remove the connecting structure."],
	"cx_dock": ["对接口", "DOCKING PORT"],
	"cx_dock_a": ["对接口由环形法兰、固定螺栓、捕获锁、导向瓣和舱门组成，用来连接两艘飞船。", "A docking port is made up of a ring flange, fixing bolts, capture latches, guide petals and a hatch, and is used to connect two ships."],
	"cx_dock_b": ["对接口后面的舱室可能还保持着内部气压，如果直接拆卸，舱内气体可能突然喷出。", "The compartment behind the docking port may still be under internal pressure. If it is removed directly, the gas inside may suddenly burst out."],
	"cx_dock_c": ["先检查对接口后面的舱室压力，确认已经完成泄压以后，再拆卸对接口。", "First check the pressure in the compartment behind the docking port, and remove the port only after confirming it has been vented."],
	"cx_dock_x": ["对接口既要承受两艘飞船连接时的受力，也要保证舱室不会漏气，所以连接处通常有几十颗固定螺栓和两道密封圈。对接时，导向瓣可以帮助两艘飞船对准位置，方便后续锁定。", "A docking port has to take the load when two ships are connected and also keep the compartment airtight, so the joint usually has several tens of fixing bolts and two seal rings. During docking, the guide petals help the two ships line up, making it easier to lock them together afterwards."],
	"cx_brake": ["盘式制动器", "DISC BRAKE"],
	"cx_brake_a": ["盘式制动器由卡钳、活塞、刹车片和油管组成，卡钳安装在制动盘边缘，通过夹紧制动盘来减慢转速。", "A disc brake is made up of a caliper, pistons, brake pads and a hydraulic line. The caliper is mounted on the edge of the brake disc and slows the rotation by clamping the disc."],
	"cx_brake_b": ["没有开启冷却就直接刹车，刹车片很容易因为温度过高而损坏。而且制动器连接的设备可能还在旋转，直接拆卸会有危险。", "If you brake without turning on cooling, the brake pads are easily damaged by excessive temperature. The equipment the brake is connected to may also still be rotating, so removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_brake_c": ["先开启制动冷却系统，再启动刹车，等设备完全停止旋转以后，才能拆卸制动器。", "First turn on the brake cooling system, then apply the brake. Remove the brake only after the equipment has stopped rotating completely."],
	"cx_brake_x": ["制动器通过刹车片和制动盘之间的摩擦，把旋转产生的动能转化成热量。就拿转速达到 20,000 rpm 的飞轮来说，要让它完全停下来，刹车片就得承受大量的热量。如果冷却效果不够好，刹车片的温度超过承受极限以后，制动器就可能失效，导致飞轮无法正常停止旋转。", "A brake turns kinetic energy from rotation into heat through friction between the brake pads and the brake disc. Take a flywheel spinning at 20,000 rpm: to bring it to a complete stop, the brake pads have to absorb a large amount of heat. If cooling is not good enough, once the pad temperature exceeds its limit the brake may fail, and the flywheel cannot be stopped properly."],
	"cx_lift": ["升降台", "SCISSOR LIFT"],
	"cx_lift_a": ["升降台由剪叉式支架、升降平台和底座组成，通过液压缸控制平台的升降。", "A lift table is made up of scissor supports, a lifting platform and a base. The platform is raised and lowered by hydraulic cylinders."],
	"cx_lift_b": ["升降台升起来以后，液压缸里面可能还保持着很高的压力，如果直接拆卸，平台可能突然下降。", "Once a lift table is raised, the hydraulic cylinders may still hold very high pressure. If the table is removed directly, the platform may suddenly drop."],
	"cx_lift_c": ["先把升降台降到最低位置，再释放液压系统里的压力，确认卸压完成以后才能开始拆卸。", "First lower the lift table to its lowest position, then release the pressure in the hydraulic system. Start removal only after confirming the pressure has been relieved."],
	"cx_lift_x": ["剪叉式支架通过液压缸推动来升降平台，支架接近折叠状态时，液压缸需要很大的推力才能把平台抬起来。拆卸前要让平台完全降到底部，再释放剩余压力，避免拆卸过程中发生意外。", "A scissor mechanism raises the platform by being pushed by the hydraulic cylinders. When the supports are close to folded, the cylinders need a very large thrust to lift the platform. Before removal, lower the platform fully to the bottom and then release the remaining pressure, to avoid accidents during removal."],
	"cx_hold_crane": ["货舱吊车", "HOLD CRANE"],
	"cx_hold_crane_a": ["货舱吊车由桥轨上的移动小车、卷扬电机和吊钩组成，可以沿着轨道移动，用来调整货物的位置。", "A hold crane is made up of a trolley on a bridge rail, a hoist motor and a hook. It moves along the rail and is used to adjust the position of cargo."],
	"cx_hold_crane_b": ["如果吊钩上还挂着货物，直接拆卸吊车可能导致货物掉落。拉杆如果还处于受力状态，直接切断也可能导致部件突然弹开。", "If the hook is still holding cargo, removing the crane directly may make the cargo drop. If a tie rod is still under load, cutting it directly may also make parts suddenly spring apart."],
	"cx_hold_crane_c": ["先把吊着的货物放下来，再松开受力的拉杆，确认没有剩余拉力以后，就可以拆卸吊车了。", "First set down the cargo being held, then release the tie rods that are under load. Once you have confirmed there is no remaining tension, you can remove the crane."],
	"cx_hold_crane_x": ["在失重环境下，货物虽然没有重量，但仍然具有惯性。吊车主要用来控制大型货物的移动方向和速度，避免货物在搬运过程中发生碰撞。", "In weightlessness, cargo has no weight but still has inertia. A crane is mainly used to control the direction and speed of large cargo, so that it does not collide with anything while being moved."],
	"cx_machine_tool": ["机床", "MACHINE TOOL"],
	"cx_machine_tool_a": ["机床主要分为车床和铣床，通常由床身、主轴、刀架或工作台等部分组成，可以用来加工金属零件。", "Machine tools are mainly divided into lathes and mills. They usually consist of a bed, a spindle, and a tool post or table, and are used to machine metal parts."],
	"cx_machine_tool_b": ["机床本身非常重，底部通常有多颗地脚螺栓固定，而且电机可能还带着电，直接拆卸容易发生危险。", "A machine tool is very heavy, and is usually fixed at the bottom with many hold-down bolts. Its motor may also still be live, so removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_machine_tool_c": ["先切断电源，再拆除底部的地脚螺栓。如果整台机床太重，就按照标记的位置分段拆卸。", "First cut the power, then undo the hold-down bolts at the bottom. If the whole machine tool is too heavy, split it into sections along the marked positions."],
	"cx_machine_tool_x": ["机床值钱的地方主要在加工精度，所以拆卸的时候要尽量保护导轨和主轴。如果导轨磨损严重，或者在拆卸时受到撞击发生变形，机床就很难继续使用，最后可能只能按照废铁的价格回收。", "A machine tool is valuable mainly for its machining accuracy, so protect the ways and the spindle as much as possible during removal. If the ways are badly worn, or are deformed by a knock during removal, the machine tool can hardly be used any more, and may end up recovered only at the price of scrap iron."],
	"cx_vehicle": ["车辆", "VEHICLE"],
	"cx_vehicle_a": ["固定在甲板上的汽车、叉车、牵引车或者其他作业车辆，通常会使用绑带和轮挡来固定位置。", "Cars, forklifts, tractors and other work vehicles fixed to the deck. They are usually held in place with straps and wheel chocks."],
	"cx_vehicle_b": ["车辆内部可能还有电池或者燃料，如果固定车辆的绑带松开，车辆就可能在舱室里滑动，撞坏附近的设备。", "A vehicle may still hold a battery or fuel inside. If the straps holding it are released, the vehicle may slide around the compartment and smash nearby equipment."],
	"cx_vehicle_c": ["可以把整辆车直接运到回收口。如果需要拆解，就先处理车内的电池和燃料，确认安全以后再开始拆卸。", "You can take the whole vehicle straight to the recovery mouth. If it needs to be taken apart, deal with the battery and fuel inside first, and start removal after confirming it is safe."],
	"cx_vehicle_x": ["完整车辆通常比拆成废金属更值钱，所以有条件的话最好整辆回收。在失重环境下，车辆本身的重量无法让它停在甲板上，需要依靠绑带和轮挡来限制移动。", "A whole vehicle is usually worth more than the same vehicle broken into scrap metal, so recover it whole if you can. In weightlessness, the vehicle’s own weight cannot keep it on the deck, so straps and wheel chocks are needed to restrict its movement."],
	"cx_cargo": ["货柜与货箱", "CONTAINERS AND CRATES"],
	"cx_cargo_a": ["用来装运货物的标准集装箱或木框货箱，回收价格根据里面申报的货物来计算。", "Standard shipping containers or wooden-framed crates. The recovery price is calculated from the cargo declared inside."],
	"cx_cargo_b": ["货箱通常比较重，搬运时很难立即停下来。冷藏货箱和居住货箱内部还可能存在压力，直接拆开会有危险。", "Cargo boxes are usually heavy, so they are hard to stop at once when being moved. Reefer containers and accommodation boxes may also hold pressure inside, and opening them directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_cargo_c": ["搬运前先查看货箱的重量，太重的话可以使用搬运无人机，或者升级抓钩。有内部压力的货箱需要先释放压力，再进行搬运。", "Before moving a box, check its mass first. If it is too heavy, use the hauler drone or upgrade the grapple. A box with internal pressure must have the pressure released before it is moved."],
	"cx_cargo_x": ["标准集装箱主要通过四个角上的角件来固定和承受搬运载荷，箱子之间可以用扭锁连接。货箱里面的货物通常比箱体本身更值钱，尽量保持整箱完整，可以卖出更高的价格。", "A standard shipping container is held and takes handling loads mainly through the corner castings at its four corners, and containers can be joined to one another with twist-locks. The cargo inside a box is usually worth more than the box itself, so keep a full box intact where possible, and it will sell for a higher price."],
	"cx_uav": ["维护无人机", "MAINTENANCE DRONE"],
	"cx_uav_a": ["一台停放在机位里的小型维护无人机，机身装有四个旋翼，前面还有用于观察周围环境的传感器。", "A small maintenance drone parked in its bay. Its body has four rotors, and at the front there are sensors for observing its surroundings."],
	"cx_uav_b": ["无人机有自己的电池，即使飞船已经断电，它也可能突然启动旋翼，如果没有固定好，就有可能直接飞出去。", "The drone has its own battery. Even when the ship has lost power, it may suddenly start its rotors, and if it is not secured, it may fly straight out."],
	"cx_uav_c": ["先断开停机位的充电电源，再关闭无人机的电池开关，取下电池包以后，就可以把无人机搬走了。", "First disconnect the charging supply to the bay, then switch off the drone’s battery switch. Once the battery pack has been removed, you can carry the drone away."],
	"cx_uav_x": ["部分无人机在触发断电保护或自动返航程序时，可能会尝试启动旋翼。如果电池还连接着，机身又没有固定好，旋翼突然转动就可能让无人机直接冲出机位，所以拆卸前一定要先断开电池。", "Some drones may try to start their rotors when power-loss protection or an automatic return-home routine is triggered. If the battery is still connected and the body is not secured, the rotors suddenly spinning may make the drone shoot straight out of its bay, so always disconnect the battery before removal."],
	"cx_stator": ["直线电机定子", "LINEAR MOTOR STATOR"],
	"cx_stator_a": ["直线电机的固定部分，里面有叠片铁芯和安装在凹槽里的线圈，两端还能看到露出来的线圈绕组。", "The fixed part of a linear motor. Inside are a laminated iron core and coils fitted in slots, and the end windings sticking out can be seen at both ends."],
	"cx_stator_b": ["定子的电源来自电容组，就算切断了主电源，电容组里也可能存着几百伏的高压电，直接拆卸会有触电危险。", "The stator is powered from a capacitor bank. Even if the main supply is cut, the capacitor bank may still hold a high voltage of several hundred volts, and removing it directly risks an electric shock."],
	"cx_stator_c": ["先把电容组里的电放干净，确认没有残余电压以后，再断开线路并拆卸线圈。", "First discharge the capacitor bank completely. After confirming there is no residual voltage, disconnect the wiring and remove the coils."],
	"cx_stator_x": ["直线电机的工作原理和普通旋转电机差不多，只是定子沿着轨道铺开，通电以后会产生沿轨道移动的磁场，推动动子向前运动。电磁弹射系统就利用这个原理，能在短短几秒内把载荷加速到每秒几百米。", "A linear motor works in much the same way as an ordinary rotary motor, except that the stator is laid out along a track. When powered, it produces a magnetic field that travels along the track and pushes the mover forward. Electromagnetic launch systems use this principle to accelerate a payload to several hundred metres per second in just a few seconds."],
	"cx_launch_cradle": ["发射滑架", "LAUNCH CRADLE"],
	"cx_launch_cradle_a": ["发射滑架安装在轨道上，由滑橇、支撑托垫和释放锁组成，发射时会沿着轨道移动。", "A launch cradle is mounted on rails and is made up of a sled, support pads and release latches. It moves along the rails during launch."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_b": ["轨道可能还保留着预紧力，如果直接打开释放锁，滑架可能会突然弹出去。", "The rails may still hold preload. If the release latches are opened directly, the cradle may suddenly shoot out."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_c": ["先释放轨道上的预紧力，确认滑架不会突然移动以后，再进行拆卸。", "First release the preload on the rails, and remove the cradle only after confirming it cannot suddenly move."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_x": ["发射时，滑架需要承受几十倍重力加速度带来的载荷，所以整体结构比较厚重，需要有足够的强度才能承受发射时的冲击。", "During launch, the cradle has to take a load from an acceleration of several tens of g, so its overall structure is thick and heavy and needs enough strength to withstand the shock of launch."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor": ["飞轮储能器", "FLYWHEEL STORE"],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_a": ["飞轮储能器的外壳内部是真空环境，里面装着复合材料飞轮、磁悬浮轴承，还有一套可以发电和驱动飞轮旋转的电机。", "The housing of a flywheel energy store is a vacuum inside. It holds a composite-material flywheel, magnetic bearings and a motor that can both generate power and drive the flywheel."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_b": ["飞轮可能还在高速旋转，这时候直接松开固定装置或者切割外壳，里面的飞轮可能会飞出去，造成严重损坏。", "The flywheel may still be spinning at high speed. If the fixings are released or the housing is cut at this point, the flywheel inside may fly out and cause serious damage."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_c": ["先启动刹车冷却系统，再使用刹车降低飞轮转速，等转速降到 300 rpm 以下以后，才能开始拆卸。", "First start the brake cooling system, then use the brake to slow the flywheel. Start removal only after its speed has dropped below 300 rpm."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_x": ["飞轮通过高速旋转来储存能量，计算公式是 E = ½Iω²，储存的能量和转速的平方成正比。拿同一个飞轮来说，转速达到 20,000 rpm 时，储存的能量就是 2,000 rpm 时的 100 倍。由于内部采用了真空环境和磁悬浮轴承，旋转阻力很小，就算不再供电，也能继续旋转好几天。", "A flywheel stores energy by spinning at high speed. The formula is E = ½Iω², so the stored energy is proportional to the square of the speed. For the same flywheel, at 20,000 rpm the stored energy is 100 times that at 2,000 rpm. Because of the vacuum inside and the magnetic bearings, rotational drag is very small, and even without power the flywheel can keep spinning for several days."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel": ["反作用飞轮", "REACTION WHEEL"],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_a": ["反作用飞轮里面装有飞轮、轴承和电机线圈，飞船可以通过调整飞轮的转速来改变自身的姿态。", "A reaction wheel contains a flywheel, bearings and motor coils. The ship can change its attitude by adjusting the speed of the wheel."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_b": ["即使已经关闭电源，里面的飞轮也可能还在高速旋转，直接拆卸可能造成设备损坏。", "Even after the power is switched off, the wheel inside may still be spinning at high speed, and removing it directly may damage the equipment."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_c": ["拆卸之前先检查飞轮的转速，确认飞轮已经完全停止旋转以后，再拆下整个设备。", "Before removal, check the speed of the wheel first. Remove the whole unit only after confirming the wheel has stopped spinning completely."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_x": ["反作用飞轮利用角动量守恒来控制飞船姿态。当电机带动飞轮向一个方向加速旋转时，飞船就会受到反方向的转动力矩，从而调整姿态。飞轮的正常工作转速通常可以达到每分钟几千转。", "A reaction wheel uses conservation of angular momentum to control the ship’s attitude. When the motor spins the wheel up in one direction, the ship receives a torque in the opposite direction and so changes its attitude. The normal operating speed of the wheel can usually reach several thousand revolutions per minute."],
	"cx_despin_brake": ["消旋制动器", "DESPIN BRAKE"],
	"cx_despin_brake_a": ["安装在旋转居住环轮毂上的制动装置，主要由制动盘、卡钳和散热片组成，用来降低居住环的旋转速度。", "A braking unit mounted on the hub of a rotating habitat ring, made up mainly of a brake disc, calipers and cooling fins. It is used to reduce the rotation speed of the ring."],
	"cx_despin_brake_b": ["如果居住环上的设备还在用电，直接启动刹车可能产生过大的回馈电流，烧坏供电滑环。如果没有开启冷却系统，刹车产生的高温还可能损坏制动器。", "If equipment on the habitat ring is still drawing power, applying the brake directly may produce an excessive regenerated current and burn out the power slip ring. If the cooling system is not turned on, the high temperature produced by braking may also damage the brake."],
	"cx_despin_brake_c": ["先切断居住环上所有设备的电源，再开启制动器的冷却系统，确认准备完成以后，同时对两个居住环进行制动。", "First cut the power to all equipment on the habitat ring, then turn on the brake’s cooling system. Once everything is ready, brake both habitat rings at the same time."],
	"cx_despin_brake_x": ["制动时，电机可以把居住环旋转产生的动能转化成电能，储存在电容器里，这个过程叫再生制动。等电容器充满以后，需要先释放里面的电能，才能继续使用这种制动方式。两个居住环需要一起减速，如果只刹住其中一个，另一个居住环的角动量可能让船体发生扭转。", "During braking, the motor can convert the kinetic energy of the ring’s rotation into electrical energy and store it in a capacitor. This process is called regenerative braking. Once the capacitor is full, its energy must be released before this braking method can continue. The two habitat rings need to slow down together: if only one is braked, the angular momentum of the other ring may twist the hull."],
	"cx_rotary_seal": ["旋转气密封", "ROTARY SEAL"],
	"cx_rotary_seal_a": ["安装在旋转轮毂和固定主轴之间的密封装置，用来减少两者之间的气体泄漏。", "A sealing device fitted between the rotating hub and the fixed spine, used to reduce gas leakage between the two."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_b": ["如果轮毂还在旋转，就直接打开过渡气闸，可能会把里面的密封结构撕坏。", "If the transfer airlock is opened while the hub is still turning, the sealing structure inside may be torn apart."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_c": ["先让轮毂完全停止旋转，再锁定轴承，确认固定好以后才能开始拆卸。", "First let the hub stop turning completely, then lock the bearing. Start removal only after confirming it is secured."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_x": ["迷宫密封内部有很多圈密封齿，气体经过这些位置时，流动阻力会逐渐增加，从而减少泄漏。中间还有缓冲气槽，可以隔开两侧的气体。由于密封结构之间没有直接接触，所以轮毂旋转的时候也能保持密封，不过如果出现了较大的开口，气体还是会直接泄漏。", "A labyrinth seal has many rings of sealing teeth inside. As gas passes through them, the flow resistance builds up step by step, which reduces leakage. In the middle there is also a buffer-gas groove that separates the gas on the two sides. Because the sealing parts do not touch each other, the seal holds even while the hub turns, but if a large opening appears, the gas will still leak straight out."],
	"cx_spoke_lift": ["轮辐电梯", "SPOKE ELEVATOR"],
	"cx_spoke_lift_a": ["安装在旋转环轮辐上的电梯，轿厢通过导轨和齿条上下移动，配有舱门、驱动电机和防止轿厢失控的安全钳。", "A lift fitted on the spoke of a rotating ring. The car moves up and down on guide rails and a rack, and has doors, a drive motor and safety gear that stops the car running away."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_b": ["旋转环还在转动的时候，轿厢会受到离心力的影响。如果这时候切断导轨，轿厢可能会直接被甩出去。", "While the rotating ring is still turning, the car is affected by centrifugal force. If the guide rail is cut at this point, the car may be flung straight off."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_c": ["先让旋转环停止转动，确认轿厢已经停稳以后，再开始拆卸电梯。", "First stop the rotating ring from turning, and start removing the lift only after confirming the car has come to a steady stop."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_x": ["旋转环通过转动产生离心力，让里面的人感觉到类似重力的效果。拿半径 100 米的旋转环来说，每分钟转动 3 圈，就能产生大约 1 g 的人工重力。电梯从中央轮毂移动到外环的过程中，乘客感受到的人工重力也会从接近零逐渐增加到 1 g。", "A rotating ring produces centrifugal force by turning, which gives the people inside an effect like gravity. For a ring with a radius of 100 m, turning 3 times per minute produces about 1 g of artificial gravity. As the lift moves from the central hub out to the outer ring, the artificial gravity felt by passengers also rises gradually from nearly zero to 1 g."],
	"cx_tether_damper": ["系绳阻尼器", "TETHER DAMPER"],
	"cx_tether_damper_a": ["由液压缸、弹簧和气囊组成的装置，用来减少系绳在工作时产生的振动。", "A device made up of a hydraulic cylinder, a spring and a gas bag, used to reduce the vibration produced in a tether while it is working."],
	"cx_tether_damper_b": ["系绳如果还处于拉紧状态，阻尼器就会承受很大的拉力，内部的弹簧和气囊也可能储存着压力，直接拆卸容易发生意外。", "If the tether is still taut, the damper takes a very large pulling force, and the spring and gas bag inside may also hold stored pressure, so removing it directly may cause an accident."],
	"cx_tether_damper_c": ["先停止系绳转动，再松开张紧器，确认系绳已经放松以后，再开始拆卸阻尼器。", "First stop the tether from turning, then release the tensioner. Start removing the damper only after confirming the tether has gone slack."],
	"cx_tether_damper_x": ["系绳太长时容易产生振动，原理和拉紧的琴弦差不多。阻尼器可以利用液压结构吸收振动产生的能量，并将这些能量转化成热量，减少系绳的晃动。", "A tether that is too long tends to vibrate, in much the same way as a taut string. The damper can use its hydraulic structure to absorb the energy of the vibration and convert it into heat, reducing the swaying of the tether."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp": ["液压夹钳", "HYDRAULIC CLAMP"],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_a": ["液压夹钳由固定钳口、液压缸控制的活动钳口和底部安装板组成，主要用来夹紧和固定设备。", "A hydraulic clamp is made up of a fixed jaw, a moving jaw controlled by a hydraulic cylinder and a base mounting plate. It is mainly used to clamp and hold equipment in place."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_b": ["液压夹钳即使停止工作，内部也可能还有压力。如果没有泄压就直接拆卸，钳口可能突然弹开，撞坏附近的设备。", "Even when a hydraulic clamp has stopped working, there may still be pressure inside. If it is removed without relieving the pressure, the jaw may suddenly spring open and smash nearby equipment."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_c": ["拆卸之前先打开保压开关，把内部剩余的压力释放掉，确认泄压完成以后再拆卸夹钳。", "Before removal, turn on the holding switch and release the remaining pressure inside. Remove the clamp only after confirming the pressure has been relieved."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_x": ["液压夹钳通过液压锁保持夹紧状态，即使液压泵停止工作，内部压力也能维持很长时间。如果有多个夹钳共同固定一件设备，拆卸时还要注意松开的顺序，因为每松开一个夹钳，剩下的夹钳就需要承担更多载荷。", "A hydraulic clamp keeps its clamping state with a hydraulic lock, so even if the hydraulic pump stops, the internal pressure can be maintained for a long time. When several clamps hold one piece of equipment together, the order of release also matters during removal, because each time a clamp is released, the remaining clamps have to carry more load."],
	"cx_iso_table": ["隔振台", "VIBRATION ISOLATION TABLE"],
	"cx_iso_table_a": ["一种用来放置精密设备的工作台，上面是蜂窝结构的台面，下面装着气动隔振支腿，还有用来调整台面高度的水平阀。", "A workbench for holding precision equipment. It has a honeycomb tabletop on top, pneumatic isolation legs underneath, and levelling valves for adjusting the height of the tabletop."],
	"cx_iso_table_b": ["隔振台没有锁定的时候，如果在附近进行切割或者发生碰撞，台面可能会产生晃动，导致上面的精密设备受到损坏。", "When an isolation table is not locked, cutting or a collision nearby may make the tabletop shake, which can damage the precision equipment on it."],
	"cx_iso_table_c": ["先把隔振台锁定，确认台面已经固定好以后，再开始切割附近的结构。", "First lock the isolation table, and start cutting the nearby structure only after confirming the tabletop is secured."],
	"cx_iso_table_x": ["隔振台通过气动支腿减少外部振动的影响，可以把几赫兹以上的振动降低到原来的 1% 以下。锁定以后，台面会和支架固定在一起，不能继续自由晃动，可以避免拆卸时因为台面移动而损坏设备。", "An isolation table uses pneumatic legs to reduce the effect of outside vibration, and can cut vibration above a few hertz to less than 1% of its original level. Once locked, the tabletop is fixed to the frame and can no longer sway freely, which avoids damaging the equipment through tabletop movement during removal."],
	"cx_escape_pod": ["救生舱", "ESCAPE POD"],
	"cx_escape_pod_a": ["安装在发射架上的救生舱，外面有防热罩和侧舱门，里面装着乘员座椅，底部还有制动火箭和发射夹。", "An escape pod mounted on a launch cradle. It has a heat shield and a side hatch outside, crew seats inside, and a retro-rocket pack and launch clamps at the bottom."],
	"cx_escape_pod_b": ["发射夹里面装有火工品，如果待发电路还在通电，救生舱就有可能意外弹出，拆卸的时候要特别注意。", "The launch clamps contain pyrotechnic charges. If the arming circuit is still powered, the pod may be ejected by accident, so take special care during removal."],
	"cx_escape_pod_c": ["先断开待发开关，确认发射电路已经断电以后，再拆卸发射夹和里面的火工品。", "First switch off the arming switch, and confirm the launch circuit is dead. Then remove the launch clamps and the pyrotechnic charges inside."],
	"cx_escape_pod_x": ["爆炸螺栓内部装有少量炸药，只需要几安培的电流持续几毫秒，就能完成起爆。发射电容使用独立的供电回路，即使主电源已经断开，也可能保留足够的电能来触发爆炸螺栓。", "An explosive bolt contains a small amount of explosive, and a current of only a few amps lasting a few milliseconds is enough to set it off. The launch capacitor uses a separate supply circuit, so even if the main power is already disconnected, it may keep enough energy to fire the explosive bolts."],
	"cx_safe_deposit": ["保管箱墙与库门", "VAULT AND DEPOSIT BOXES"],
	"cx_safe_deposit_a": ["一整面墙的密封保管箱，或者装有机械锁栓的厚重库门。", "A whole wall of sealed deposit boxes, or a thick vault door with mechanical locking bolts."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_b": ["库门的电磁锁可能还在通电，库房内部也可能存在残余气压，直接开门会有危险。", "The vault door’s electromagnetic lock may still be powered, and there may also be residual pressure inside the vault, so opening the door directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_c": ["先切断门锁的所有供电线路，再释放库房内部的压力，确认安全以后打开库门，尽量把保管箱完整拆下来运走。", "First cut every power supply line to the door lock, then release the pressure inside the vault. Once it is confirmed safe, open the door and take the deposit boxes out whole where possible."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_x": ["库门使用电磁铁控制锁栓，只要还有一路电源接通，机械释放杆就无法扳动。所有电源断开以后，锁栓仍然会保持在原来的位置，需要手动扳动释放杆才能把锁栓收回去。", "The vault door uses a solenoid to control its locking bolts, and as long as any one supply is still connected, the mechanical release lever cannot be pulled. After all supplies are disconnected, the bolts still stay in their original position, and the release lever has to be pulled by hand to retract them."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: nuclear
	"cx_pwr_core": ["压水堆", "PRESSURISED-WATER REACTOR"],
	"cx_pwr_core_a": ["压水堆的主体包括压力容器、顶部的螺栓环、控制棒驱动管、堆芯和下腔室。", "The main body of a pressurised-water reactor includes the pressure vessel, the stud ring on top, the control rod drive housings, the core and the lower plenum."],
	"cx_pwr_core_b": ["即使反应堆已经停止运行，内部仍然有很强的辐射，而且会持续产生热量。一次冷却回路里的水也处于高温高压状态，拆卸时要特别小心。", "Even after the reactor has stopped running, there is still strong radiation inside, and it keeps producing heat. The water in the primary cooling loop is also at high temperature and high pressure, so take special care during removal."],
	"cx_pwr_core_c": ["先保持冷却系统正常运行，等反应堆的温度降下来以后，再做好辐射屏蔽措施，将整个设备拆下来，通过危险品出口运走。", "First keep the cooling system running normally and wait for the reactor temperature to drop. Then put radiation shielding measures in place, remove the whole unit, and send it out through the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_pwr_core_x": ["压水堆的一次冷却回路通常保持在 15.5 MPa 左右，水温可以达到 315℃，由于内部压力很高，水在这个温度下仍然不会沸腾。反应堆停止运行一小时后，衰变热大约还有额定热功率的 1.5%，一天后也有约 0.5%。拿一座热功率为 100 MW 的反应堆来说，即使停堆一天，内部仍然会持续产生大约 0.5 MW 的热量，所以冷却系统还得继续运行。", "The primary cooling loop of a pressurised-water reactor is usually kept at about 15.5 MPa, and the water temperature can reach 315 °C. Because the internal pressure is so high, the water still does not boil at this temperature. One hour after the reactor stops, the decay heat is still about 1.5% of rated thermal power, and about 0.5% after one day. Take a reactor with a thermal power of 100 MW: even a day after shutdown it still keeps producing about 0.5 MW of heat, so the cooling system has to keep running."],
	"cx_crdm": ["控制棒驱动机构", "CONTROL ROD DRIVE"],
	"cx_crdm_a": ["用来控制反应堆控制棒位置的设备，主要由耐压外壳、提升线圈、保持线圈、棒位指示装置和驱动杆组成。", "A unit for controlling the position of the reactor control rods, made up mainly of a pressure-tight housing, lift coils, hold coils, a rod position indicator and a drive rod."],
	"cx_crdm_b": ["这套机构也是反应堆一回路压力边界的一部分，如果一回路还没有泄压，直接拆卸可能导致高温冷却剂喷出。", "This mechanism is also part of the reactor’s primary loop pressure boundary. If the primary loop has not been depressurised, removing it directly may make high-temperature coolant spray out."],
	"cx_crdm_c": ["先给反应堆一回路泄压，等冷却剂温度降下来以后，再拆卸控制棒驱动机构。", "First depressurise the reactor primary loop, and remove the control rod drive mechanism after the coolant temperature has dropped."],
	"cx_crdm_x": ["磁力提升式驱动机构通过电磁线圈控制控制棒的位置，一旦失去电源，机构就会释放控制棒，让控制棒依靠重力落入堆芯，使反应堆自动停堆。这种设计叫作失电安全。", "A magnetic-jack drive mechanism controls the position of the control rods with electromagnetic coils. Once power is lost, the mechanism releases the rods, and they drop into the core under gravity, so the reactor shuts down automatically. This design is called fail-safe."],
	"cx_rcp": ["主冷却剂泵", "REACTOR COOLANT PUMP"],
	"cx_rcp_a": ["负责让冷却剂在反应堆内部循环的设备，主要由屏蔽电机、飞轮、密封组件和泵壳组成。", "A unit that circulates coolant through the reactor, made up mainly of a canned motor, a flywheel, a seal package and a pump casing."],
	"cx_rcp_b": ["主冷却剂泵负责维持堆芯的冷却循环，如果反应堆还没有充分冷却就切断电源，冷却剂流量会逐渐下降，堆芯温度可能再次升高。", "The reactor coolant pump keeps the core cooling circulation going. If the power is cut before the reactor has cooled enough, the coolant flow gradually falls and the core temperature may rise again."],
	"cx_rcp_c": ["先让反应堆完成停堆和冷却，确认堆芯温度已经降到安全范围以后，再切断主冷却剂泵的电源。", "First let the reactor finish shutting down and cooling, and cut the power to the reactor coolant pump only after confirming the core temperature has dropped to a safe range."],
	"cx_rcp_x": ["主冷却剂泵上的飞轮可以在断电以后继续带动泵转动，让冷却剂流量慢慢下降，通常能为堆芯争取几十秒的额外冷却时间。", "The flywheel on the reactor coolant pump keeps the pump turning after a power loss, so the coolant flow falls off slowly, which usually gives the core several tens of seconds of extra cooling time."],
	"cx_pressurizer": ["稳压器", "PRESSURISER"],
	"cx_pressurizer_a": ["用来控制反应堆一回路压力的大型容器，内部上方留有蒸汽空间，还装有喷淋头、电加热器和安全阀。", "A large vessel for controlling the pressure of the reactor primary loop. Inside, there is a steam space in the upper part, and it also holds a spray head, electric heaters and relief valves."],
	"cx_pressurizer_b": ["稳压器内部装有高压热水和蒸汽，如果一回路还没有泄压就直接拆卸，里面的高温水和蒸汽可能会喷出来。", "The pressuriser holds high-pressure hot water and steam. If it is removed directly before the primary loop has been depressurised, the hot water and steam inside may spray out."],
	"cx_pressurizer_c": ["先让一回路完成泄压和冷却，确认内部压力和温度都降到安全范围以后，再拆卸稳压器。", "First let the primary loop finish depressurising and cooling. Remove the pressuriser only after you have confirmed that the internal pressure and temperature are both within safe limits."],
	"cx_pressurizer_x": ["稳压器通过加热器和喷淋系统来调整一回路的压力。需要升压时，加热器会把一部分水变成蒸汽；需要降压时，就通过喷淋冷水让部分蒸汽冷凝。在 15.5 MPa 的压力下，水的饱和温度大约是 345°C。", "The pressuriser adjusts the pressure of the primary loop with heaters and a spray system. To raise the pressure, the heaters turn some of the water into steam. To lower it, cold water is sprayed in and condenses some of the steam. At a pressure of 15.5 MPa, the saturation temperature of water is about 345°C."],
	"cx_steam_turbine": ["汽轮机", "STEAM TURBINE"],
	"cx_steam_turbine_a": ["汽轮机由高压缸和低压缸组成，内部的转子连接在同一根轴上，叶片从前到后逐渐变长。", "A steam turbine consists of a high-pressure cylinder and a low-pressure cylinder. The rotors inside are joined on the same shaft, and the blades grow longer from front to back."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_b": ["汽轮机通常有几十吨重，而且停机以后，转子可能还在缓慢转动，直接拆卸会有危险。", "A steam turbine usually weighs several tens of tonnes, and after shutdown the rotor may still be turning slowly, so removing it directly is dangerous."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_c": ["先确认转子已经完全停止，再隔离蒸汽管路，之后沿着法兰连接处把汽轮机分段拆下来。", "First confirm that the rotor has stopped completely, then isolate the steam lines, and after that take the turbine apart in sections along its flange joints."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_x": ["蒸汽经过汽轮机时，会在每一级叶片之间逐渐膨胀，压力降低的同时体积也会增大，所以后面需要使用更长的叶片。大型汽轮机通常重达几十吨。", "As steam passes through the turbine, it expands gradually between the stages of blades. Its pressure falls and its volume grows, so the later stages need longer blades. A large turbine usually weighs several tens of tonnes."],
	"cx_condenser": ["凝汽器", "CONDENSER"],
	"cx_condenser_a": ["负责把汽轮机排出的蒸汽冷却成水的设备，主要由壳体、管束、水室和热井组成，冷凝后的水会收集在热井里。", "This unit cools the exhaust steam from the turbine back into water. It consists mainly of a shell, a tube bundle, waterboxes and a hotwell, and the condensed water collects in the hotwell."],
	"cx_condenser_b": ["凝汽器的管束里还有冷却水，底部热井也可能存有凝结水，如果没有排空就直接拆卸，里面的积水可能会大量流出。", "The tube bundle of a condenser still contains cooling water, and the hotwell at the bottom may hold condensate. If you remove the condenser without draining it, a large amount of standing water may pour out."],
	"cx_condenser_c": ["先把冷却水和凝结水全部排空，确认内部压力恢复正常以后，再开始拆卸凝汽器。", "First drain all the cooling water and condensate, and confirm that the internal pressure has returned to normal, then begin removing the condenser."],
	"cx_condenser_x": ["凝汽器通常在接近真空的低压环境下工作，蒸汽接触冷却管束后会逐渐凝结成水，体积能够缩小上千倍，从而帮助凝汽器维持内部的低压状态。", "A condenser normally works at a low pressure close to a vacuum. When steam touches the cooling tubes it gradually condenses into water, and its volume shrinks by a factor of thousands, which helps the condenser keep its internal pressure low."],
	"cx_control_drum": ["控制鼓", "CONTROL DRUM"],
	"cx_control_drum_a": ["一种用来调节反应堆反应性的装置，鼓体由铍制成，一侧装有碳化硼吸收材料，可以通过电机控制旋转角度。", "A device for adjusting the reactivity of the reactor. The drum is made of beryllium, with boron carbide absorber material fitted on one side, and a motor controls its angle of rotation."],
	"cx_control_drum_b": ["如果吊装堆芯前没有固定好控制鼓，吊装过程中控制鼓可能发生转动，让吸收材料偏离原来的位置，导致反应堆反应性升高，附近的辐射剂量也可能突然增加。", "If the control drums are not secured before the core is lifted, a drum may turn during the lift and move the absorber away from its original position. This raises the reactivity of the reactor, and the radiation dose nearby may also rise suddenly."],
	"cx_control_drum_c": ["吊装堆芯之前，先用机械锁定装置固定好每一个控制鼓，确认它们不会转动以后，再开始吊装。", "Before lifting the core, secure every control drum with its mechanical lock, confirm that none of them can turn, and only then begin the lift."],
	"cx_control_drum_x": ["控制鼓通过旋转来调节堆芯的中子数量。当碳化硼吸收材料朝向堆芯时，会吸收更多中子，降低反应性；当铍制反射面朝向堆芯时，会将更多中子反射回去，提高反应性。", "A control drum adjusts the number of neutrons in the core by rotating. When the boron carbide absorber faces the core, it absorbs more neutrons and lowers the reactivity. When the beryllium reflecting face faces the core, it reflects more neutrons back and raises the reactivity."],
	"cx_shadow_shield": ["阴影屏蔽板", "SHADOW SHIELD"],
	"cx_shadow_shield_a": ["由钨和氢化锂交替叠放制成的屏蔽板，主要用来阻挡反应堆堆芯产生的辐射，保护屏蔽板后方的人员和设备。", "A shield plate made of alternating layers of tungsten and lithium hydride. It mainly blocks the radiation produced by the reactor core, protecting the people and equipment behind it."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_b": ["屏蔽板后方的辐射水平比较低，如果提前把它拆走，原本受到保护的工作区域就会直接暴露在堆芯辐射下。", "The radiation level behind the shield plate is low. If you remove the plate too early, the work area it used to protect is exposed directly to the radiation from the core."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_c": ["先用吊装设备固定好屏蔽板，让它继续挡在堆芯前方，工作人员可以在屏蔽板后面的低辐射区域进行拆卸。", "First secure the shield plate with lifting equipment so that it stays in front of the core. The crew can then work on the removal in the low-radiation area behind the plate."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_x": ["屏蔽板里的钨主要负责阻挡伽马射线，氢化锂则负责减慢并吸收中子。在设计条件下，屏蔽板后方的辐射剂量率可以降低到原来的约 1%。航天反应堆通常只在乘员所在的方向设置这种屏蔽板，这样可以减少整套设备的重量。", "The tungsten in the shield plate mainly blocks gamma rays, and the lithium hydride slows and absorbs neutrons. Under design conditions, the radiation dose rate behind the plate can be reduced to about 1% of the original. A space reactor usually carries this kind of shield plate only in the direction where the crew are, which reduces the weight of the whole installation."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: fusion
	"cx_tf_coil": ["超导纵场线圈", "SUPERCONDUCTING TF COIL"],
	"cx_tf_coil_a": ["线圈外面有一层钢制外壳，里面是用铠装超导导体绕成的线圈，每一匝导体内部都有液氦流过，用来维持超导所需的低温。", "The coil has a steel case on the outside. Inside is a winding of armoured superconducting conductor, and liquid helium flows through the inside of every turn of conductor to keep the low temperature that superconductivity needs."],
	"cx_tf_coil_b": ["线圈内部储存着几十亿焦耳的磁场能量，如果冷却系统失效，或者提前拆掉支撑结构，就可能发生失超，让储存的能量在短时间内大量释放，造成严重损坏。", "The coil stores several gigajoules of magnetic energy. If the cooling system fails, or the support structure is removed too early, the coil may quench and release a large amount of the stored energy in a short time, causing serious damage."],
	"cx_tf_coil_c": ["先打开泄能开关，同时保持冷却系统正常运行，等线圈储存的磁场能量全部释放以后，再开始拆卸。", "First open the dump switch while keeping the cooling system running normally. Begin removal only after all the magnetic energy stored in the coil has been released."],
	"cx_tf_coil_x": ["Nb₃Sn 超导材料在适当条件下，温度低于约 18 K 时可以进入超导状态，电阻降到零。实际运行时通常会用约 4.5 K 的液氦进行冷却。如果线圈发生失超，部分导体就会恢复电阻，电流经过这些位置时会产生大量热量，导致附近的导体也逐渐失去超导状态。严重时，整个过程只需要几秒钟，大量磁场能量就会转化成热量，并产生很大的机械作用力。", "Under suitable conditions, Nb₃Sn superconducting material enters the superconducting state below about 18 K, and its resistance drops to zero. In actual operation it is usually cooled with liquid helium at about 4.5 K. If the coil quenches, part of the conductor regains resistance, and the current passing through those places produces a large amount of heat, so the neighbouring conductor gradually loses superconductivity too. In serious cases the whole process takes only a few seconds, and a large amount of magnetic energy turns into heat and produces a great mechanical force."],
	"cx_cs_stack": ["中心螺线管", "CENTRAL SOLENOID"],
	"cx_cs_stack_a": ["由多层饼式线圈叠加组成，线圈中间留有通孔，外面装有拉紧板，上下两端还有预压法兰，用来固定整个结构。", "It is built from many pancake windings stacked together, with a through bore in the middle, tie plates on the outside, and pre-compression flanges at the top and bottom ends to hold the whole structure."],
	"cx_cs_stack_b": ["中心螺线管内部同样储存着大量磁场能量，如果冷却系统失效，就可能发生失超，导致储存的能量在短时间内大量释放。", "The central solenoid also stores a large amount of magnetic energy. If its cooling system fails, it may quench and release the stored energy in a short time."],
	"cx_cs_stack_c": ["先通过泄能系统释放线圈储存的磁场能量，确认泄能完成以后，再拆卸预压法兰和其他固定结构。", "First release the magnetic energy stored in the coil through the dump system, and confirm that the discharge is complete. Then remove the pre-compression flanges and the other holding structures."],
	"cx_cs_stack_x": ["中心螺线管通过改变磁场，在等离子体内部感应出电流，工作原理和变压器类似。运行时，线圈需要承受很大的电磁力，所以必须提前使用预压结构将线圈固定好，防止线圈在受力时发生变形或位移。", "The central solenoid induces a current inside the plasma by changing the magnetic field, on a principle similar to a transformer. In operation the coil has to withstand very large electromagnetic forces, so a pre-compression structure must be fitted in advance to hold the coil and prevent it from deforming or shifting under load."],
	"cx_grav_support": ["线圈支撑", "COIL SUPPORT"],
	"cx_grav_support_a": ["由两端的固定块和中间多层柔性薄板组成，主要用来支撑线圈，同时允许线圈在冷却收缩时产生少量位移，避免底座受到过大的拉力。", "It consists of fixed blocks at the two ends and several layers of thin flexible plates in between. It mainly supports the coil while allowing it a small displacement as it contracts on cooling, so that the base is not subjected to excessive tension."],
	"cx_grav_support_b": ["如果线圈还没有完成泄能，就直接切割或者拆卸支撑结构，可能导致线圈发生位移或变形，严重时还会引起失超，释放大量储存的磁场能量。", "If you cut or remove the support structure before the coil has been discharged, the coil may shift or deform, and in serious cases it may quench and release a large amount of stored magnetic energy."],
	"cx_grav_support_c": ["先确认线圈已经完成泄能，再拆卸两端的固定块和中间的柔性支撑板。", "First confirm that the coil has been discharged, then remove the fixed blocks at the two ends and the flexible support plates in the middle."],
	"cx_grav_support_x": ["钢结构从室温冷却到约 4 K 时会发生收缩，几米长的部件可能缩短几毫米。中间的柔性板可以沿一个方向产生少量弯曲，同时在另一个方向保持足够的刚度，这样既能承受线圈的重量，也能适应冷却时产生的收缩，避免底座和连接部位受到损坏。", "A steel structure shrinks when it is cooled from room temperature to about 4 K, and a part several metres long may shorten by several millimetres. The flexible plates in the middle can bend slightly in one direction while staying sufficiently stiff in the other. This lets them carry the weight of the coil and also accommodate the contraction during cooling, preventing damage to the base and the joints."],
	"cx_vv_wall": ["真空室壁", "VACUUM VESSEL WALL"],
	"cx_vv_wall_a": ["真空室壁由内外两层金属外壳组成，中间装有加强肋，用来支撑整个结构。两层外壳之间还有冷却水通道，里面的屏蔽水可以减少中子辐射对外部设备的影响。", "A vacuum vessel wall consists of an inner and an outer metal shell, with stiffening ribs between them to support the whole structure. There are also cooling water channels between the two shells, and the shielding water in them reduces the effect of neutron radiation on external equipment."],
	"cx_vv_wall_b": ["真空室的夹层里可能还残留着冷却水，而且内壁长期受到聚变中子的照射，部分金属材料已经带有放射性，拆卸时需要注意辐射风险。", "Cooling water may still remain in the gap of the vacuum vessel, and the inner wall has been exposed to fusion neutrons for a long time, so some of the metal is already radioactive. Take care over the radiation risk during removal."],
	"cx_vv_wall_c": ["先把夹层里面残留的冷却水全部排空，确认排水完成以后，再沿着标记好的切割线，将真空室壁分段拆除。", "First drain all the cooling water remaining in the gap and confirm that the draining is complete. Then cut the vacuum vessel wall into sections along the marked cutting lines."],
	"cx_vv_wall_x": ["真空室负责将等离子体与外部环境隔开，同时也能防止氚向外泄漏。聚变反应产生的中子会持续照射真空室内壁，让部分结构钢产生放射性。反应堆退役以后，这些受到活化的材料需要按照放射性水平进行分类处理，其中一部分可以作为低放射性废物处置。", "The vacuum vessel separates the plasma from the outside environment and also stops tritium from leaking out. The neutrons produced by the fusion reaction keep irradiating the inner wall of the vessel, making part of the structural steel radioactive. After the reactor is decommissioned, this activated material has to be sorted according to its radioactivity level, and some of it can be disposed of as low-level radioactive waste."],
	"cx_blanket": ["包层模块", "BLANKET MODULE"],
	"cx_blanket_a": ["安装在真空室内壁上的防护模块，主要由面向等离子体的第一壁和后方的屏蔽块组成，用来承受热量并保护后面的设备。", "A protective module mounted on the inner wall of the vacuum vessel. It consists mainly of a first wall facing the plasma and a shield block behind it, and it takes the heat and protects the equipment behind."],
	"cx_blanket_b": ["第一壁表面的铍瓦比较容易受到撞击损坏，内部冷却管还装有冷却水，如果直接拆卸，可能造成冷却水泄漏。", "The beryllium tiles on the surface of the first wall are easily damaged by impacts, and the cooling pipes inside still hold cooling water. If you remove the module directly, the cooling water may leak."],
	"cx_blanket_c": ["先排空冷却管里面的水，确认没有残留压力以后，再拆下固定螺栓，把整个包层模块取出来。", "First drain the water from the cooling pipes and confirm that no pressure remains. Then remove the fixing bolts and take out the whole blanket module."],
	"cx_blanket_x": ["包层模块的第一壁直接面对高温等离子体，表面需要承受每平方米几兆瓦的热流，所以必须依靠冷却系统带走热量。第一壁使用的铍材料具有毒性，切割时可能产生含铍粉尘，因此尽量保持模块完整，避免直接切割铍瓦。", "The first wall of a blanket module faces the hot plasma directly. Its surface has to withstand a heat flux of several megawatts per square metre, so the cooling system must carry the heat away. The beryllium used in the first wall is toxic and cutting it may produce beryllium-bearing dust, so keep the module intact as far as possible and avoid cutting the beryllium tiles directly."],
	"cx_divertor": ["偏滤器", "DIVERTOR"],
	"cx_divertor_a": ["偏滤器由钢制主体、内外两侧的靶板和中间的穹顶组成。靶板表面安装了很多钨块，内部还有冷却管道，用来带走运行时产生的热量。", "A divertor consists of a steel body, target plates on the inner and outer sides, and a dome in the middle. Many tungsten blocks are mounted on the surface of the target plates, and there are cooling pipes inside to carry away the heat produced in operation."],
	"cx_divertor_b": ["偏滤器本身非常重，而且冷却管道里面可能还存有高压水。如果没有提前排空，拆卸时可能发生高压水喷出，整套设备也需要做好承重固定。", "The divertor itself is very heavy, and the cooling pipes may still hold high-pressure water. If they have not been drained beforehand, high-pressure water may spray out during removal, and the whole unit must also be properly secured to carry its weight."],
	"cx_divertor_c": ["先排空冷却管道里的水，确认内部压力已经释放，再把整套偏滤器从安装位置拆下来。", "First drain the water from the cooling pipes and confirm that the internal pressure has been released. Then remove the whole divertor from its mounting position."],
	"cx_divertor_x": ["偏滤器主要负责接收等离子体边缘排出的热量和杂质，并把它们集中到靶板上。运行时，靶板每平方米可能承受 10–20 MW 的热功率，热负荷接近火箭发动机喉部，所以需要持续使用冷却水来控制温度。", "The divertor receives the heat and impurities exhausted from the edge of the plasma and concentrates them on the target plates. In operation the target plates may take 10–20 MW of heat power per square metre, a heat load close to that at a rocket throat, so cooling water must be used continuously to control the temperature."],
	"cx_gyrotron": ["回旋管", "GYROTRON"],
	"cx_gyrotron_a": ["回旋管是一种用来产生高功率微波的设备，主要由电子枪、超导磁体中的谐振腔、输出窗和顶部的电子收集极组成。", "A gyrotron is a device that produces high-power microwaves. It consists mainly of an electron gun, a cavity inside a superconducting magnet, an output window, and an electron collector at the top."],
	"cx_gyrotron_b": ["回旋管自带超导磁体，内部可能还储存着大量磁场能量。电子枪和收集极使用几十千伏的高压电，即使设备已经停止运行，也可能有残余电荷，直接拆卸会有触电危险。", "A gyrotron has its own superconducting magnet, which may still store a large amount of magnetic energy. The electron gun and the collector use high voltage of several tens of kilovolts, and even after the device has stopped, residual charge may remain, so removing it directly carries a risk of electric shock."],
	"cx_gyrotron_c": ["先切断高压电源并完成放电，再把超导磁体储存的能量释放掉，确认设备已经断电后，将整台回旋管拆下来。", "First cut off the high-voltage supply and complete the discharge, then release the energy stored in the superconducting magnet. After confirming that the device is de-energised, remove the whole gyrotron."],
	"cx_gyrotron_x": ["回旋管利用强磁场让高速电子进行回旋运动，再把电子的部分能量转换成毫米波。一台大型回旋管可以输出约 1 MW、频率为 170 GHz 的微波，用来加热聚变反应堆中的等离子体。输出窗通常使用人造金刚石制造，因为这种材料能够承受较高的热负荷，同时让微波顺利通过。", "A gyrotron uses a strong magnetic field to make fast electrons move in circles, and then converts part of the electrons’ energy into millimetre waves. One large gyrotron can output about 1 MW of microwave power at a frequency of 170 GHz, which is used to heat the plasma in a fusion reactor. The output window is usually made of synthetic diamond, because this material can withstand a high heat load while letting the microwaves pass through."],
	"cx_ech": ["电子回旋加热天线", "EC LAUNCHER"],
	"cx_ech_a": ["这套设备由波纹波导、固定聚焦镜和可以调整方向的反射镜组成，主要负责把微波输送到等离子体内部。", "This equipment consists of corrugated waveguides, a fixed focusing mirror and a mirror whose direction can be adjusted. It mainly delivers the microwaves into the plasma."],
	"cx_ech_b": ["反射镜属于精密部件，很容易在拆卸过程中损坏。波导里面还可能存有绝缘气体，直接切割可能导致气体泄漏。", "The mirrors are precision parts and are easily damaged during removal. The waveguides may also hold insulating gas, and cutting them directly may let the gas leak."],
	"cx_ech_c": ["先确认波导已经泄压，再避开反射镜和波导进行切割，尽量保持设备完整，最后把整套天线拆下来。", "First confirm that the waveguides have been depressurised, then cut while keeping clear of the mirrors and the waveguides, keep the equipment intact as far as possible, and finally remove the whole antenna."],
	"cx_ech_x": ["这套设备通过调整反射镜的角度，把高功率微波送到等离子体内部指定的磁面上。微波可以把能量传递给电子，用来提高等离子体温度，也可以帮助维持等离子体内部的电流。", "By adjusting the angle of the mirror, this equipment sends the high-power microwaves to a chosen magnetic surface inside the plasma. The microwaves can pass their energy to the electrons to raise the plasma temperature, and can also help to sustain the current inside the plasma."],
	"cx_nbi": ["中性束注入器", "NEUTRAL BEAM INJECTOR"],
	"cx_nbi_a": ["用来给等离子体加热的设备，主要由离子源、加速栅极、中和室、偏转磁铁和低温泵组成。", "A device for heating the plasma. It consists mainly of an ion source, accelerator grids, a neutraliser, a bending magnet and cryopumps."],
	"cx_nbi_b": ["加速栅极的工作电压接近一百万伏，断电以后也可能残留高压。低温泵内部还冷凝着氢气，如果温度升高，这些氢就会重新变成气体，导致内部压力上升。", "The accelerator grids operate at a voltage close to a million volts, and high voltage may remain even after the power is cut. Hydrogen is also condensed inside the cryopumps, and if their temperature rises, this hydrogen turns back into gas and the internal pressure goes up."],
	"cx_nbi_c": ["先切断高压电源，释放栅极上的残余电荷，再让低温泵逐渐恢复到常温，排出内部积存的气体，确认安全以后再开始拆卸。", "First cut off the high-voltage supply and discharge the residual charge on the grids. Then let the cryopumps warm up gradually to room temperature and vent the gas stored inside, and begin removal only after confirming that it is safe."],
	"cx_nbi_x": ["中性束注入器会先把氘离子加速到上百 keV，再通过中和室将其转化为不带电的中性原子。这样就能让它们穿过磁场进入等离子体，通过碰撞把能量传递给等离子体，达到加热的目的。低温泵则负责在运行时冷凝并收集气体，一旦停止冷却，原本冷凝在内部的氢就会重新变成气体，所以拆卸前必须先完成回温和排气。", "A neutral beam injector first accelerates deuterium ions to hundreds of keV, and then converts them into uncharged neutral atoms in the neutraliser. This lets them pass through the magnetic field into the plasma, where collisions transfer their energy to the plasma and heat it. The cryopumps condense and collect gas during operation. Once cooling stops, the hydrogen that was condensed inside turns back into gas, so the pumps must be warmed up and vented before removal."],
	"cx_pellet": ["弹丸注入器", "PELLET INJECTOR"],
	"cx_pellet_a": ["这套设备用来制作和发射氘冰弹丸，里面有负责冷冻氘燃料的冷头、制作弹丸的螺杆挤出机，还有切刀和气枪发射管。", "This equipment makes and fires deuterium ice pellets. Inside are a cold head that freezes the deuterium fuel, a screw extruder that forms the pellets, and a cutter and a gas gun barrel."],
	"cx_pellet_b": ["设备内部存有低温冻结的氘燃料，温度升高以后，氘冰会逐渐变成可燃气体。如果没有提前排放，拆卸时就可能发生气体泄漏。", "The equipment holds deuterium fuel frozen at low temperature. When the temperature rises, the deuterium ice gradually turns into a flammable gas. If it has not been vented beforehand, gas may leak during removal."],
	"cx_pellet_c": ["先让设备逐渐恢复到正常温度，排放内部剩余的氘气，确认没有残余压力以后再进行拆卸。", "First let the equipment warm up gradually to normal temperature and vent the remaining deuterium gas. Remove it only after confirming that no residual pressure remains."],
	"cx_pellet_x": ["弹丸注入器会把氘燃料冷冻成几毫米大小的冰弹丸，再通过气枪以每秒几百米的速度发射进等离子体内部。这样就能直接向等离子体内部补充燃料，让反应堆维持运行。", "A pellet injector freezes deuterium fuel into ice pellets a few millimetres across and fires them with a gas gun into the plasma at several hundred metres per second. This adds fuel directly inside the plasma and keeps the reactor running."],
	"cx_port_plug": ["窗口插件", "PORT PLUG"],
	"cx_port_plug_a": ["安装在反应堆观察窗口里的大型屏蔽组件，内部有多组反射镜，可以让诊断光线经过多次反射后进入观测设备。", "A large shielding assembly fitted in an observation port of the reactor. It contains several sets of mirrors, which let the diagnostic light enter the observing instruments after several reflections."],
	"cx_port_plug_b": ["整个组件非常重，而且正面长期受到中子照射，部分材料可能已经被活化，拆卸时需要注意辐射和吊装安全。", "The whole assembly is very heavy, and its front face has been exposed to neutrons for a long time, so some of the material may be activated. Take care over radiation and lifting safety during removal."],
	"cx_port_plug_c": ["先确认吊装设备已经固定好，再按照组件上的分段标记，依次把各个部分吊出来。", "First confirm that the lifting equipment is secured, then lift out the sections one after another according to the section marks on the assembly."],
	"cx_port_plug_x": ["内部的反射镜会让诊断光线经过几次转弯，最终到达观测设备。这样可以减少中子沿着窗口直接向外传播，让工作人员和外部设备受到的辐射更少。", "The mirrors inside turn the diagnostic light several times before it reaches the observing instruments. This reduces the neutrons travelling straight out through the port, so the crew and external equipment receive less radiation."],
	"cx_coldbox": ["制冷机冷箱（氦）", "CRYOPLANT COLD BOX"],
	"cx_coldbox_a": ["一套安装在真空容器里的低温制冷设备，内部装有板翅式换热器和透平膨胀机，可以把氦冷却到约 4.5 K，用来给超导线圈提供低温冷却。", "A cryogenic refrigeration unit installed in a vacuum vessel. Inside are plate-fin heat exchangers and turboexpanders, which can cool helium to about 4.5 K to supply low-temperature cooling to the superconducting coils."],
	"cx_coldbox_b": ["超导线圈需要持续保持低温，如果提前关闭冷箱，线圈的温度就会逐渐升高，严重时还可能发生失超。", "The superconducting coils must be kept cold continuously. If the cold box is shut down too early, the coil temperature gradually rises, and in serious cases a quench may occur."],
	"cx_coldbox_c": ["先保持冷箱正常供电和制冷，等超导磁体储存的能量全部释放以后，再关闭冷箱并开始拆卸。", "First keep the cold box powered and refrigerating normally. Shut it down and begin removal only after all the energy stored in the superconducting magnets has been released."],
	"cx_coldbox_x": ["冷箱需要经过多级换热和膨胀，才能把氦从室温冷却到约 4.5 K。维持这种低温需要消耗大量电力，在约 4 K 的温度下，每带走 1 W 的热量，室温端通常就需要消耗几百瓦的电力。", "The cold box needs several stages of heat exchange and expansion to cool helium from room temperature to about 4.5 K. Keeping this low temperature takes a great deal of electric power: at about 4 K, for every 1 W of heat removed, the room-temperature end usually needs several hundred watts of electric power."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2": ["氢冷箱", "HYDROGEN COLD BOX"],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_a": ["氢冷箱内部有一套低温制冷设备，包括安装在真空夹套里的板翅式换热器、透平和节流阀，主要用来把氢气冷却成液氢。", "A hydrogen cold box contains a cryogenic refrigeration unit, including plate-fin heat exchangers, turbines and a throttle valve mounted in a vacuum jacket. It is mainly used to cool hydrogen gas into liquid hydrogen."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_b": ["氢冷箱还负责处理储罐里蒸发出来的氢气，如果提前关闭，蒸发的氢气就会在罐内不断积累，导致储罐压力逐渐升高。", "The hydrogen cold box also handles the hydrogen that boils off in the storage tanks. If it is shut down too early, the boiled-off hydrogen keeps accumulating in the tanks and the tank pressure gradually rises."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_c": ["抽取液氢期间，需要让氢冷箱继续运行，等液氢抽取完成并确认储罐压力安全以后，再关闭设备电源。", "While the liquid hydrogen is being drawn off, keep the hydrogen cold box running. Cut its power only after the drawing is finished and the tank pressure is confirmed safe."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_x": ["氢气在常压下需要冷却到大约 −253°C 才能液化。液氢储罐即使有保温层，也会不断吸收外部热量，导致一部分液氢蒸发。氢冷箱可以把这些蒸发出来的氢气重新冷却成液体，减少罐内的气体积累，帮助维持储罐压力。", "At normal pressure, hydrogen has to be cooled to about −253°C to liquefy. Even with insulation, a liquid hydrogen tank keeps absorbing heat from outside, and some of the liquid evaporates. The hydrogen cold box can cool this evaporated gas back into liquid, which reduces the gas accumulating in the tank and helps maintain the tank pressure."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: cryogenic physics
	"cx_dr_stage": ["稀释制冷机冷板", "DILUTION FRIDGE STAGE"],
	"cx_dr_stage_a": ["制冷机内部装着多层镀金铜板，从上到下依次是 50 K 级、4 K 级、蒸馏室、冷板和混合室，每一层都有不同的工作温度。", "The refrigerator contains several layers of gold-plated copper plates. From top to bottom they are the 50 K stage, the 4 K stage, the still, the cold plate and the mixing chamber, and each layer works at a different temperature."],
	"cx_dr_stage_b": ["如果混合室还处于毫开尔文级的低温状态，直接移动或者拆卸冷板，可能会导致下方的芯片开裂。", "If you move or remove the cold plate while the mixing chamber is still at millikelvin temperature, the chip below it may crack."],
	"cx_dr_stage_c": ["先按照顺序让各级冷板逐渐恢复温度，等所有部件都回到接近室温的状态以后，再开始拆卸。", "First let the cold plates warm up gradually in order, and begin removal only after all the parts have returned to a state close to room temperature."],
	"cx_dr_stage_x": ["稀释制冷机利用氦-3（³He）进入稀相时需要吸收热量的原理进行制冷，可以让混合室的温度降低到约 10 mK。各层冷板之间通过细同轴线连接，并使用导热能力较低的支撑结构隔开，减少不同温度层之间的热量传递，让越往下的冷板保持越低的温度。", "A dilution refrigerator cools by the principle that ³He must absorb heat when it enters the dilute phase, which can bring the mixing chamber down to about 10 mK. The plates are connected by thin coaxial lines and separated by supports of low thermal conductivity, which reduces heat transfer between the temperature layers, so the lower a plate is, the colder it stays."],
	"cx_qpu": ["量子处理器封装", "QUANTUM PROCESSOR PACKAGE"],
	"cx_qpu_a": ["一个铜制样品盒，里面装着超导量子芯片，盒子边缘还有一排 SMA 接头，用来连接外部的信号线路。", "A copper sample box containing a superconducting quantum chip, with a row of SMA connectors along the edge of the box to connect the external signal lines."],
	"cx_qpu_b": ["芯片在极低温环境下很容易受到损坏，如果突然改变温度，或者在拆卸时发生振动和碰撞，都可能导致芯片开裂。", "The chip is easily damaged at extremely low temperature. A sudden change of temperature, or vibration and knocks during removal, may crack the chip."],
	"cx_qpu_c": ["先按照规定顺序让设备逐渐恢复到室温附近，再固定好隔振台，确认没有明显振动以后，才能取出量子处理器。", "First let the equipment warm up gradually to near room temperature in the prescribed order, then lock the vibration isolation table. Take out the quantum processor only after confirming that there is no noticeable vibration."],
	"cx_qpu_x": ["超导量子比特通常需要在约 10 mK 的极低温环境下运行，温度变化、机械振动和外界杂散光都可能干扰量子态，影响计算结果。这类芯片的制造成本很高，也是整艘船上最值钱的单件设备之一。", "Superconducting qubits usually have to operate at an extremely low temperature of about 10 mK. Temperature changes, mechanical vibration and stray light from outside can all disturb the quantum state and affect the results of a calculation. Such chips are very expensive to make, and this is one of the most valuable single items on the whole ship."],
	"cx_pulse_tube": ["脉管制冷机冷头", "PULSE-TUBE COLD HEAD"],
	"cx_pulse_tube_a": ["制冷系统由旋转阀、回热器、脉管和两级冷台组成，可以把设备预冷到约 4 K，为后面的稀释制冷提供低温环境。", "The cooling system consists of a rotary valve, regenerators, pulse tubes and a two-stage cold platform. It can pre-cool the equipment to about 4 K, providing a low-temperature environment for the dilution cooling that follows."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_b": ["如果提前关闭脉管制冷机，整套稀释制冷系统就会逐渐回温，可能影响还在低温状态下运行的设备。", "If the pulse tube cooler is shut down too early, the whole dilution refrigeration system gradually warms up, which may affect equipment still operating at low temperature."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_c": ["先完成稀释制冷机内部的混合气回收，确认回收结束以后，再关闭脉管制冷机。", "First finish recovering the gas mixture inside the dilution refrigerator and confirm that the recovery is complete. Then shut down the pulse tube cooler."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_x": ["脉管制冷机利用氦气的周期性压力变化进行制冷，冷端没有需要来回运动的机械部件，所以运行时产生的振动比较小，适合用在量子计算设备上。压缩机通过柔性氦气管路与冷头连接，可以进一步减少传到设备上的振动。", "A pulse tube cooler refrigerates using periodic pressure changes of helium gas. Its cold end has no mechanical parts moving back and forth, so it produces little vibration in operation and is suitable for quantum computing equipment. The compressor is connected to the cold head by flexible helium lines, which further reduces the vibration passed on to the equipment."],
	"cx_ghs": ["气体处理系统", "GAS HANDLING SYSTEM"],
	"cx_ghs_a": ["这套系统负责管理氦-3（³He）和氦-4（⁴He）的混合气体，主要包括控制面板、压力表、冷阱和循环泵。", "This system manages the mixed gas of helium-3 (³He) and helium-4 (⁴He). It consists mainly of a control panel, pressure gauges, a cold trap and circulation pumps."],
	"cx_ghs_b": ["循环回路里有价格很高的氦-3，如果还没有回收气体就直接停机，温度升高后可能造成气体损失。", "The circulation loop holds very expensive ³He. If you shut down before the gas has been recovered, the gas may be lost as the temperature rises."],
	"cx_ghs_c": ["先停止气体循环，把回路里的混合气体全部回收到储罐中，确认回收完成以后，再关闭制冷机的冷头。", "First stop the gas circulation and recover all the gas mixture in the loop into the storage tank. After confirming that the recovery is complete, shut down the cold head of the refrigerator."],
	"cx_ghs_x": ["一台稀释制冷机通常需要使用几十升标准状态下的氦-3，每升价格可能达到数千美元，所以拆卸之前一定要把气体回收好。混合气体进入储罐以后，储罐内部的压力会逐渐升高，最后达到平衡状态。", "A dilution refrigerator usually needs several tens of litres of ³He at standard conditions, and each litre may cost several thousand dollars, so the gas must be recovered before removal. Once the gas mixture has entered the storage tank, the pressure inside the tank gradually rises and finally reaches equilibrium."],
	"cx_instrument_rack": ["室温测控机柜", "ROOM-TEMPERATURE ELECTRONICS"],
	"cx_instrument_rack_a": ["机柜里面装着任意波形发生器和数字化仪等测控设备，面板上还有一排 SMA 接口，用来连接制冷机的控制和测量线路。", "The rack contains measurement and control equipment such as arbitrary waveform generators and digitisers, and its panel has a row of SMA ports for connecting the control and measurement lines of the refrigerator."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_b": ["机柜里的仪器价格很高，也容易因为碰撞而损坏。部分设备还通过同轴线连接着制冷机，直接搬动可能会扯坏接口和线路。", "The instruments in the rack are very expensive and easily damaged by knocks. Some of them are also connected to the refrigerator by coaxial lines, and moving them directly may tear off the ports and lines."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_c": ["先关闭机柜电源，拔掉所有连接线，确认机柜已经完全断开以后，再把整套设备运送到设备出口。", "First cut the power to the rack and unplug all the connecting lines. After confirming that the rack is completely disconnected, send the whole unit to the equipment mouth."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_x": ["量子计算机需要通过微波信号控制和读取量子比特，每个量子比特通常都需要多条控制和读出线路。对于采用大量独立线路的系统，几十个量子比特就可能需要数百根同轴线，所以拆卸机柜之前要把这些线路全部断开。", "A quantum computer controls and reads its qubits with microwave signals, and each qubit usually needs several control and readout lines. In a system with many independent lines, a few tens of qubits may need hundreds of coaxial lines, so all of these lines must be disconnected before the rack is removed."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: optics and instruments
	"cx_mirror": ["镜片（主镜 / 副镜）", "MIRROR SEGMENT"],
	"cx_mirror_a": ["望远镜使用的高精度镜片，表面有一层很薄的反射镀膜，背面则采用带有加强肋板的轻量化结构，用来减轻镜片的重量。", "A high-precision mirror segment used in a telescope. Its surface carries a very thin reflective coating, and its back is a lightweight structure with stiffening ribs to reduce the weight of the mirror."],
	"cx_mirror_b": ["附近切割金属时产生的粉尘可能落到镜面上，影响镜片的反射效果。如果支撑镜片的促动器还没有锁定，直接拆卸也可能导致镜片掉落或碎裂。", "Dust produced by cutting metal nearby may land on the mirror face and impair its reflectivity. If you remove the mirror before the actuators that support it have been locked, the mirror may also fall or shatter."],
	"cx_mirror_c": ["先给镜面装好防尘罩，再锁定支撑镜片的促动器，确认镜片已经固定好以后，从外圈开始逐块拆卸。", "First fit the dust cover over the mirror face, then lock the actuators that support the mirror. After confirming that the mirror is secured, remove the segments one by one, starting from the outer ring."],
	"cx_mirror_x": ["望远镜的镜面需要保持很高的精度，表面形状的误差通常只有几十纳米，铝或金制成的反射镀膜也只有大约 100 纳米厚。即使只有一粒金属粉尘落在镜面上，也可能造成光线散射。每块镜片通常由 3 到 6 个促动器支撑，外圈镜片的边缘还搭在内圈上，所以拆卸时需要按照顺序进行。", "A telescope mirror has to keep a very high precision. The error of its surface shape is usually only a few tens of nanometres, and the reflective coating of aluminium or gold is only about 100 nm thick. Even a single grain of metal dust on the mirror face may scatter the light. Each segment is usually supported by 3 to 6 actuators, and the edges of the outer-ring segments also rest on the inner ring, so the removal has to follow a set order."],
	"cx_hexapod": ["六足调整机构", "HEXAPOD"],
	"cx_hexapod_a": ["由上下两个平台和中间 6 根交叉安装的直线作动器组成，可以通过调整每根作动器的长度，改变上方平台的位置和角度。", "It consists of an upper and a lower platform with 6 crossed linear actuators between them. By adjusting the length of each actuator, it can change the position and angle of the upper platform."],
	"cx_hexapod_b": ["这套机构负责支撑望远镜的副镜，如果还没有固定好副镜就直接拆卸，副镜可能失去支撑，发生倾斜或者掉落。", "This mechanism supports the secondary mirror of the telescope. If you remove it before the secondary mirror has been secured, the mirror may lose its support and tilt or fall."],
	"cx_hexapod_c": ["先把副镜固定好，确认重量已经由其他支撑结构承担，再切断调整机构的电源，最后将整套机构拆卸下来。", "First secure the secondary mirror and confirm that its weight is carried by other supporting structures. Then cut the power to the adjusting mechanism, and finally remove the whole mechanism."],
	"cx_hexapod_x": ["这种结构也叫 Stewart 平台，通过改变 6 根作动器的长度，可以精确调整上方平台的前后、左右、上下位置，以及三个方向的旋转角度，总共有 6 个自由度。高精度型号的位置调整精度可以达到微米级，所以经常用在需要精确调整方向的光学设备上。", "This structure is also called a Stewart platform. By changing the lengths of the 6 actuators, you can precisely adjust the front-back, left-right and up-down position of the upper platform, as well as its rotation about three axes, giving 6 degrees of freedom in total. The positioning accuracy of high-precision models can reach the micrometre level, so they are often used in optical equipment that needs precise pointing adjustment."],
	"cx_aft_optics": ["后光学平台", "AFT OPTICS BENCH"],
	"cx_aft_optics_a": ["平台上安装了三镜、折转镜和精密指向镜，这些镜子按照光路的位置排列，把接收到的光线引导到后面的观测仪器。", "The bench carries a tertiary mirror, fold mirrors and a fine steering mirror. These mirrors are arranged along the light path and guide the light they receive to the observing instruments behind."],
	"cx_aft_optics_b": ["平台上的镜子都经过精密校准，安装位置要求很高。如果拆卸时发生碰撞，就可能让整套光学系统失去原来的对准精度。", "All the mirrors on the bench have been precisely aligned, and their mounting positions are very demanding. If a knock occurs during removal, the whole optical system may lose its original alignment accuracy."],
	"cx_aft_optics_c": ["不要在平台附近进行切割，拆卸时尽量保持整体完整，再把整个平台慢慢搬运出去。", "Do not cut near the bench. Keep it intact as far as possible during removal, and then carry the whole bench out slowly."],
	"cx_aft_optics_x": ["平台使用碳化硅、殷钢等热膨胀较小的材料制造，可以减少温度变化造成的结构变形，让镜子之间的位置保持稳定，避免影响光路的对准精度。", "The bench is made of materials with low thermal expansion, such as silicon carbide and Invar. This reduces the structural deformation caused by temperature changes and keeps the positions of the mirrors stable, so the alignment accuracy of the light path is not affected."],
	"cx_fsm": ["精密指向镜", "FAST STEERING MIRROR"],
	"cx_fsm_a": ["一面安装在柔性铰链上的小型反射镜，背面装有三组压电驱动器，可以对镜面的角度进行精细调整。", "A small mirror mounted on a flexure hinge, with three sets of piezo drivers behind it that can adjust the angle of the mirror face finely."],
	"cx_fsm_b": ["压电驱动器工作时需要高电压，断电前直接拆卸可能发生触电。镜面也很容易受到污染，接触或划伤后会影响光学性能。", "The piezo drivers need high voltage when working, so removing them before the power is cut may cause electric shock. The mirror face is also easily contaminated, and touching or scratching it affects the optical performance."],
	"cx_fsm_c": ["先切断电源，确认设备已经断电，再把精密指向镜完整拆下来，搬运时注意保护镜面。", "First cut the power and confirm that the equipment is de-energised. Then remove the whole fine steering mirror, and protect the mirror face while carrying it."],
	"cx_fsm_x": ["精密指向镜通过压电驱动器快速调整镜面角度，每秒可以修正上千次，用来抵消船体振动造成的光路偏移。镜面的调整范围通常只有几毫弧度，但已经足够完成精密指向修正。", "A fine steering mirror adjusts the angle of its mirror face quickly with piezo drivers, correcting it more than a thousand times a second, to cancel the light path shift caused by vibration of the hull. The adjustment range of the mirror is usually only a few milliradians, but this is enough for precise pointing correction."],
	"cx_fgs": ["精密导星仪", "FINE GUIDANCE SENSOR"],
	"cx_fgs_a": ["用来帮助望远镜保持指向精度的设备，内部装有取光镜、中继光学系统和两个导星探测器，可以持续测量导星的位置。", "A device that helps the telescope keep its pointing accuracy. Inside are a pick-off mirror, relay optics and two guide detectors, and it can measure the position of a guide star continuously."],
	"cx_fgs_b": ["内部的光学零件非常精密，拆卸时如果发生碰撞，或者让灰尘进入设备，都可能影响后续的测量精度。", "The optical parts inside are very precise. If a knock occurs during removal, or dust gets into the device, the accuracy of later measurements may be affected."],
	"cx_fgs_c": ["拆卸时要避开附近的切割作业，尽量把整套设备完整拆下来，搬运时也要避免碰撞。", "During removal, keep clear of cutting work nearby, remove the whole device intact as far as possible, and avoid knocks while carrying it."],
	"cx_fgs_x": ["精密导星仪会持续测量一颗导星的位置，再根据位置变化帮助望远镜修正指向，可以将指向误差控制在毫角秒级。", "A fine guidance sensor measures the position of a guide star continuously and uses changes in that position to help the telescope correct its pointing, holding the pointing error to the milliarcsecond level."],
	"cx_wfs": ["波前传感器", "WAVEFRONT SENSOR"],
	"cx_wfs_a": ["内部装有微透镜阵列和相机，光线经过微透镜阵列后会形成许多光点，相机通过测量这些光点的位置变化，判断光线发生了多大的偏移。", "Inside are a lenslet array and a camera. After the light passes through the lenslet array it forms many spots, and the camera measures how the positions of these spots shift to determine how far the light has been deflected."],
	"cx_wfs_b": ["内部的微透镜和相机都属于精密设备，如果拆卸时发生碰撞，可能损坏光学零件，影响测量精度。", "The lenslets and the camera inside are both precision equipment. If a knock occurs during removal, the optical parts may be damaged and the measurement accuracy affected."],
	"cx_wfs_c": ["先切断设备电源，确认断电以后，再把整套传感器完整拆下来，搬运时注意避免碰撞。", "First cut the power to the equipment and confirm that it is de-energised. Then remove the whole sensor, and avoid knocks while carrying it."],
	"cx_wfs_x": ["这种设备使用的是夏克-哈特曼测量原理，微透镜会把进入的光线分成许多光点，相机测出每个光点偏离正常位置的距离，就能计算出对应位置的波前倾斜程度，再根据测量结果调整镜面，减少光学系统产生的误差。", "This device works on the Shack-Hartmann principle. The lenslets split the incoming light into many spots, and the camera measures how far each spot is from its normal position. From this the local slope of the wavefront can be calculated, and the mirror is then adjusted according to the result to reduce the errors of the optical system."],
	"cx_recoater": ["镜片镀膜舱", "MIRROR RECOATER"],
	"cx_recoater_a": ["用来给镜片表面镀反射膜的设备，内部有真空腔、蒸发源和挡板，镜片安装在夹具上，镀膜的一面朝下。", "Equipment for coating the surface of a mirror with a reflective film. Inside are a vacuum chamber, evaporation sources and a shutter, and the mirror is mounted on a fixture with the side to be coated facing down."],
	"cx_recoater_b": ["真空腔里面可能还装着镜片，拆卸时要小心碰撞。蒸发源工作时需要通电，直接拆卸可能发生触电。", "A mirror may still be inside the vacuum chamber, so take care not to knock it during removal. The evaporation sources need electric power when working, and removing them directly may cause electric shock."],
	"cx_recoater_c": ["先切断设备电源，确认真空腔已经恢复正常气压，再打开舱体，把里面的镜片单独取出来，最后拆卸镀膜舱。", "First cut the power to the equipment and confirm that the vacuum chamber has returned to normal air pressure. Then open the chamber, take out the mirror inside separately, and finally remove the recoating chamber."],
	"cx_recoater_x": ["镀膜时，设备会在真空环境中加热铝，让铝蒸发成气体，随后铝原子会沉积在镜片表面，形成一层大约 100 纳米厚的反射膜。", "During coating, the equipment heats aluminium in a vacuum and makes it evaporate into gas. The aluminium atoms then deposit on the surface of the mirror and form a reflective film about 100 nm thick."],
	"cx_ir_camera": ["红外相机", "INFRARED CAMERA"],
	"cx_ir_camera_a": ["用来接收红外光线的观测设备，内部装有真空杜瓦、冷指、滤光轮和镜筒，后面还连接着一台制冷机，用来降低探测器的温度。", "An observing instrument for receiving infrared light. Inside are a vacuum dewar, a cold finger, a filter wheel and a lens barrel, and a cryocooler is connected at the back to lower the temperature of the detector."],
	"cx_ir_camera_b": ["探测器工作时处于极低温状态，杜瓦内部保持真空，制冷机也需要通电运行。如果没有提前断电和回温，直接拆卸可能损坏设备。", "The detector is at an extremely low temperature while working, the inside of the dewar is kept under vacuum, and the cryocooler also needs power to run. If you remove the camera without cutting the power and warming it up first, the equipment may be damaged."],
	"cx_ir_camera_c": ["先关闭制冷机并切断电源，等待探测器逐渐恢复到安全温度，再把整台红外相机完整拆下来。", "First shut down the cryocooler and cut the power, wait for the detector to warm up gradually to a safe temperature, and then remove the whole infrared camera."],
	"cx_ir_camera_x": ["红外探测器需要在很低的温度下工作，有些设备甚至要冷却到几十开尔文以下，因为探测器本身也会产生热辐射。如果温度太高，这些热辐射就会干扰相机接收到的红外信号，影响观测结果。", "An infrared detector has to work at a very low temperature, and some must be cooled to below a few tens of kelvin, because the detector itself also produces thermal radiation. If the temperature is too high, this thermal radiation interferes with the infrared signal the camera receives and affects the observations."],
	"cx_spectrograph": ["光谱仪", "SPECTROGRAPH"],
	"cx_spectrograph_a": ["用来分析光线的观测设备，内部装有入射狭缝、准直镜、衍射光栅、相机镜头和探测器，可以把接收到的光线按照波长分开。", "An observing instrument for analysing light. Inside are an entrance slit, a collimator, a diffraction grating, camera optics and a detector, and it can separate the light it receives by wavelength."],
	"cx_spectrograph_b": ["内部的衍射光栅非常精密，表面有大量密集的刻线，如果拆卸时直接接触或者发生碰撞，就可能损坏光栅，影响后续的测量精度。", "The diffraction grating inside is very precise, and its surface carries a great many closely spaced lines. If you touch it directly or knock it during removal, the grating may be damaged and the accuracy of later measurements affected."],
	"cx_spectrograph_c": ["拆卸之前先盖好遮光罩，保护内部的光学零件，然后把整台光谱仪完整拆下来，搬运时注意避免碰撞。", "Before removal, first put on the light cover to protect the optical parts inside. Then remove the whole spectrograph, and avoid knocks while carrying it."],
	"cx_spectrograph_x": ["衍射光栅每毫米可以有上千条刻线，不同波长的光经过光栅后会沿不同方向传播，探测器就能分别记录这些光线。通过分析得到的光谱线，可以判断观测目标含有哪些元素，还能根据谱线的偏移计算目标的运动速度。", "A diffraction grating can have thousands of lines per millimetre. After passing through the grating, light of different wavelengths travels in different directions, and the detector can record each of them separately. By analysing the resulting spectral lines you can tell which elements the target contains, and you can also calculate the target’s velocity from the shift of the lines."],
	"cx_coronagraph": ["日冕仪", "CORONAGRAPH"],
	"cx_coronagraph_a": ["镜筒入口装有一块遮挡盘，可以挡住恒星本体发出的强光，让仪器能够观察到恒星周围亮度很低的日冕。", "An occulting disc at the entrance of the tube blocks the strong light from the star itself, so that the instrument can observe the very dim corona around the star."],
	"cx_coronagraph_b": ["飞船刚经过近日点，设备可能还没有完全冷却，表面温度会很高。内部的光学零件也很精密，拆卸时要避免碰撞。", "The ship has just passed perihelion, so the instrument may not have cooled completely and its surface temperature may be very high. The optical parts inside are also precise, so avoid knocks during removal."],
	"cx_coronagraph_c": ["先测量设备温度，等温度降下来以后，再把整套日冕仪完整拆下来。", "First measure the temperature of the equipment, wait for it to cool down, and then remove the whole coronagraph."],
	"cx_coronagraph_x": ["日冕的亮度大约只有太阳表面的百万分之一，要观察到这么微弱的光线，就得尽量减少其他光线的干扰。所以镜筒内部安装了很多层挡光环，用来阻挡多余的杂散光。", "The brightness of the corona is only about one millionth of that of the solar surface. To observe light this faint, interference from other light must be reduced as far as possible. So many layers of baffle rings are fitted inside the tube to block the unwanted stray light."],
	"cx_particle_det": ["粒子探测器", "PARTICLE DETECTOR"],
	"cx_particle_det_a": ["用来检测粒子种类和能量的设备，准直器后面安装着多层硅探测器和吸收板，可以测量粒子穿过不同材料时损失的能量。", "A device for detecting the kind and energy of particles. Behind the collimator are several layers of silicon detectors and absorber plates, which can measure the energy a particle loses as it passes through different materials."],
	"cx_particle_det_b": ["内部的硅探测器属于精密零件，受到碰撞可能损坏。偏压电源还会产生高电压，设备没有断电时不能直接拆卸。", "The silicon detectors inside are precision parts and may be damaged by knocks. The bias supply also produces high voltage, so do not remove the device directly while it is still powered."],
	"cx_particle_det_c": ["先关闭偏压电源，确认设备已经断电以后，再把整个粒子探测器完整拆下来，搬运时注意避免碰撞。", "First switch off the bias supply and confirm that the equipment is de-energised. Then remove the whole particle detector, and avoid knocks while carrying it."],
	"cx_particle_det_x": ["粒子每穿过一层硅探测器，都会损失一部分能量。通过测量粒子在每一层损失了多少能量，以及它最终能穿透多深，就可以判断粒子的种类和能量大小。", "Each time a particle passes through a layer of silicon detector, it loses some of its energy. By measuring how much energy the particle loses in each layer, and how deep it finally penetrates, you can determine the kind of the particle and its energy."],
	"cx_magnetometer": ["磁强计", "MAGNETOMETER"],
	"cx_magnetometer_a": ["一套用来测量磁场的设备，由三个互相垂直的磁通门传感绕组和配套的电子箱组成，可以测量不同方向的磁场强度。", "A set of equipment for measuring magnetic fields. It consists of three mutually perpendicular fluxgate sensor windings and a matching electronics box, and it can measure the field strength in different directions."],
	"cx_magnetometer_b": ["磁强计属于精密测量设备，传感头安装在伸杆末端，拆卸时如果发生碰撞，可能会影响测量精度。", "The magnetometer is a precision measuring instrument, and its sensor head is mounted at the end of a boom. If a knock occurs during removal, the measurement accuracy may be affected."],
	"cx_magnetometer_c": ["拆卸时注意保护传感头和连接线，把整套设备完整拆下来，再送到设备回收口。", "During removal, take care to protect the sensor head and the connecting lines. Remove the whole set intact and then send it to the equipment recovery mouth."],
	"cx_magnetometer_x": ["船上的金属材料和电气设备都会产生磁场，影响磁强计的测量结果，所以传感头一般会安装在远离船体的长杆末端，配套的电子箱则安装在伸杆根部，这样可以减少船体对测量结果的干扰。", "The metal materials and electrical equipment on the ship all produce magnetic fields that affect the magnetometer’s measurements, so the sensor head is usually mounted at the end of a long pole away from the hull, and the matching electronics box is mounted at the root of the boom. This reduces the interference of the hull with the measurements."],
	"cx_lab": ["分析仪器", "LABORATORY INSTRUMENTS"],
	"cx_lab_a": ["实验室里使用的各种分析设备，包括气相色谱仪、质谱仪和显微镜，主要用来检测样本中的物质成分，或者观察样本的内部结构。", "Various analytical instruments used in a laboratory, including gas chromatographs, mass spectrometers and microscopes. They are mainly used to detect the substances in a sample or to observe its internal structure."],
	"cx_lab_b": ["这些仪器通常比较昂贵，内部还有不少精密零件，拆卸时需要避免碰撞。质谱仪还装有真空泵和高压部件，断电前不要直接拆卸。", "These instruments are usually expensive and contain many precision parts, so avoid knocks during removal. A mass spectrometer also has vacuum pumps and high-voltage parts, so do not remove it directly before the power is cut."],
	"cx_lab_c": ["先切断设备电源，再把仪器完整拆下来，小心搬运到设备回收口，尽量不要损坏内部零件。", "First cut the power to the equipment, then remove the whole instrument, carry it carefully to the equipment recovery mouth, and try not to damage the parts inside."],
	"cx_lab_x": ["气相色谱仪可以利用不同物质沸点和极性的差异，把混合气体中的各种成分分离出来。质谱仪则会测量离子的质荷比，用来分析样本中有哪些物质，以及它们的相对含量。", "A gas chromatograph can separate the components of a mixed gas by using the differences in boiling point and polarity between substances. A mass spectrometer measures the mass-to-charge ratio of ions, which is used to analyse which substances are in a sample and their relative amounts."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: data centre
	"cx_immersion_rack": ["浸没式服务器机柜", "IMMERSION RACK"],
	"cx_immersion_rack_a": ["刀片服务器竖直插放，整台服务器浸在装有绝缘冷却液的槽里。", "Blade servers are inserted upright, and each whole server is immersed in a tank of dielectric coolant."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_b": ["如果槽内还有冷却液就吊出机柜，冷却液会泼洒出来，导致相邻机柜短路。", "If you lift out the rack while the tank still holds coolant, the coolant spills out and short-circuits the neighbouring racks."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_c": ["先通过槽上的接口抽干冷却液，再吊出机柜。", "Drain the coolant through the port on the tank first, then lift out the rack."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_x": ["绝缘液使用氟化液或合成油，能够直接接触芯片并带走热量，冷却效率比风冷高得多。绝缘液价格很高，泼洒会造成损失；在失重环境中，泼出的液团还会漂到相邻机柜上。", "The dielectric fluid is a fluorinated fluid or a synthetic oil. It touches the chips directly and carries away heat, with much higher cooling efficiency than air. The fluid itself is very expensive, so spilling it causes a loss. In free fall, the spilt globules also drift onto the neighbouring racks."],
	"cx_storage_array": ["存储阵列与交换机", "STORAGE AND SWITCHING"],
	"cx_storage_array_a": ["存储阵列由多层硬盘托架和控制器组成；核心交换机则配有线卡。", "A storage array consists of several shelves of drive carriers and controllers. A core switch has line cards instead."],
	"cx_storage_array_b": ["硬盘中可能存有客户的监管数据。", "The drives may hold the client’s data under custody."],
	"cx_storage_array_c": ["先把监管硬盘锁进运输箱，再拆卸阵列。", "Latch the custody drives into their transport bays first, then remove the array."],
	"cx_storage_array_x": ["数据价值与硬件价值无关：一块硬盘的硬件价值只有几百块，硬盘内的数据却可能涉及合同违约。", "The value of the data has nothing to do with the value of the hardware. A drive may be worth only a few hundred, but the data on it may involve a breach of contract."],
	"cx_drive_carrier": ["监管硬盘", "CUSTODY DRIVE"],
	"cx_drive_carrier_a": ["硬盘安装在托架中，托架上有锁扣把手和活动灯。", "A drive is mounted in a carrier, which has a latch handle and an activity light."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_b": ["如果没有把硬盘锁进屏蔽运输箱就带走，会被判定为违约并受到罚款。", "If you take a drive away without latching it into a shielded transport bay, it counts as a breach of contract and you are fined."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_c": ["先拨开硬盘的监管锁扣，再将整件硬盘运走。", "Throw the drive’s custody latch first, then take the whole drive away."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_x": ["“监管链”要求从硬盘离开机柜到交给客户的每个步骤都能证明数据没有被读取或复制。", "‘Chain of custody’ means that every step from the drive leaving the rack to its handover to the client must prove that the data was never read or copied."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: drilling
	"cx_top_drive": ["顶驱", "TOP DRIVE"],
	"cx_top_drive_a": ["顶驱是吊在游车下方的钻井电机，由齿轮箱、主轴、两个内防喷阀和吊卡组成。", "A top drive is a drilling motor hung below the travelling block. It consists of a gearbox, a main shaft, two inside BOP valves and an elevator."],
	"cx_top_drive_b": ["顶驱连接着钻杆，钻杆内可能仍有扭矩和泥浆压力。", "The top drive is connected to the drill string, which may still hold torque and mud pressure."],
	"cx_top_drive_c": ["先释放钻杆内的扭矩和压力，再处理顶驱。", "Release the torque and pressure in the drill string first, then deal with the top drive."],
	"cx_top_drive_x": ["顶驱从上方直接带动钻杆旋转，同时通过鹅颈管注入泥浆。顶驱的功率通常在 1 MW 以上。", "A top drive turns the drill string directly from above, and injects mud through its gooseneck at the same time. The power of a top drive is usually above 1 MW."],
	"cx_drawworks": ["绞车", "DRAWWORKS"],
	"cx_drawworks_a": ["绞车由缠绕大绳的卷筒、盘式刹车、电机和齿轮箱组成。", "A drawworks consists of a drum wound with the drill line, disc brakes, a motor and a gearbox."],
	"cx_drawworks_b": ["大绳承受着整串钻具的拉力。", "Its line carries the whole string's pull."],
	"cx_drawworks_c": ["先卸下全部钻具，等大绳松弛后再拆卸绞车。", "Take out all the drilling tools first, and remove the drawworks only after the line has gone slack."],
	"cx_drawworks_x": ["大绳穿过天车和游车，形成多股滑轮组。绞车拉动其中一股大绳，就能吊起几百吨的重量。", "The drill line is reeved through the crown block and the travelling block to form a multi-line pulley system. By pulling one line, the drawworks can lift a weight of hundreds of tonnes."],
	"cx_blocks": ["天车与游车", "CROWN AND TRAVELLING BLOCKS"],
	"cx_blocks_a": ["天车是井架顶部的一排滑轮，游车是可以上下移动的滑轮组。", "The crown block is a row of sheaves at the top of the derrick, and the travelling block is a pulley assembly that can move up and down."],
	"cx_blocks_b": ["大绳绷紧时，天车和游车共同构成一套张紧的滑轮组。", "While the line is taut, the crown block and the travelling block together form a tensioned pulley system."],
	"cx_blocks_c": ["先松开大绳，再拆卸天车和游车。", "Slacken the line first, then remove the crown block and the travelling block."],
	"cx_blocks_x": ["对于使用 10 股大绳的滑轮组，绞车拉力乘以约 10 就是吊重。", "For a pulley system with 10 lines strung, the drawworks pull multiplied by about 10 gives the hook load."],
	"cx_rotary_table": ["转盘", "ROTARY TABLE"],
	"cx_rotary_table_a": ["转盘位于钻台上，由齿圈、方补心和驱动小齿轮组成。", "The rotary table sits on the drill floor. It consists of a ring gear, a master bushing and a drive pinion."],
	"cx_rotary_table_b": ["转盘的刹车锁住了钻杆内的残余扭矩。", "The rotary table’s brake holds the residual torque in the drill string."],
	"cx_rotary_table_c": ["关闭转盘刹车并释放扭矩，直到扭矩表的读数接近 0。", "Release the rotary brake and bleed the torque until the torque gauge reads close to 0."],
	"cx_rotary_table_x": ["几千米长的钻杆可以储存扭转产生的弹性能。转盘停下时，钻杆可能仍处于扭转了几圈的状态。", "Several kilometres of drill pipe can store elastic energy from twisting. When the rotary table stops, the drill string may still be twisted by several turns."],
	"cx_drillpipe": ["钻杆", "DRILL PIPE"],
	"cx_drillpipe_a": ["钻杆每三根组成一立，接头处有耐磨带。排放架上分层码放着钻杆。", "Drill pipe is made up in stands of three joints, with hardbanding at the tool joints. The pipe is racked in layers on the pipe rack."],
	"cx_drillpipe_b": ["仍在井内的钻杆承受着扭矩和泥浆压力。", "Pipe that is still in the hole holds torque and mud pressure."],
	"cx_drillpipe_c": ["先释放扭矩和压力，再从上到下逐节卸开接头。", "Release the torque and pressure first, then break out the connections one joint at a time from the top down."],
	"cx_drillpipe_x": ["钻杆接头使用锥形螺纹，上扣扭矩达到几万牛·米。排放架上的钻杆属于普通货物。", "Tool joints use tapered threads, made up to a torque of tens of thousands of newton-metres. Pipe racked on the pipe rack counts as ordinary cargo."],
	"cx_bha": ["钻具组合", "BOTTOM-HOLE ASSEMBLY"],
	"cx_bha_a": ["钻具组合包括钻铤、扶正器、随钻测量工具、取芯筒和钻头。", "The bottom hole assembly includes drill collars, a stabiliser, an MWD tool, a core barrel and a bit."],
	"cx_bha_b": ["这部分是最重的一段钻具。随钻工具内有电池，取芯筒内有岩芯。", "This is the heaviest section of the drilling tools. The MWD tool contains batteries, and the core barrel contains a core."],
	"cx_bha_c": ["按照危险品要求处理电池，单独回收岩芯。", "Handle the batteries according to the hazard requirements, and recover the core separately."],
	"cx_bha_x": ["钻铤向钻头施加压力，扶正器使井眼保持笔直。岩芯是钻井取得的产品，通常是合同指定件。", "The drill collars put weight on the bit, and the stabiliser keeps the hole straight. The core is the product that drilling obtains, and is usually a named item in the contract."],
	"cx_mud_pump": ["泥浆泵", "MUD PUMP"],
	"cx_mud_pump_a": ["泥浆泵是三缸往复泵，由动力端、十字头、液力端和脉动阻尼器组成。", "A mud pump is a triplex reciprocating pump. It consists of a power end, crossheads, a fluid end and a pulsation dampener."],
	"cx_mud_pump_b": ["排出管和阻尼器内有高压泥浆，阻尼器内还预充了氮气。", "The discharge line and the dampener hold high-pressure mud, and the dampener is also precharged with nitrogen."],
	"cx_mud_pump_c": ["先释放排出管内的压力和阻尼器内的氮气，再拆卸泥浆泵。", "Release the pressure in the discharge line and the nitrogen in the dampener first, then remove the mud pump."],
	"cx_mud_pump_x": ["泥浆泵的排出压力可达 35 MPa。脉动阻尼器内的氮气囊可以吸收每个冲程产生的压力波动。", "The discharge pressure of a mud pump can reach 35 MPa. The nitrogen bladder inside the pulsation dampener absorbs the pressure fluctuation produced by each stroke."],
	"cx_shaker": ["振动筛", "SHALE SHAKER"],
	"cx_shaker_a": ["振动筛由安装在弹簧上的倾斜筛箱和两台振动电机组成，用于筛出钻屑。", "A shaker consists of a tilted screen basket mounted on springs and two vibrator motors. It screens out the drill cuttings."],
	"cx_shaker_b": ["筛箱内有黏稠的泥浆。", "The basket is full of sticky mud."],
	"cx_shaker_c": ["先断开电源，再将振动筛整件拆下。", "Cut the power first, then remove the shaker as a whole."],
	"cx_shaker_x": ["在失重环境中，钻屑无法依靠重力滑下筛面。船上的振动筛通过控制振动方向将钻屑抛出。", "In free fall, cuttings cannot slide off the screen under gravity. A ship’s shaker throws the cuttings off by controlling the direction of vibration."],
	"cx_mud_clean": ["泥浆净化设备", "MUD TREATMENT"],
	"cx_mud_clean_a": ["泥浆净化设备包括除砂器、除气器、离心机、液气分离器和搅拌器。", "Mud cleaning equipment includes a desander, a degasser, a centrifuge, a mud-gas separator and an agitator."],
	"cx_mud_clean_b": ["设备内有泥浆，除气器和液气分离器中还可能有可燃气体。", "The equipment holds mud, and the degasser and the mud-gas separator may also hold flammable gas."],
	"cx_mud_clean_c": ["先排空设备并通风，再进行拆卸。", "Drain the equipment and ventilate it first, then remove it."],
	"cx_mud_clean_x": ["钻头进入含气地层时，返回的泥浆会携带天然气。除气器在真空状态下分离出气体，再将气体送去燃烧或放空。", "When the bit enters a gas-bearing formation, the returning mud carries natural gas. The degasser separates the gas out under vacuum, then sends the gas off to be flared or vented."],
	"cx_roughneck": ["铁钻工", "IRON ROUGHNECK"],
	"cx_roughneck_a": ["铁钻工由轨道上的小车、折叠臂和上下两套扳手头组成。", "An iron roughneck consists of a carriage on a rail, a folding arm, and two sets of wrench heads, upper and lower."],
	"cx_roughneck_b": ["铁钻工使用液压驱动，系统仍有压力时，设备可能发生剧烈动作。", "The iron roughneck is hydraulically driven. If the system still holds pressure, the equipment may make violent movements."],
	"cx_roughneck_c": ["先释放液压系统的压力，再拆卸铁钻工。", "Release the pressure in the hydraulic system first, then remove the iron roughneck."],
	"cx_roughneck_x": ["铁钻工代替人安装和拆卸钻杆螺纹。上方扳手头负责旋扣，下方扳手头使用几万牛·米的扭矩紧扣或松扣。", "An iron roughneck makes up and breaks out the pipe threads in place of a crew. The upper wrench head spins the connection, and the lower wrench head tightens or loosens it with a torque of tens of thousands of newton-metres."],
	"cx_bop": ["防喷器组", "BLOWOUT PREVENTER"],
	"cx_bop_a": ["防喷器组包括环形防喷器、三道闸板防喷器和侧出口阀；其中一道闸板是剪切闸板。", "A BOP stack includes an annular preventer, three ram preventers and side outlet valves. One of the rams is a shear ram."],
	"cx_bop_b": ["关闭的闸板下方可能仍有井压。", "There may still be well pressure below the closed rams."],
	"cx_bop_c": ["先通过节流管线或压井管线泄压，确认没有压力后再拆卸防喷器组。", "Bleed the pressure through the choke line or the kill line first, and remove the BOP stack only after confirming there is no pressure."],
	"cx_bop_x": ["发生井涌时，防喷器可在几秒内封住井口；剪切闸板可以剪断钻杆并封井。防喷器组是井控的最后一道屏障，也是钻井船上最昂贵的设备之一。", "In a kick, the BOP can shut in the wellhead within a few seconds, and the shear rams can cut the drill pipe and seal the well. The BOP stack is the last barrier of well control, and also one of the most expensive items on a drillship."],
	"cx_well_manifold": ["立管与节流管汇", "STANDPIPE AND CHOKE MANIFOLD"],
	"cx_well_manifold_a": ["这套设备包括立管、闸阀、节流阀、压力表和防喷器蓄能器组。", "This equipment includes a standpipe, gate valves, an adjustable choke, pressure gauges and the BOP accumulator unit."],
	"cx_well_manifold_b": ["管汇和蓄能器内都有高压。", "Both the manifold and the accumulators hold high pressure."],
	"cx_well_manifold_c": ["先通过泄压阀释放压力，等蓄能器压力降到 0 后再拆卸。", "Release the pressure through the bleed valves first, and remove the equipment only after the accumulator pressure has dropped to 0."],
	"cx_well_manifold_x": ["防喷器蓄能器（Koomey）在 21 MPa 压力下储存足以关闭全部闸板的液压能，断电后仍能工作。", "The BOP accumulators (Koomey unit) store, at a pressure of 21 MPa, enough hydraulic energy to close every ram, and still work after power is lost."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: gas plant
	"cx_ortho_para": ["正仲氢转化器", "ORTHO-PARA CONVERTER"],
	"cx_ortho_para_a": ["换热器通道内填有氧化铁催化剂，通道浸在冷浴中。", "The passages of the heat exchanger are packed with iron oxide catalyst, and the passages are immersed in a cold bath."],
	"cx_ortho_para_b": ["转化器内有极冷的氢。", "The converter holds very cold hydrogen."],
	"cx_ortho_para_c": ["先让转化器回温并释放压力，再进行拆卸。", "Let the converter warm up and release the pressure first, then remove it."],
	"cx_ortho_para_x": ["常温下的氢有 75% 是正氢。氢液化后，正氢会自发转化为仲氢并释放热量，足以蒸发掉一罐液氢的大半。因此，液化时需要使用催化剂完成转化。", "Hydrogen at room temperature is 75% ortho-hydrogen. After hydrogen is liquefied, the ortho-hydrogen converts spontaneously to para-hydrogen and gives off heat, enough to boil away most of a tank of liquid hydrogen. So a catalyst is used to complete the conversion during liquefaction."],
	"cx_precooler": ["液氮预冷器", "LN₂ PRECOOLER"],
	"cx_precooler_a": ["液氮浴槽内装有盘管，工艺气通过盘管时会被预冷。", "A liquid nitrogen bath contains a coiled tube bundle, and the process gas is pre-cooled as it passes through the coil."],
	"cx_precooler_b": ["浴槽内有液氮，液氮会持续蒸发。", "The bath holds liquid nitrogen, which keeps boiling off."],
	"cx_precooler_c": ["先抽空液氮并放出蒸发气体，再拆卸预冷器。", "Draw off the liquid nitrogen and vent the boil-off gas first, then remove the pre-cooler."],
	"cx_precooler_x": ["系统先使用 77 K 的液氮预冷气体，后续透平才能高效地将气体冷却到 20 K。", "The system first pre-cools the gas with 77 K liquid nitrogen, so that the turbines downstream can then efficiently cool the gas to 20 K."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: industry
	"cx_arc_furnace": ["电弧炉炉芯", "ARC FURNACE CORE"],
	"cx_arc_furnace_a": ["电弧炉炉芯由带耐火衬里的炉壳、三根石墨电极和水冷炉顶组成。", "An arc furnace core consists of a refractory-lined shell, three graphite electrodes and a water-cooled roof."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_b": ["停机并不代表炉芯已经冷却。如果几百度的炉芯失去冷却，耐火材料会因热震开裂。", "Stopped does not mean the core has cooled. If a core still at several hundred degrees loses its cooling, the refractory cracks from thermal shock."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_c": ["保持冷却，直到炉芯完全冷却后再将其整件吊出。", "Keep the cooling on until the core is completely cold, then lift it out as a whole."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_x": ["耐火材料的导热性较差，内外温差较大时，热应力会使材料开裂。冷却回路正常工作时，炉芯从 760 °C 降至 150 °C 约需两分半。", "Refractory conducts heat poorly, and when the temperature difference between inside and outside is large, thermal stress cracks the material. With the cooling loop working normally, the core takes about two and a half minutes to drop from 760 °C to 150 °C."],
	"cx_sorter": ["分选机", "SORTER"],
	"cx_sorter_a": ["分选机采用涡电流分选机或磁选滚筒，按金属种类进行分选。", "The sorter is an eddy-current separator or a magnetic drum. It sorts metals by kind."],
	"cx_sorter_b": ["转子内有强永磁体，会吸引铁屑和无人机。", "The rotor contains strong permanent magnets, which attract steel swarf and the drone."],
	"cx_sorter_c": ["先断开电源，等转子停止后再拆卸分选机。", "Cut the power first and wait for the rotor to stop, then remove the sorter."],
	"cx_sorter_x": ["高速旋转的磁极会在铝和铜中感应出涡流，产生的斥力将有色金属弹过分料板，铁则会被磁力吸走。", "The fast-spinning magnetic poles induce eddy currents in aluminium and copper, and the repulsion this produces flicks the non-ferrous metals over the splitter, while iron is pulled away by the magnet."],
	"cx_scrubber": ["尾气洗涤塔", "WET SCRUBBER"],
	"cx_scrubber_a": ["尾气洗涤塔由填料床、喷淋头、除雾器和循环泵组成。", "An off-gas scrubber consists of a packed bed, a spray header, a mist eliminator and a recirculation pump."],
	"cx_scrubber_b": ["塔底液体吸收了有害气体，具有腐蚀性。", "The liquid in the sump has absorbed the harmful gases and is corrosive."],
	"cx_scrubber_c": ["先排空塔底液体，再拆卸洗涤塔。", "Drain the sump liquid first, then remove the scrubber."],
	"cx_scrubber_x": ["喷淋的碱液可以吸收尾气中的酸性气体，包括 SO₂ 和 HCl。", "The sprayed alkaline solution can absorb the acid gases in the off-gas, including SO₂ and HCl."],
	"cx_crusher": ["破碎头", "CRUSHER"],
	"cx_crusher_a": ["圆锥破碎机的动锥在碗形衬板内偏心摆动。", "In a cone crusher, the mantle gyrates eccentrically inside a bowl liner."],
	"cx_crusher_b": ["如果料仓内还有矿石，破碎头仍承受着矿堆的重量。", "If there is still ore in the hopper, the crusher head still bears the weight of the ore pile."],
	"cx_crusher_c": ["先卸空料仓，再拆卸破碎头。", "Empty the hopper first, then remove the crusher head."],
	"cx_crusher_x": ["偏心轴使动锥反复张合，将矿石挤碎在狭缝内。破碎头很重，通常需要分段拆卸。", "An eccentric shaft makes the mantle open and close repeatedly, crushing the ore in the narrow gap. The crusher head is heavy and usually has to be removed in sections."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: weapons
	"cx_turret": ["炮塔与炮座", "GUN TURRET"],
	"cx_turret_a": ["炮塔与炮座包括多面体炮室、炮管、耳轴、回转座圈，以及下方的弹药提升机。", "The turret and its mount include a faceted gunhouse, a barrel, trunnions, a slewing ring, and an ammunition hoist below."],
	"cx_turret_b": ["弹药提升机和炮膛内可能还有弹药。", "There may still be ammunition in the ammunition hoist and the breech."],
	"cx_turret_c": ["先清空弹药，再沿标线拆卸炮塔。", "Clear the ammunition first, then take the turret apart along the marked lines."],
	"cx_turret_x": ["炮塔重量很大，座圈滚道承受炮塔的全部重量和后坐力；炮管采用厚壁高强钢。", "A turret is very heavy, and the roller race of the ring carries the turret’s whole weight and the recoil. The barrel is made of thick-walled high-strength steel."],
	"cx_launcher": ["箱式发射架", "BOX LAUNCHER"],
	"cx_launcher_a": ["箱式发射架由并排的发射箱组成，每个发射箱都有易碎盖；也可能是诱饵弹发射筒。", "A box launcher consists of canisters side by side, each with a frangible cover. It may also be a decoy launcher tube."],
	"cx_launcher_b": ["发射箱内可能有弹药。切割、加热或撞击都可能引爆弹药。", "A canister may still hold ammunition. Cutting, heating or knocks can set the ammunition off."],
	"cx_launcher_c": ["不要在发射架附近切割；将弹药整件送往危险品处理处。", "Do not cut near the launcher. Send the ammunition, as a whole, to hazard handling."],
	"cx_launcher_x": ["导弹的固体发动机和战斗部都含有含能材料，加热到一定温度后会自燃，这种现象称为烤燃。", "A missile’s solid motor and warhead both contain energetic materials, which ignite on their own once heated to a certain temperature. This is called cook-off."],
	"cx_ciws": ["近防炮", "CLOSE-IN WEAPON SYSTEM"],
	"cx_ciws_a": ["近防炮由旋转多管炮、上方的雷达罩和底座组成。", "A close-in weapon system consists of a rotary multi-barrel cannon, a radome above it and a mount."],
	"cx_ciws_b": ["弹鼓内可能还有弹药，电容也可能带电。", "The drum may still hold ammunition, and the capacitors may also be charged."],
	"cx_ciws_c": ["先给电容放电并清空弹鼓，再拆卸近防炮。", "Discharge the capacitors and empty the drum first, then remove the close-in weapon system."],
	"cx_ciws_x": ["近防炮每分钟可以发射几千发弹药，弹鼓可装上千发弹药，因此一个弹鼓相当于一座小型弹药库。", "A close-in weapon system can fire thousands of rounds a minute, and its drum can hold over a thousand rounds, so one drum is equivalent to a small magazine."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: stored energy
	"cx_m_munitions": ["弹药：烤燃与殉爆", "MUNITIONS: COOK-OFF AND CHAIN"],
	"cx_m_munitions_a": ["弹库中的炮弹和导弹受到加热或撞击时会起爆。一发弹药起爆后，可能引发一连串爆炸。", "The shells and missiles in a magazine explode when heated or knocked. Once one round explodes, it may set off a chain of explosions."],
	"cx_m_munitions_b": ["在弹药附近切割会持续加热弹药，直至弹药起爆；一发弹药爆炸后，附近的弹药会接连殉爆。", "Cutting near a round keeps heating it until it explodes. After one round explodes, the rounds near it go off one after another in sympathetic detonation."],
	"cx_m_munitions_c": ["可以先打开注水阀淹没弹库，使弹药报废并消除危险；也可以远离弹药作业。", "You can open the flood valve first to flood the magazine, which makes the rounds scrap and removes the danger. You can also work far away from the rounds."],
	"cx_m_munitions_x": ["激光在弹药一定范围内工作时会持续加热弹药，温度达到烤燃温度后，弹药就会起爆。弹药以超过一定速度撞击物体时也会起爆。弹库的热测点显示温度最高的那发弹药的读数。注水后的弹药不再受加热或撞击影响，但也失去价值。", "When the laser works within a certain range of a round, it keeps heating the round, and once the temperature reaches the cook-off temperature the round explodes. A round also explodes if it hits an object faster than a certain speed. The magazine’s heat test point shows the reading of the hottest round. Rounds that have been flooded are no longer affected by heating or knocks, but they also lose their value."],
	"cx_m_quench": ["超导磁体失超", "SUPERCONDUCTING MAGNET QUENCH"],
	"cx_m_quench_a": ["八组超导线圈储存着磁能，液氦和冷箱负责维持超导状态。", "Eight coil packs store magnetic energy, and liquid helium and the cold box keep them superconducting."],
	"cx_m_quench_b": ["如果线圈失去冷却并升温超过临界温度，或在线圈仍有磁场时切断支撑，线圈就会失超，瞬间释放能量，并引发相邻线圈连锁失超。", "If a coil loses its cooling and warms above the critical temperature, or a support is cut while the coil still carries a field, the coil quenches and releases its energy instantly, and triggers a chain quench of the neighbouring coils."],
	"cx_m_quench_c": ["先合上泄能开关，保持冷箱供电。等储能读数降到安全值后，再断开冷却并拆卸线圈。", "Close the dump switch first and keep the cold box powered. When the stored-energy reading has dropped to a safe value, then switch off the cooling and remove the coils."],
	"cx_m_quench_x": ["泄能时，电流经泄能电阻按 e^(−t/τ) 衰减，经过几个时间常数后会降到安全值以下。此时线圈升温也不会造成危害。如果先断开冷却，线圈会在储存全部能量时升温超过临界温度。失超释放的热量和电磁力会损毁线圈与周围设备，还会烧掉一部分昂贵的液氦。", "When dumping, the current decays through the dump resistor as e^(−t/τ), and after a few time constants it falls below the safe value. At that point the coil can warm up without causing harm. If you switch off the cooling first, the coil warms above the critical temperature while still holding all its energy. The heat and electromagnetic forces released by the quench destroy the coil and the surrounding equipment, and also boil off some of the expensive liquid helium."],
	"cx_m_flywheel": ["还在转的飞轮", "A FLYWHEEL STILL SPINNING"],
	"cx_m_flywheel_a": ["飞轮在开局时的转速为 20,000 rpm，设备配有刹车、冷却系统和转速表。", "The flywheel starts at 20,000 rpm. The equipment comes with a brake, a cooling system and a tachometer."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_b": ["如果不开启冷却就直接刹车，卡钳会在 8 秒后烧坏，飞轮此后无法停下。如果在转速达到或超过 300 rpm 时松开飞轮，飞轮会甩出去。", "If you brake without turning on the cooling, the caliper burns out after 8 s and the flywheel can no longer be stopped. If you free the flywheel at 300 rpm or above, it is thrown out."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_c": ["先开启刹车冷却，再使用刹车。等转速降到 300 rpm 以下后拆卸飞轮；轨道预紧机构则从尾部向头部逐个松开。", "Turn on the brake cooling first, then use the brake. Remove the flywheel once the speed has dropped below 300 rpm. Release the rail preload mechanisms one by one from the tail towards the head."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_x": ["开启冷却后，刹车每秒降低 250 rpm，飞轮从 20,000 rpm 降下来约需 80 秒；不开冷却时，降速减半。飞轮能量与转速的平方成正比，转速降至 300 rpm 时，能量只剩开局时的 0.02%。断开主电源后，两组电容仍带有 400 V 电压，并为上轨的直线电机供电，拆卸前需要先放电。", "With cooling on, the brake takes 250 rpm off every second, so it takes about 80 s to bring the flywheel down from 20,000 rpm. Without cooling, the slowdown is half as fast. Flywheel energy is proportional to the square of its speed, so at 300 rpm only 0.02% of the starting energy is left. After the main supply is disconnected, the two capacitor banks still hold 400 V and supply the linear motor on the upper rail, so they must be discharged before removal."],
	"cx_m_pyro": ["救生舱火工品", "ESCAPE POD PYROTECHNICS"],
	"cx_m_pyro_a": ["每个救生舱有两个发射夹。前方发射夹装有爆炸螺栓，并连接独立的发射电容。", "Each pod has two launch clamps. The front launch clamp carries an explosive bolt and is connected to its own launch capacitor."],
	"cx_m_pyro_b": ["如果待发电路仍然带电时拆卸发射夹或火工品，爆炸螺栓会走火，将救生舱弹出。", "If you remove a launch clamp or a pyrotechnic charge while the arming circuit is still live, the explosive bolt fires and throws the pod out."],
	"cx_m_pyro_c": ["先在竖井的救生舱控制面板上断开待发开关，再拆卸发射夹；将火工品送往危险品口。", "Switch off the arming switch at the pod control panel in the shaft first, then remove the launch clamps. Send the pyrotechnic charges to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_m_pyro_x": ["发射电容是独立电源，主开关无法切断它。爆炸螺栓本身属于危险品，不能送入熔炉。某些合同中，一个救生舱的发射电路仍会带电，这就是“救生舱待发”事故。", "The launch capacitor is a separate supply, and the main switch cannot cut it off. The explosive bolts themselves are hazardous goods and must not be put into the furnace. In some contracts, the launch circuit of one escape pod is still live. This is the ‘armed pod’ incident."],
	"cx_m_magnet": ["残磁", "RESIDUAL MAGNETISM"],
	"cx_m_magnet_a": ["磁力牵引头断电后仍会保留磁场。", "The magnetic towing head keeps its magnetic field after the power is switched off."],
	"cx_m_magnet_b": ["磁场会吸引范围内的无人机和散落钢件，导致它们发生碰撞。", "The magnetic field attracts drones and loose steel parts within range, making them collide with the head."],
	"cx_m_magnet_c": ["先断开线圈电源，再使用退磁控件消磁，然后靠近牵引头。", "Disconnect the coil supply first, then use the degauss control to demagnetise the head, and only then go near the towing head."],
	"cx_m_magnet_x": ["铁磁材料被磁化后会保留剩磁。退磁时，逐渐衰减的交变磁场会打乱磁畴。退磁前必须断开线圈电源，否则线圈会重新磁化。", "Ferromagnetic material keeps some remanent magnetisation after being magnetised. In degaussing, a decaying alternating field scrambles the magnetic domains. The coil supply must be disconnected before degaussing, otherwise the coil magnetises the material again."],
	"cx_m_preload": ["预紧机构", "PRELOADED MECHANISMS"],
	"cx_m_preload_a": ["这些臂、轴、铰链和缆索依靠液压蓄能器或锁销保持支撑，并储存着力。", "These arms, shafts, hinges and cables are held in support by hydraulic accumulators or locking pins, and they store force."],
	"cx_m_preload_b": ["如果锁销尚未拔出或液压系统仍有压力就拆卸枢轴，机构会弹开，损坏自身和撞上的物体。", "If you remove a pivot while a locking pin is still in or the hydraulic system is still under pressure, the mechanism springs open and damages itself and whatever it hits."],
	"cx_m_preload_c": ["先释放蓄能器内的压力，再拔出全部锁销。确认张力表归零后，最后拆卸枢轴。", "Release the pressure in the accumulator first, then pull out all the locking pins. Once the tension gauge reads zero, remove the pivot last."],
	"cx_m_preload_x": ["预紧机构储存弹性能和液压能：拉缆的能量 E = F²L/2EA，蓄能器的能量 E ≈ pV·ln(p/p₀)。卸能顺序始终是“能量—锁—结构”。如果拆除锁销后没有泄压，全部作用力会集中在枢轴上，松开枢轴时就会释放。", "A preload mechanism stores elastic energy and hydraulic energy. For a pulled cable, the energy is E = F²L/2EA; for an accumulator, E ≈ pV·ln(p/p₀). The order of unloading is always energy, then locks, then structure. If you remove the locking pins without releasing the pressure, all the force acts on the pivot, and it is released as soon as the pivot is loosened."],
	"cx_m_drones": ["各自带电的无人机", "DRONES WITH THEIR OWN POWER"],
	"cx_m_drones_a": ["机库里的每个机位和每架无人机都配有独立电池。", "Every bay and every drone in the hangar has its own battery."],
	"cx_m_drones_b": ["断开主电池后，机位和无人机仍然带电。如果机身电池尚未拆除就松开无人机，无人机会启动并撞上机位。", "After the main battery is disconnected, the bays and drones are still live. If you release a drone while its onboard battery is still fitted, the drone starts up and crashes into its bay."],
	"cx_m_drones_c": ["先断开机位充电开关和机身电池开关，再拔掉两根线、拆下电池包，最后将无人机整机运走。", "Switch off the bay charging switch and the airframe battery switch first, then unplug the two leads and remove the battery pack, and finally move the whole drone away."],
	"cx_m_drones_x": ["无人机的飞控系统失去链路后会尝试自主起飞。只有物理断开电池，才能确认安全。将无人机整机交付到设备口，比将其熔成废料的价值高得多。", "When a drone’s flight controller loses its link, it tries to take off on its own. Only a physically disconnected battery is safe. A drone delivered whole to the equipment bay is worth much more than one melted down for scrap."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: cryogenics
	"cx_m_cryo_tank": ["低温货罐", "CRYOGENIC CARGO TANKS"],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_a": ["低温货罐安装在真空夹套内，罐内压力会随着温度变化。", "The cryogenic cargo tanks are fitted inside vacuum jackets, and the pressure in a tank changes with its temperature."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_b": ["货罐回温后，内部压力会升高。如果安全阀冻住，压力可能持续升高，最终导致货罐爆裂。真空夹套破损后，漏热速度会加快十倍。", "When a tank warms up, the pressure inside rises. If the relief valve is frozen, the pressure can keep rising until the tank bursts. When the vacuum jacket is damaged, heat leaks in ten times faster."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_c": ["保持制冷机运行，从货罐接口抽走液体。如果安全阀已经冻住，先加热解冻。", "Keep the chillers running and draw the liquid off through the tank ports. If a relief valve is frozen, heat it to thaw it first."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_x": ["货罐里有液体时，蒸气压大约每升高 20 °C 翻一倍。真空夹套完好时，漏热速度很慢，在一份合同的作业时间内温度升幅不到 10 °C；夹套破损后，温度上升会快得多。", "With liquid in the tank, the vapour pressure roughly doubles for every 20 °C rise. While the vacuum jacket is intact, heat leaks in slowly, and the temperature rises by less than 10 °C within the working time of one contract. Once the jacket is damaged, the temperature rises much faster."],
	"cx_m_boiloff": ["蒸发升压", "BOIL-OFF"],
	"cx_m_boiloff_a": ["低温罐里的液体会持续蒸发，使罐内压力升高。制冷系统运行时，罐压能够保持稳定。", "The liquid in the cryogenic tanks keeps boiling off, which raises the tank pressure. While the refrigeration system is running, the tank pressure stays stable."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_b": ["如果先切断电源，制冷系统停止运行，罐压就会升高，可能导致安全阀放空、货物损失，甚至引发爆罐。", "If you cut the power first, the refrigeration system stops running and the tank pressure rises. This may make the relief valve vent, losing cargo, or even make the tank burst."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_c": ["保持制冷系统运行，同时用软管抽走液体；抽出的液体越多，罐压越低。最后再切断电源。", "Keep the refrigeration system running and draw the liquid off through the hose at the same time. The more you draw off, the lower the tank pressure. Cut the power last."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_x": ["蒸发后的气体体积是液体的几百倍，因此少量漏热也会使罐压明显升高。保温层破损后，压力上升得更快；安全阀排出的气体也是货物的一部分。", "Boiled-off gas takes up hundreds of times the volume of the liquid, so even a small heat leak raises the tank pressure noticeably. When the insulation is damaged, the pressure rises faster. The gas vented by the relief valve is part of the cargo too."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve": ["冻住的安全阀", "A FROZEN RELIEF VALVE"],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_a": ["安全阀出口结了冰，阀门被冻住，无法正常泄压。", "One tank's relief valve has an ice plug in its outlet and won't lift."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_b": ["罐内压力超过安全值，阀门也打不开。压力继续升高，可能导致爆罐。", "Past its set pressure it doesn't relieve; the tank climbs on until it bursts."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_c": ["先测阀门温度。如果结冰，就加热解冻；也可以先抽走罐内气体，降低压力。", "Read each relief valve's temperature: thaw the abnormally cold one with its heater, or draw its tank down first."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_x": ["泄放的低温气体在出口膨胀降温，空气或水汽在出口冻成冰塞。测温探针能发现它：冻住的阀比其它阀冷得多。", "Cold gas venting through the outlet expands and chills it, freezing moisture into an ice plug. The probe shows it: the frozen valve reads far colder than the rest."],
	"cx_m_dilution": ["稀释制冷机按序回温", "DILUTION FRIDGE WARM-UP"],
	"cx_m_dilution_a": ["量子芯片放在混合室里，温度接近绝对零度。外面有好几层冷板，靠制冷机一直降温。", "The qubit chip sits in the mixing chamber at millikelvin, hung under stage after stage."],
	"cx_m_dilution_b": ["混合气还没回收就停冷头，气体受热沸腾，可能损坏冷板。芯片温度太低时直接加热，也可能裂开。", "Stop the cold head before recovering the mixture and it boils off; heat it or touch it while still at millikelvin and the chip cracks."],
	"cx_m_dilution_c": ["先停循环泵，回收混合气，再停脉管冷头。等冷板自然回温后再加热，拆卸前锁住隔振台。", "Stop circulation → recover the mixture → stop the pulse tube → let the stages warm, heaters only past the coldest → lock the isolation table before any cutting."],
	"cx_m_dilution_x": ["混合室最冷、回温最慢。在低于热震温度时打开加热器，芯片表面和内部温差太大，硅片会裂；低于脆性温度时任何振动都能让它碎。隔振台没锁，附近的切割会通过台面震到芯片。", "The mixing chamber is coldest and warms slowest. Heaters switched on below the shock temperature put too much difference between the chip's surface and its body and the silicon cracks; below the brittle temperature any shake breaks it. With the isolation table unlocked, a nearby cut shakes the chip."],
	"cx_m_coldchain": ["冷链不能断", "THE COLD CHAIN"],
	"cx_m_coldchain_a": ["三个冷舱的温度保持在 −25 °C，由冷机和制冷主机提供冷却。", "The temperature of the three cold holds is kept at −25 °C, with cooling supplied by the chillers and the refrigeration plant."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_b": ["如果切断电源或损坏制冷系统，冷舱就会逐渐回温。温度超过 −5 °C 后，货物会解冻，价值只剩原来的 45%。", "If you cut the power or damage the refrigeration system, the cold holds gradually warm up. Once the temperature goes above −5 °C, the cargo thaws and keeps only 45% of its value."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_c": ["先在外部面板接通“船坞临时供冷”，然后再切断电源，拆除原有制冷系统。", "First connect ‘berth temporary cooling’ at the outside panel, then cut the power and remove the original refrigeration system."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_x": ["冷冻货物需要始终保持低温；一旦解冻，价值损失无法挽回。制冷剂需要从储液罐的回收口闭环回收。打开舱顶货舱口之前，还要先给舱室放气。", "Frozen cargo must be kept cold at all times. Once it thaws, the loss of value cannot be recovered. The refrigerant must be recovered in a closed loop at the receiver’s recovery port. Before opening a hold’s roof hatch, also vent the hold first."],
	"cx_m_ice": ["冰体", "THE ICE"],
	"cx_m_ice_a": ["整座冰山都是需要回收的货物。每块冰含有 0.6 m³ 的水，可以用加热垫逐块融化。", "The whole iceberg is cargo to be recovered. Each block contains 0.6 m³ of water and can be melted block by block with the heater pads."],
	"cx_m_ice_b": ["如果融水积累到 3 m³ 仍未抽走，而且总线还带电，发动机舱就会发生短路。如果鞍座仍夹住冰体时切割裂纹处，冰体就会裂开。", "If 3 m³ of melt water has built up without being drawn off and the bus is still live, the engine room shorts out. If you cut along a crack while the saddles are still clamping the ice, the ice splits."],
	"cx_m_ice_c": ["启动加热垫，融化冰块的同时，从水总管接口抽走融水。等剩余冰体不到一半时，再松开鞍座。", "Switch on the heater pads, and draw the melt water off at the water header port as the blocks melt. Release the saddles only once less than half of the ice is left."],
	"cx_m_ice_x": ["融化 1 kg 的冰需要 334 kJ 的能量。冰的切割速度很慢，因为切口会重新冻结。应变表显示冰体裂纹的扩展程度，初始读数为 90%。", "Melting 1 kg of ice takes 334 kJ of energy. Ice cuts very slowly, because the kerf freezes over again. The strain gauge shows how far the crack in the ice has spread, and its initial reading is 90%."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: fluids
	"cx_m_drill_torque": ["钻杆残余扭矩与泥浆压力", "TRAPPED TORQUE AND MUD PRESSURE"],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_a": ["八节立根仍然带有残余扭矩，钻杆内部也有受压的泥浆。", "The eight stands still hold residual torque, and the inside of the drill pipe holds pressurised mud."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_b": ["钻杆带有扭矩时卸扣，钻杆可能反弹、扭断并甩打钻台；带压卸扣则会使泥浆喷出，污染设备。", "If you break out a connection while the pipe is under torque, the pipe may spring back, twist off and whip against the drill floor. If you break it out under pressure, mud sprays out and contaminates the equipment."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_c": ["关闭转盘刹车释放扭矩，等扭矩表读数低于 5%。再打开泄压阀排出可回收的泥浆，最后拆卸钻杆接头。", "Release the rotary brake to bleed the torque, until the torque gauge reads below 5%. Then open the relief valve to drain off the recoverable mud, and finally break out the tool joints."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_x": ["扭矩按照时间常数呈指数下降。通过泄压阀排到回收口的泥浆可以作为货物回收。扭矩表和压力表都安装在钻台上。", "The torque decays exponentially according to a time constant. The mud drained through the relief valve to the recovery port can be recovered as cargo. The torque gauge and the pressure gauge are both mounted on the drill floor."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips": ["卡瓦与自上而下", "SLIPS, TOP DOWN"],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_a": ["每节立根下方都有一副卡瓦，用来托住该节立根和下面的整串钻杆。", "Under each stand there is a set of slips, which holds that stand and the whole drill string below it."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_b": ["如果先卸下面的钻杆，上面的钻杆会因失去支撑而掉落。如果卡瓦没有安装到位就卸扣，下方整串钻杆会掉进井内。", "If you break out a lower stand first, the pipe above loses its support and drops. If you break out a connection while the slips are not properly set, the whole drill string below falls into the hole."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_c": ["从最上面一节开始拆卸。每拆一节之前，都要确认下方的卡瓦已经安装到位，再逐节向下拆卸。", "Start with the top stand. Before breaking out each stand, check that the slips below it are set, then work downwards stand by stand."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_x": ["卡瓦由楔形牙块组成，钻杆越重，卡瓦夹得越紧。拆卸期间，必须始终使用卡瓦或吊卡固定钻杆。", "Slips are wedge-shaped dies, and the heavier the pipe, the tighter they grip. During the work, the drill string must always be held by the slips or the elevator."],
	"cx_m_tanknet": ["交叉连通罐", "CROSS-CONNECTED TANKS"],
	"cx_m_tanknet_a": ["三个储罐通过交叉阀连接到同一根总管，大型泵通过泵房回收口抽取总管里的液体。", "Three tanks are connected to one header through crossover valves, and the big pump draws the liquid from the header through the pump room’s recovery port."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_b": ["如果提前断电，回收泵就无法运行。液体抽干后继续运行水泵，会因空转而损坏水泵；如果先排掉罐顶气体再抽液，储罐可能被吸瘪。", "If you cut the power early, the recovery pump cannot run. If the pump keeps running after the liquid has been drawn off, it runs dry and is damaged. If you vent the ullage gas from the tank tops before drawing the liquid, the tank gets sucked flat."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_c": ["打开交叉阀，在保持增压的情况下抽完液体并关闭回收口，再关闭增压阀、排出罐顶气体。支管中的残液需要从低点排放口抽走。", "Open the crossover valves, draw the liquid off while keeping the pressurisation on, and close the recovery port. Then close the pressurisation valve and vent the ullage gas from the tank tops. Draw the residual liquid in the branch lines off at the low-point drains."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_x": ["交叉阀打开后，各储罐的液位会通过总管逐渐趋于一致。增压阀打开时，氮气球罐会维持储罐压力，避免抽液时产生真空。有些合同中的交叉阀虽然显示关闭，但实际存在内漏，关闭后相应储罐的液位仍会下降。", "With the crossover valves open, the liquid levels in the tanks gradually even out through the header. While the pressurisation valve is open, the nitrogen sphere keeps up the tank pressure and prevents a vacuum forming during drawing. In some contracts, a crossover valve reads closed but actually leaks internally, so the level in the corresponding tank keeps falling even with it closed."],
	"cx_m_immersion": ["浸没冷却", "IMMERSION COOLING"],
	"cx_m_immersion_a": ["十二个机柜分别安装在装有绝缘冷却液的液槽中。", "Twelve racks each stand in a tank of dielectric coolant."],
	"cx_m_immersion_b": ["如果液槽中还有冷却液就吊出机柜，液体会洒出，导致同一排的相邻机柜短路。", "If you lift out a rack while its tank still holds coolant, the liquid spills and short-circuits the neighbouring racks in the same row."],
	"cx_m_immersion_c": ["先通过每个液槽的接口抽干冷却液，再吊出机柜。", "Draw each tank dry through its port first, then lift out the rack."],
	"cx_m_immersion_x": ["冷却液本身价值较高，按回收体积计价。在失重环境中，洒出的液体会形成液团，并漂向相邻机柜。", "The coolant itself is valuable and is paid by recovered volume. In free fall, the spilt liquid forms globules and drifts onto the neighbouring racks."],
	"cx_m_custody": ["数据监管", "DATA CUSTODY"],
	"cx_m_custody_a": ["存储阵列中的硬盘属于客户的监管物品，需要装入屏蔽运输箱。", "The drives in the storage array are the client’s items held in custody, and must be latched into shielded transport bays."],
	"cx_m_custody_b": ["如果没有拨动监管锁扣就拔出硬盘，会被判定为违约并受到罚款。", "If you pull a drive without throwing its custody latch, it counts as a breach of contract and you are fined."],
	"cx_m_custody_c": ["先拨动每块硬盘的监管锁扣，再将运输箱完整送到设备回收口。", "Throw each drive’s custody latch first, then take the transport bays, complete, to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_m_custody_x": ["运输箱本身也是合同指定物品。锁好锁扣后，硬盘作为客户封存的财产，按完整物品计价。", "The transport bays are themselves items named in the contract. Once latched, the drives are the client’s sealed property and are paid as whole items."],
	"cx_m_waterball": ["失重水球", "THE WATER BALL"],
	"cx_m_waterball_a": ["网罩内有几十立方米的水，水中养着鱼。", "The net holds tens of cubic metres of water, with fish living in it."],
	"cx_m_waterball_b": ["如果切割或拆除网罩和支架，水球会散开，造成水资源损失，并使舱内电气设备进水。如果总线仍带电，还会发生短路，鱼也会死亡。", "If you cut or remove the net or its frame, the water ball bursts. Water is lost, and the room’s electrical equipment is soaked. If the bus is still live, it also shorts out, and the fish die."],
	"cx_m_waterball_c": ["先用泵抽走部分水，直到剩余水量降到安全范围，再拆除网罩。鱼苗箱属于合同指定物品。", "Pump out part of the water first, until the remaining amount is down to the safe range, then remove the net. The fish holding tank is an item named in the contract."],
	"cx_m_waterball_x": ["在失重环境中，表面张力使水聚集成球，网罩负责托住水球。30 m³ 水的质量为 30 吨；水球散开后，水团会保持原有速度并向各处漂移。", "In free fall, surface tension pulls the water into a ball, and the net only cradles it. 30 m³ of water has a mass of 30 tonnes. When the ball bursts, the water drifts apart in all directions, keeping its original speed."],
	"cx_m_media": ["外观相同的三种介质", "THREE LOOK-ALIKE MEDIA"],
	"cx_m_media_a": ["三只储罐分别装有溶剂、酸液和乙二醇。三路管道外观相同，并且在途中交叉。", "Solvent, acid and glycol are in three separate tanks. The three pipes look identical and cross each other on the way."],
	"cx_m_media_b": ["抽取其中一种液体时，如果没有关闭另外两路阀门，三种介质会混合成废液，失去回收价值，还会产生处理费用。", "If you draw one of the liquids without closing the valves of the other two branches, the three media mix into waste liquid, which has no recovery value and also incurs a disposal fee."],
	"cx_m_media_c": ["先在总管各个接口旁的取样点检查介质，再关闭另外两路阀门，最后抽取对应液体。", "First check each medium at the sampling point beside each header port, then close the valves of the other two branches, and finally draw the corresponding liquid."],
	"cx_m_media_x": ["总管 1 号口连接 3 号罐，2 号口连接 1 号罐，3 号口连接 2 号罐；不取样就可能接错。如果支管里仍有液体就拆除总管，各路液体都会泄漏，并按泄漏量罚款。分离器可能有残余压力，需要通过塔上的接口泄压。", "Header port 1 connects to tank 3, port 2 connects to tank 1, and port 3 connects to tank 2. Without sampling, you may connect the wrong one. If you remove the header while the branch lines still hold liquid, all the liquids leak and you are fined by the leaked volume. The separator may hold residual pressure, which must be relieved at the port on the tower."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: atmosphere, fire, contamination
	"cx_m_o2_flash": ["富氧闪燃", "OXYGEN-RICH FLASH FIRE"],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_a": ["各个舱室的氧气浓度不同，部分舱室的氧气浓度远高于普通空气中的 21%。", "The oxygen concentration differs between rooms, and in some rooms it is far above the 21% of ordinary air."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_b": ["舱室有气压且氧气浓度超过阈值时，在附近使用激光会引发全舱闪燃，烧坏设备并损伤无人机。", "When a room has pressure and its oxygen concentration is over the threshold, using the laser nearby causes a flash fire in the whole room, burning the equipment and damaging the drone."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_c": ["先检查各舱室的氧气浓度，分别通过各自的接口放气，再使用激光。", "First check the oxygen concentration in each room and vent each room through its own port, then use the laser."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_x": ["氧气浓度从 21% 升至 35% 以上时，可燃物的点燃温度会明显下降，燃烧速度也会成倍提高，织物和塑料更容易被点燃。打开舱门后，两侧舱室的空气会混合。", "When oxygen rises from 21% to over 35%, the ignition temperature of combustible materials falls markedly and burning rates increase several times over, so fabrics and plastics ignite more easily. After a door is opened, the air in the rooms on both sides mixes."],
	"cx_m_composite": ["复合材料毒烟", "COMPOSITE FUMES"],
	"cx_m_composite_a": ["机身板件由碳纤维复合材料制成，并通过螺栓固定。", "The airframe panels are made of carbon-fibre composite and are fixed with bolts."],
	"cx_m_composite_b": ["在有气体的舱室附近用激光切割板件，会产生有毒烟雾，使电子设备价值降低、玻璃起雾。", "If you cut a panel with the laser near a room that holds air, it produces toxic smoke, which lowers the value of electronics and fogs glass."],
	"cx_m_composite_c": ["拧下螺栓，整块拆除板件；也可以先将舱室抽成真空，再进行切割。", "Unbolt the panels and remove them whole. Alternatively, vent the room to vacuum first and then cut."],
	"cx_m_composite_x": ["环氧树脂基体受激光加热后会发生热解，产生一氧化碳、氰化氢和细碳纤维粉尘。将舱室抽成真空时，烟雾会随空气一同排出。", "The epoxy resin matrix pyrolyses when heated by the laser, producing carbon monoxide, hydrogen cyanide and fine carbon-fibre dust. When the room is vented to vacuum, the smoke leaves with the air."],
	"cx_m_radiation": ["辐射阴影", "RADIATION SHADOW"],
	"cx_m_radiation_a": ["反应堆虽然已经停止运行，但堆芯附近仍然有很强的辐射，距离堆芯 1 米的位置，辐射剂量率还有 3.2 Sv/h。屏蔽板、掩蔽间和液氢罐都可以阻挡辐射，在它们后面会形成相对安全的区域。", "Although the reactor has stopped running, the area near the core still has strong radiation. At 1 metre from the core, the radiation dose rate is still 3.2 Sv/h. The shield, the shelter and the liquid hydrogen tanks can all block radiation, and the area behind them is relatively safe."],
	"cx_m_radiation_b": ["无人机受到的累计辐射剂量超过 150 mSv 后，电子设备就会开始出现故障。如果使用激光切割设备直接切到堆芯，还会引发核爆炸。", "Once the drone’s accumulated radiation dose exceeds 150 mSv, its electronics start to fail. If you cut the equipment with the laser straight into the core, it also causes a nuclear explosion."],
	"cx_m_radiation_c": ["先用吊车把屏蔽板移动到堆芯前面，利用屏蔽板挡住辐射，再让无人机进入后方区域进行拆卸。操作之前还要锁定控制鼓，最后把整个堆芯从危险品出口运走，不要直接切割堆芯。", "First use the crane to move the shield in front of the core, use it to block the radiation, then let the drone enter the area behind it to work. Before working, also lock the control drums, and finally send the whole core out through the hazard mouth. Do not cut the core directly."],
	"cx_m_radiation_x": ["距离堆芯越远，受到的辐射就越少，剂量率会按照距离平方的反比下降。在距离堆芯 7 米的位置，剂量率大约还有 65 mSv/h，停留一分多钟就可能超过安全剂量。游戏里每经过 1 秒，都会按照现实中的 2 分钟计算辐射剂量。\n屏蔽板可以阻挡辐射，只要把屏蔽板放在堆芯和无人机之间，无人机就能利用后面的辐射阴影进行作业。屏蔽板即使还吊在吊车上，也一样能够发挥作用。剂量探头显示的是当前位置的辐射剂量率，可以根据读数判断作业区域是否安全。", "The farther you are from the core, the less radiation you receive, and the dose rate falls with the inverse square of the distance. At 7 metres from the core, the dose rate is still about 65 mSv/h, and staying a little over a minute there may exceed the safe dose. In the game, every 1 second that passes counts as 2 minutes of real time for the radiation dose.\nThe shield can block radiation. As long as you put the shield between the core and the drone, the drone can work in the radiation shadow behind it. The shield works even while it is still hanging from the crane. The dose probe shows the radiation dose rate at its current position, and you can judge from the reading whether the work area is safe."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat": ["停机不等于冷却", "STOPPED ISN'T COLD"],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_a": ["炉芯或堆芯停止运行后，温度仍可能达到几百度，需要依靠冷却回路降温。", "After a furnace core or reactor core stops running, its temperature may still reach several hundred degrees, and it must be cooled down by its cooling loop."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_b": ["高温时切断冷却，热冲击可能使炉芯或堆芯开裂。尚未冷却完成时吊出炉芯或收起散热瓣，也可能造成开裂或变形。", "If you cut the cooling while it is hot, thermal shock may crack the furnace core or reactor core. Lifting out the core, or folding the radiator petals, before cooling is complete can also cause cracking or deformation."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_c": ["保持冷却泵供电，并确保冷却回路充满冷却液。观察温度，等炉芯或堆芯充分冷却后，再断电并吊出。", "Keep the cooling pump powered and make sure the cooling loop is full of coolant. Watch the temperature, and once the furnace core or reactor core has cooled enough, cut the power and lift it out."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_x": ["冷却回路运行时，温度约每秒下降 4 °C。MF-126 炉芯在 350 °C 以上停止冷却会开裂，在 150 °C 以上吊出会开裂；NR-95 堆芯在 60 °C 以上收起散热瓣会变形。", "While the cooling loop is running, the temperature falls by about 4 °C per second. The MF-126 furnace core cracks if cooling is stopped above 350 °C, and cracks if lifted out above 150 °C. The NR-95 reactor core deforms if the radiator petals are folded above 60 °C."],
	"cx_m_thermal": ["近日点余热", "PERIHELION HEAT"],
	"cx_m_thermal_a": ["飞船刚刚掠过太阳，各区域的隔热瓦和前部壳体温度达到 300–800 °C。", "The ship has just passed close to the sun, and the heat tiles and forward hull in each zone are at 300–800 °C."],
	"cx_m_thermal_b": ["在高温区域切割隔热瓦会导致隔热瓦破碎；从高温区域取出的设备可能被高温损坏；无人机进入最热区域也会受到损伤。", "Cutting a heat tile in a hot zone makes the tile shatter. Equipment taken out of a hot zone may be damaged by the heat. The drone is also damaged if it enters the hottest zone."],
	"cx_m_thermal_c": ["接通船坞冷却回路，加快降温。使用测温探针检查各区域的温度，冷却后再开始拆除。", "Connect the berth cooling loop to speed up the cooling. Check the temperature of each zone with the temperature probe, and start the removal once it has cooled."],
	"cx_m_thermal_x": ["在真空环境中，设备只能通过热辐射散热，各区域会以不同速度自然冷却。冷却回路能够接入的区域降温更快。", "In vacuum, equipment can only lose heat by thermal radiation, and each zone cools naturally at a different rate. Zones that the cooling loop can reach cool faster."],
	"cx_m_bio": ["负压与生物污染", "NEGATIVE PRESSURE AND BIOHAZARD"],
	"cx_m_bio_a": ["隔离舱的压力低于相邻舱室，舱内的生物废物箱、滤芯和废液罐都带有污染物。", "The pressure in an isolation room is lower than in the neighbouring rooms, and the biohazard boxes, filters and waste tanks inside it are contaminated."],
	"cx_m_bio_b": ["如果切开危险品或在未密封时搬运，污染物会进入舱内空气并随气流扩散。干净舱室受到污染后，设备价值会降低四分之一。", "If you cut a hazardous item open, or move it without sealing it, the contaminant gets into the room air and spreads with the airflow. When a clean room is contaminated, the value of its equipment drops by a quarter."],
	"cx_m_bio_c": ["先密封每件生物危险品，再通过回收软管的滤芯放气，最后打开舱门。", "Seal every biohazard item first, then vent through the filter on the recovery hose, and finally open the doors."],
	"cx_m_bio_x": ["负压使空气流向隔离舱，限制污染物向外扩散。如果打开舱门或切开舱壁，负压条件就会消失，气流方向可能反转。回收软管的过滤器可以过滤空气中的污染物。", "Negative pressure makes air flow towards the isolation room, which limits contaminants from spreading outwards. If a door is opened or a wall is cut, the negative pressure is lost and the airflow may reverse. The filter on the recovery hose removes contaminants from the air."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: loads and motion
	"cx_m_balance": ["按受力顺序释放", "RELEASE IN ORDER OF LOAD"],
	"cx_m_balance_a": ["卷扬机缆绳仍然绷紧，两台外挂吊舱分别安装在舰尾的上方和下方。", "The winch cable is still taut, and the two outboard pods are mounted aft, one above and one below the stern."],
	"cx_m_balance_b": ["如果没有松开刹车就拆除卷扬轴，卷筒会被甩出。如果只拆除一台吊舱，另一台吊舱的载荷会使船体扭转。", "If you remove the winch shaft without releasing the brake, the drum is thrown out. If you remove only one pod, the load of the other pod twists the hull."],
	"cx_m_balance_c": ["先拔出刹车销，确认张力表读数归零。拆除吊舱前，在舰尾设置船体支撑，或者同时拆除两台吊舱。", "Pull the brake pins first and make sure the tension gauge reads zero. Before removing a pod, set the hull support at the stern, or remove both pods together."],
	"cx_m_balance_x": ["对称安装的两个重物可以相互平衡。拆掉其中一个后，船体需要承受另一个重物产生的全部力矩；如果超过承载能力，吊梁和支柱就会扭坏。锁喉夹块受到的力来自卷扬机缆绳，需要处理刹车、锁销和蓄能器。", "Two weights mounted symmetrically balance each other. After one is removed, the hull has to carry the whole moment of the other weight, and if that exceeds its capacity, the beams and struts twist and fail. The load on the throat clamp block comes from the winch cable, so the brake, the locking pins and the accumulator all have to be dealt with."],
	"cx_m_sandwich": ["拆三明治", "UNMAKING THE SANDWICH"],
	"cx_m_sandwich_a": ["上下两条船体通过 8 个液压夹钳夹住中间的居住舱。", "The upper and lower hulls clamp the habitat between them with 8 hydraulic clamps."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_b": ["货舱没有放气就松开夹钳，夹钳会弹开。如果一侧比另一侧多松开两个夹钳，货舱会发生扭转，已经开裂的横梁 2 也会断裂。", "If you release a clamp before the hold is vented, the clamp springs open. If one side has two more clamps released than the other, the hold twists, and the already cracked beam 2 also breaks."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_c": ["先给货舱放气，再按以下顺序交叉成对松开夹钳：上1→下4→上4→下1→上2→下3→上3→下2。松开上1和下1后，再拆除横梁 2。", "Vent the hold first, then release the clamps in crossed pairs in this order: U1→L4→U4→L1→U2→L3→U3→L2. Remove beam 2 after U1 and L1 have been released."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_x": ["横梁 2 已经开裂，载荷表读数为 192 kN，其余横梁的读数为 120 kN。如果夹钳仍处于保压状态时整件拆下，钳口会弹开。三套电路相互独立：上部船体使用主电池，下部船体和货舱各有独立电池。", "Beam 2 is already cracked, and its load cell reads 192 kN, while the other beams read 120 kN. If a clamp is removed whole while it is still holding pressure, its jaw springs open. The three circuits are independent of each other: the upper hull uses the main battery, and the lower hull and the hold each have their own battery."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam": ["货柜就是承力梁", "THE CONTAINERS ARE THE BEAM"],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_a": ["货柜通过四角的扭锁相互连接，整列货柜共同构成船体的承力箱梁。", "The containers are connected to each other by twist-locks at the four corners, and each column of containers together forms a load-bearing box beam of the hull."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_b": ["外侧货柜仍在时卸空内侧一列，会使该列结构弯曲。同一列货柜如果从下往上拆，上面的货柜会压下来。切断仍然绷紧的拉杆，拉杆会回弹。", "If you empty an inner column while the outer containers are still there, that column buckles. If you remove containers in a column from the bottom up, the ones above come down. If you cut a tie rod that is still tight, the rod whips back."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_c": ["从两端向中间卸货，每列从上往下拆。拆除拉杆前，先松开花篮螺丝，确认拉力计读数为 0；带压货柜需要先抽气。", "Unload from both ends towards the middle, and work each column from the top down. Before removing a tie rod, slacken the turnbuckles and check that the tension gauge reads 0. Pump down pressurised containers first."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_x": ["船坞夹具固定着第 4 列。每列的弯曲程度等于外侧仍在位货柜的数量乘以力臂，再除以本列的刚度；刚度由弦杆和在位货柜数量决定。应变片显示本列弯曲程度占极限的百分比。住人箱的压力为 60 kPa，低温箱为 450 kPa。", "The berth clamps hold column 4. The bending of each column equals the number of containers still in place outboard of it times the lever arm, divided by the stiffness of the column itself; the stiffness is set by the chords and the number of containers in place. The strain gauges show the bending of the column as a percentage of its limit. Accommodation boxes are at 60 kPa, and cryogenic boxes at 450 kPa."],
	"cx_m_sail": ["帆的张力网", "THE SAIL'S TENSION NET"],
	"cx_m_sail_a": ["四台绞盘的刹车分别固定四个象限的帆膜和撑索，每根撑索的张力为 12 kN。", "Four winch brakes hold the film and stays of the four quadrants in place, and the tension in each stay is 12 kN."],
	"cx_m_sail_b": ["帆膜仍然绷紧时切割，会产生向两侧扩展的裂口。切断撑索会使角梁甩向吊舱。如果没有接地就接触帆膜，静电会损伤无人机。", "If you cut the film while it is taut, it produces tears that spread to both sides. Cutting a stay makes the corner spar whip towards the gondola. If you touch the film without earthing, static discharge damages the drone."],
	"cx_m_sail_c": ["先连接接地线 GND，从右侧检修门洞进入通道，通过舱门旁的 G-G 接口抽气，再打开舱门 HT-G。随后松开绞盘刹车 W，启动收帆电机 F，将四角的帆膜卷起。", "First connect the GND earth lead, enter the lane through the service gate on the right, vent through the G-G port beside the hatch, then open hatch HT-G. Then release the winch brakes W and start the furling motors F to roll up the film at the four corners."],
	"cx_m_sail_x": ["完整收帆时，先连接左下角的接地线 GND。外框和撑索包围着吊舱，右侧外框留有检修门洞，门洞后方有一条没有帆膜的通道，可以通过这里飞到舱门，避免撞破帆膜。将软管接到舱门旁的 G-G 气口，把舱压抽到 5 kPa 以下，再打开舱门 HT-G。进入后，依次松开 W-NW、W-NE、W-SE、W-SW 四台绞盘的刹车，让四角的帆膜松弛。然后启动 F-NW、F-NE、F-SE、F-SW 四台收帆电机，将四角的帆膜逐块卷上绞盘。最后拆下四个帆卷，送往设备回收口。", "To furl the sail whole, first connect the earth lead GND at the bottom left. The frame and stays enclose the gondola. The right-hand frame has a service gate, and behind the gate there is a lane with no film, through which you can fly to the hatch without breaking the film. Connect the hose to the G-G port beside the hatch, pump the gondola pressure down below 5 kPa, then open hatch HT-G. Once inside, release the brakes on the four winches W-NW, W-NE, W-SE and W-SW in turn, so that the film at the four corners goes slack. Then start the four furling motors F-NW, F-NE, F-SE and F-SW, and roll the film at each corner onto its winch piece by piece. Finally, remove the four sail rolls and send them to the equipment mouth."],
	"cx_m_softshell": ["软壳气囊", "SOFT-SHELL GASBAGS"],
	"cx_m_softshell_a": ["每个气囊的内部压力为 30 kPa，气囊依靠内压维持形状，并配有张紧器和束缚带。", "The internal pressure of each gasbag is 30 kPa. The gasbags keep their shape by internal pressure and are fitted with tensioners and restraint straps."],
	"cx_m_softshell_b": ["气囊充气时直接切割，囊壁会撕裂并坍塌，砸坏附近设备。如果张紧器仍在工作就拆除束缚带，带子会回弹。", "If you cut a gasbag while it is inflated, the wall tears and collapses, smashing nearby equipment. If you remove a strap while the tensioner is still working, the strap whips back."],
	"cx_m_softshell_c": ["依次处理每个气囊：先将气压抽到 3 kPa 以下，使气囊折叠；再松开张紧器，拆除束缚带，最后拆下气囊。", "Deal with the gasbags one at a time. First pump the pressure below 3 kPa so that the bag folds, then release the tensioner and remove the restraint straps, and finally remove the bag."],
	"cx_m_softshell_x": ["织物壳体只能承受拉力，不能承受压力；泄气后，气囊会失去原来的形状。服务舱电池是独立电源，切断脊柱电池后仍然带电，电容也有单独的放电点。", "A fabric shell can only carry tension, not compression. When it is deflated, the gasbag loses its shape. The service bay battery is an independent supply and is still live after the spine battery is cut off. The capacitor also has its own discharge point."],
	"cx_m_tether": ["旋转的系绳", "A SPINNING TETHER"],
	"cx_m_tether_a": ["两个吊舱由系绳连接，整体以 2.0 rpm 的速度旋转，张紧器还提供 8 kN 的额外张力。", "The two pods are joined by a tether, and the whole assembly rotates at 2.0 rpm. The tensioner adds an extra 8 kN of tension."],
	"cx_m_tether_b": ["旋转时切断系绳，两个吊舱会沿切线方向甩出。如果不打开冷却就制动，滚轮在 6 秒后会打滑，导致制动器永久失效。", "If you cut the tether while it is rotating, the two pods fly off along the tangent. If you brake without turning on the cooling, the rollers slip after 6 seconds and the brake fails permanently."],
	"cx_m_tether_c": ["先启动制动冷却，再进行制动。等吊舱停止旋转后，松开张紧器并拆除系绳。暂时保留推进剂：制动失效时，需要使用 B 舱的姿态控制系统反向喷射。", "Start the brake cooling first, then brake. Once the pods have stopped rotating, release the tensioner and remove the tether. Keep the propellant for now: if the brake fails, you have to fire the attitude control system on pod B in reverse."],
	"cx_m_tether_x": ["系绳张力 = 40 kN × (rpm/2)² + 张紧器提供的 8 kN。启动冷却时，制动可使转速每秒下降 0.025 rpm。磨损段只剩 5/7 股；即使吊舱已经停止旋转，如果没有松开张紧器就切割，整根系绳仍会崩断。", "Tether tension = 40 kN × (rpm/2)² + the 8 kN supplied by the tensioner. With cooling on, the brake can reduce the speed by 0.025 rpm per second. The worn section has only 5 of 7 strands left. Even after the pods have stopped rotating, if you cut it without releasing the tensioner, the whole tether still snaps."],
	"cx_m_train": ["铰接与单总线", "ARTICULATION AND ONE BUS"],
	"cx_m_train_a": ["七节模块通过铰接结构连接成一列，400 V 总线经过每个联轴器向后延伸。其中 K-4 联轴器卡死在弯曲状态。", "Seven modules are joined by articulated connections into a train, and a 400 V bus runs backwards through every coupling. Coupling K-4 is jammed in a bent position."],
	"cx_m_train_b": ["如果切断上游总线，后方模块会失去供电，储罐泵也无法运行。如果 K-4 后方仍连接着 75 t 以上的载荷就拆除 K-4，后半列模块会弹开。", "If you cut the upstream bus, the modules behind lose power and the tank pumps cannot run. If you remove K-4 while a load of more than 75 t is still attached behind it, the rear half of the train springs apart."],
	"cx_m_train_c": ["从尾部开始拆除 M7、M6，最后处理 K-4。如果后段仍需要供电，先打开 M6 的备用电池。", "Remove M7 and M6 from the tail first, and deal with K-4 last. If the rear section still needs power, turn on M6’s backup battery first."],
	"cx_m_train_x": ["K-4 上的弯矩计显示后方仍连接的载荷，满载时约为 160 t。如果冷却液软管的阀门仍然打开，切割时会喷出冷却液；应先关闭阀门，再从低点排放口排出残液。", "The bending gauge on K-4 shows the load still attached behind it, about 160 t when full. If a coolant hose’s valve is still open, coolant sprays out when it is cut. Close the valves first, then drain the residual liquid at the low-point drains."],
	"cx_m_ore": ["料仓与松散矿石", "THE HOPPER AND LOOSE ORE"],
	"cx_m_ore_a": ["料仓内装有细矿和几十块可见的矿块，矿石通过底部放料门排出。", "The hopper holds fine ore and several tens of visible lumps, and the ore is let out through the gates in its floor."],
	"cx_m_ore_b": ["料仓内的矿石超过一半时，如果强行撬开或切开放料门，矿石会突然倒向一侧，撕裂料仓焊缝。", "When the hopper is more than half full of ore, if you force open or cut open a gate, the ore suddenly dumps to one side and tears the hopper welds."],
	"cx_m_ore_c": ["正常打开放料门，让矿石流入长槽，按吨计价。拆除受力部件之前，先释放张力。", "Open the gates normally and let the ore run into the trough, paid by the tonne. Before removing load-bearing members, release the tension first."],
	"cx_m_ore_x": ["细矿以每秒几吨的流量排出，按矿石种类计价。矿堆下降时，上方矿块会逐渐松开，并随细矿一起流出。", "The fines run out at a flow of several tonnes per second and are paid by ore type. As the heap sinks, the lumps above come loose gradually and flow out with the fines."],
	"cx_m_rails": ["锁轨货物", "RAIL-LOCKED CARGO"],
	"cx_m_rails_a": ["货物通过轨道锁固定在滑轨上，不使用螺栓，因此无法用扳手拆除。", "The cargo is held on its rail by rail locks, not bolts, so it cannot be removed with a wrench."],
	"cx_m_rails_b": ["货门没有打开时解除轨道锁，货物会撞上货门。如果前面的货物仍然锁定就释放后面的货物，两件货物会相撞。切断支撑货物的轨道也会损坏货物。", "If you unlock a piece while the doors are not open, the cargo hits the doors. If you release a piece while the one in front of it is still locked, the two pieces collide. Cutting the rail that carries a piece also damages the cargo."],
	"cx_m_rails_c": ["先给货舱放气，再打开货门。货门依靠总线供电，需要在断电之前打开。之后从最前面的货物开始依次解锁，让货物沿轨道移出。", "Vent the hold first, then open the cargo doors. The doors run on bus power, so open them before the power is cut. Then unlock the cargo one piece at a time from the front, letting each piece move out along its rail."],
	"cx_m_rails_x": ["货物离开轨道末端后会减速至 0.4 m/s，随后缓慢滑出。如果前一件货物尚未运走就释放下一件，两件货物会相撞。SV-122 的仪器安装在减振吊架上；如果还有仪器固定在吊架上就切断主梁或减振连杆，整个吊架会掉落。", "After cargo leaves the end of the rail, it slows to 0.4 m/s and then drifts out slowly. If you release the next piece before the previous one has been moved away, the two pieces collide. The SV-122 instruments are mounted on a damped hanger frame. If you cut the main beam or the damping links while instruments are still fixed to the frame, the whole frame drops."],
	"cx_m_rings": ["还在转的居住环", "HABITAT RINGS STILL TURNING"],
	"cx_m_rings_a": ["两个居住环以约 3 rpm 的速度旋转，通过轮毂上的电机和制动器停止旋转。", "Two habitat rings turn at about 3 rpm, and are stopped by the motors and brakes on their hubs."],
	"cx_m_rings_b": ["居住环上的负载仍然带电时进行制动，回馈电流会烧坏滑环。如果只制动一个居住环，船体会受到扭转；居住环仍在旋转时锁定轴承，轴承会卡死。", "If you brake while the loads on a ring are still live, the regenerated current burns out the slip ring. If you brake only one habitat ring, the hull is twisted. If you lock the bearing while the ring is still turning, the bearing seizes."],
	"cx_m_rings_c": ["先断开居住环上的负载，再启动制动冷却，并同时制动两个居住环。电容充满后需要放电；等居住环停止旋转，再锁定轴承并打开过渡气闸。", "Disconnect the loads on the ring first, then start the brake cooling and brake both habitat rings at the same time. Discharge the capacitor when it is full. Once the rings have stopped turning, lock the bearings and open the transfer airlocks."],
	"cx_m_rings_x": ["制动时，居住环的动能会转化为电能并存入电容。电容充满后，制动器会停止工作，需要先放电才能继续制动。如果两个居住环的转速差过大并持续过久，船坞夹具会过载。将环上的门朝压力低得多的一侧打开，气流冲击会打碎玻璃。", "During braking, the ring’s kinetic energy is converted into electrical energy and stored in a capacitor. When the capacitor is full, the brake stops working and the capacitor must be discharged before braking can continue. If the speed difference between the two habitat rings is too large for too long, the berth clamps are overloaded. If a door on a ring is opened onto a side at much lower pressure, the rush of air breaks the glass."],
	"cx_m_spine": ["主轴受力", "THE SPINE'S LOAD PATH"],
	"cx_m_spine_a": ["尾部的反应堆、发动机和推进剂安装在 440 m 长的主轴上，弦杆负责传递载荷。", "The reactor, engines and propellant at the tail are mounted on the 440 m long spine, and the chords carry the load."],
	"cx_m_spine_b": ["切断一根弦杆后，其余弦杆需要共同承担尾部的全部载荷。如果某一段的载荷超过承受能力，该段结构会撕裂，尾部会下坠并扭转。", "After one chord is cut, the remaining chords have to carry the whole load of the tail together. If the load on any segment exceeds what it can bear, that segment tears, and the tail sags and twists."],
	"cx_m_spine_c": ["先拆除尾部的重物，最后切割弦杆。", "Remove the heavy items from the tail first, and cut the chords last."],
	"cx_m_spine_x": ["主轴每一段都要承受其后方仍在船上的全部重量，并由该段仍然完整的弦杆共同分担。应变探头显示各段的受力情况。", "Each segment of the spine carries the whole weight still aboard behind it, shared by the chords of that segment that are still intact. The strain probes show the load on each segment."],
	"cx_m_workday": ["多日作业", "A JOB OF SEVERAL DAYS"],
	"cx_m_workday_a": ["这艘船体积较大，无法在一个工作日内拆解完成。", "This ship is too big to be taken apart in one working day."],
	"cx_m_workday_b": ["作业每增加一天，合同就会增加一天的运营成本。", "Each extra day of work adds one day of running cost to the contract."],
	"cx_m_workday_c": ["提前规划拆解顺序，减少不必要的操作。收工时游戏会自动保存，第二天可以继续作业。", "Plan the order of the dismantling in advance and cut down unnecessary operations. The game saves automatically at the end of the day, and you can continue the work the next day."],
	"cx_m_workday_x": ["工作日按照合同的游戏时间计算。收工时会保存完整的物理状态，下一天从原来的位置继续作业。", "Working days are counted from the contract’s play time. At the end of the day, the complete physical state is saved, and the next day continues from where the work stopped."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: precision
	"cx_m_mirror_dust": ["镜面污染", "MIRROR CONTAMINATION"],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_a": ["主镜的镜片非常昂贵，而且很容易损坏，镜面前方安装了一套可以升降的电动防尘罩。", "The primary mirror segments are very expensive and easily damaged. A motorised dust cover that can be raised and lowered sits in front of the mirror."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_b": ["如果在镜面附近进行切割，产生的金属粉尘就会落到镜片上，每次切割都会让镜片损失一部分回收价值。", "Cutting near the mirror sends metal dust onto the segments, and every cut costs the mirror part of its recovery value."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_c": ["切割附近的设备之前，先确认防尘罩的电机还有电，然后把防尘罩完全放下来，遮住镜面以后再开始切割。", "Before cutting nearby equipment, check that the dust cover's motor still has power, lower the cover all the way over the mirror, then start cutting."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_x": ["防尘罩通过电机控制升降，断电以后就无法放下。如果连同卷轴一起拆除，防尘罩也会被拆走。镜片受到的粉尘污染达到上限后，继续切割就不会再造成额外的价值损失。", "The cover is raised and lowered by its motor, so it cannot come down without power. Remove it together with its roller and the cover goes with it. Once the dust on the mirror reaches its limit, further cutting costs no more value."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock": ["镜片锁定与拆除顺序", "Locking the segments and the removal order"],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_a": ["每一圈镜片的促动器都有独立的锁定开关，需要通过镜面控制柜进行操作，而且控制柜必须保持通电才能完成锁定。", "Each ring of segments has its own actuator lock switch, worked from the mirror control cabinet, and the cabinet must stay powered for the lock to engage."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_b": ["如果没有锁定促动器就直接拆除镜片，镜片可能从镜座中掉落并摔碎。如果外圈还有镜片就开始拆除内圈，外圈镜片的边缘也会受到损坏。", "Remove a segment with its actuators unlocked and it can fall out of its mount and shatter. Start on an inner ring while the outer ring is still in place and the outer segments' edges are damaged too."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_c": ["切断控制柜电源之前，先把所有促动器全部锁定，然后按照从外圈到内圈的顺序，逐圈拆除镜片。", "Before cutting the cabinet's power, lock every actuator, then remove the segments ring by ring from the outside in."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_x": ["外圈镜片的内侧边缘搭在内圈镜片上，需要依靠内圈镜片提供支撑，所以拆除时必须先处理外圈。促动器也需要在控制柜通电时完成锁定，断电以后就无法继续操作。", "The inner edge of each outer segment rests on the inner ring, which supports it, so the outer ring must come out first. The actuators can only be locked while the cabinet is powered; once the power is off, nothing more can be done."],
	"cx_m_glass": ["承压玻璃与烤裂", "GLASS UNDER PRESSURE AND HEAT"],
	"cx_m_glass_a": ["观景玻璃、穹顶玻璃和精密设备的玻璃罩板，通常靠周围的压条和螺栓固定。只要舱内还有压力，这些玻璃就一直承受着内部气压产生的推力。", "Viewing windows, dome glass and the glass covers of precision equipment are usually held by the clamping strips and bolts around them. While the room holds pressure, the glass carries the push of the air inside."],
	"cx_m_glass_b": ["如果舱内还没有泄压就拆卸玻璃，松开固定螺栓后，玻璃可能会被内部气压直接推出去摔碎。在距离玻璃 0.7 米以内使用激光切割，也可能因为局部温度过高导致玻璃开裂。", "Take the glass out before the room is vented and, once the bolts are loose, the air pressure can push it straight out to shatter. Laser cutting within 0.7 m of the glass can also crack it by overheating it locally."],
	"cx_m_glass_c": ["拆卸之前先把舱内压力降到安全范围，使用激光切割时也要与玻璃保持足够的距离。确认安全后，再拆下固定压条和螺栓，把整块玻璃完整取出来。", "Before removal, bring the room's pressure down to a safe level, and keep the laser well away from the glass. Once it is safe, remove the clamping strips and bolts and take the pane out whole."],
	"cx_m_glass_x": ["一块面积为 2 平方米的观景玻璃，如果两侧存在 100 kPa 的压差，就要承受相当于约 20 吨重量的推力。一旦松开固定压条和螺栓，玻璃就可能被这股压力推出去。PS-12 的中央竖井还有一个需要注意的地方，如果上下两层的舱门同时打开，两层空间就会连通。这时候只要对其中一层进行泄压，另一层的空气也会一起排出去，所以拆卸之前一定要检查两层舱门的状态。", "A 2 m² viewing window with 100 kPa across it carries a push equal to about 20 tonnes. Loosen its strips and bolts and that pressure can push the glass out. PS-12's central shaft needs extra care: with the hatches on both levels open, the two levels are one space, and venting either one vents the other too, so check both hatches before removal."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: isolation and extraction
	"cx_m_vault": ["双路电锁库门", "THE TWO-SUPPLY VAULT LOCK"],
	"cx_m_vault_a": ["库门的电磁锁有两路供电，一路连接主电力总线，另一路连接舰尾检修柜里的备用电源。", "The vault door's solenoid lock has two supplies: one from the main bus, the other from the backup supply in the aft service cabinet."],
	"cx_m_vault_b": ["就算关闭了外部主开关，测量点显示电压为零，库门的电磁锁和主电力总线也可能仍然带电，因为备用电源会通过电磁铁向总线反向供电。", "Even with the main switch outside off and the test point reading zero, the lock and the main bus can still be live, because the backup supply feeds back into the bus through the solenoid."],
	"cx_m_vault_c": ["先进入舰尾检修柜，关闭门锁的备用电源。确认两路电源都断开后，再扳动释放杆，等货库完成泄压以后才能打开库门。", "Go into the aft service cabinet and switch off the lock's backup supply. Once both supplies are confirmed off, pull the release lever, and open the door only after the vault has been vented."],
	"cx_m_vault_x": ["只要电磁锁还在通电，库门就会保持锁定状态，释放杆也无法扳动。等两路电源全部断开以后，就可以扳动释放杆解除锁定，之后打开库门不需要再供电。库门打开以后，里面的保管箱可以整件运走。", "While the solenoid is powered the door stays locked and the release lever will not move. With both supplies off, the lever releases the lock, and the door then opens without power. Once it is open, the safe-deposit boxes inside can be taken out whole."],
	"cx_m_nested": ["船中船", "A SHIP INSIDE A SHIP"],
	"cx_m_nested_a": ["货舱里面还装着一艘完整的小型飞船，按照合同要求，你需要把它整艘取出来，不能拆成零件。", "The hold contains a complete small spacecraft. The contract requires you to take it out whole, not in parts."],
	"cx_m_nested_b": ["只要切割或者拆除了小船的任何一块外壳，就会失去整船回收的资格，最后只能按照零件价格结算。如果先松开船首一侧的托架锁，小船还可能失去固定，直接撞上前面的舱门。", "Cut or remove any panel of its hull and it no longer counts as a whole ship; it is settled at parts prices. Release the cradle lock at the bow end first and the small ship can come loose and hit the door in front of it."],
	"cx_m_nested_c": ["先处理好小船内部的电池、燃料和舱压，确认安全以后，从船尾开始逐个松开托架锁，一直处理到船首。等所有固定装置都解除后，再打开船首舱门，使用绞车把小船完整拖出来。", "First deal with the small ship's batteries, fuel and cabin pressure. Once it is safe, release the cradle locks one by one from the stern to the bow. With every fixing released, open the bow door and winch the ship out whole."],
	"cx_m_nested_x": ["合同会按照整艘飞船的完整程度计算回收价格，只要外壳和主要结构没有被拆除，就能获得整船回收的额外溢价，价值大约是拆成零件出售的 7 倍。拖运的时候也要注意，小船如果撞到舱门，可能会损坏内部设备，整船回收的额外溢价也会被扣掉一部分。", "The contract prices the craft by how complete it is. As long as its hull and main structure are intact, it earns the whole-ship premium, about 7 times what its parts would fetch. Take care while towing too: if the small ship hits the door, its equipment can be damaged and part of the premium is deducted."],
	"cx_s_ullage": ["带压罐与气垫", "PRESSURISED TANKS AND THE ULLAGE"],
	"cx_s_ullage_a": ["推进剂储罐的顶部有一层高压气体，也叫增压气。它会对罐内的液体施加压力，让推进剂能够从出口正常排出。", "The top of a propellant tank holds a layer of high-pressure gas, the pressurant. It presses on the liquid so the propellant can flow out of the outlet."],
	"cx_s_ullage_b": ["如果储罐还带着压力就直接切开，高压气体会把里面的推进剂一起喷出来。如果把整个储罐切断，里面的推进剂可能在几秒钟内全部喷出。完成泄压以后，即使储罐出现破口，剩余的液体也只会缓慢渗出。", "Cut a tank while it is still under pressure and the gas blows the propellant out with it. Sever the whole tank and the propellant can all spray out in seconds. Once the tank is vented, liquid only seeps slowly from a hole."],
	"cx_s_ullage_c": ["拆解之前，先关闭增压气体的供应，再通过排气口释放罐内的高压气体。确认储罐完成泄压以后，才能开始抽取推进剂，最后再拆除储罐。", "Before taking it apart, shut off the pressurant supply, then release the gas through the vent. Only when the tank is confirmed vented, draw off the propellant, and remove the tank last."],
	"cx_s_ullage_x": ["增压系统会不断向储罐补充高压气体，所以只打开排气口还不够，只要增压系统没有关闭，罐内压力就很难降下来。正确的处理顺序是先关闭增压气源，再排出罐内的高压气体。完成泄压以后，储罐内部主要剩下推进剂自身的蒸气压，即使切开储罐，液体通常也只会从破口缓慢渗出，不会再因为增压气体的压力而大量喷射。", "The pressurisation system keeps feeding gas into the tank, so opening the vent alone is not enough: while the system is on, the tank pressure barely falls. The right order is to shut off the pressurant first, then vent the gas in the tank. Once vented, mostly the propellant's own vapour pressure is left, so even if the tank is cut, the liquid usually seeps slowly from the hole instead of being driven out in a jet."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic": ["自燃推进剂", "HYPERGOLIC PROPELLANTS"],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_a": ["甲基肼储存在 T-1 和 T-3 罐中，四氧化二氮单独储存在 T-2 罐中。T-2 没有连接燃料总管，需要单独处理。", "Monomethylhydrazine is stored in tanks T-1 and T-3, and nitrogen tetroxide on its own in T-2. T-2 is not connected to the fuel manifold and has to be handled separately."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_b": ["这两种推进剂只要接触就会起火，不需要点火，在真空环境中也可能发生爆炸。爆燃造成的伤害范围按照 TNT 当量计算。", "These two propellants catch fire as soon as they touch, with no ignition needed, and can explode even in vacuum. The blast's damage radius is worked out in TNT equivalent."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_c": ["通过专用排放口 LD-2 单独抽空 T-2 罐，拆解时注意分开处理两种推进剂，千万不要同时切开它们的储罐或管线。", "Empty T-2 on its own through its dedicated drain LD-2. Keep the two propellants apart while dismantling, and never cut their tanks or lines at the same time."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_x": ["自燃推进剂不需要额外安装点火器，发动机即使反复启动几百次，也能保持较高的可靠性，所以经常用在航天器的姿态控制和轨道调整上。不过这两种推进剂都有很强的毒性和腐蚀性，一旦发生泄漏，蒸气混合后就可能直接起火。拆解的时候必须把两种推进剂分开排放，等一种处理完成后，再处理另一种，避免发生意外。", "Hypergolic propellants need no igniter, so an engine stays reliable even after hundreds of restarts; that is why they are common in attitude control and orbit adjustment. But both are highly toxic and corrosive, and if they leak, their mixing vapours can catch fire at once. When dismantling, drain the two separately: finish one before starting the other."],
	"cx_s_contents": ["检查容器里的内容物", "Checking what a container holds"],
	"cx_s_contents_a": ["灭火瓶、气瓶和储罐里面通常都装着东西，使用测量工具扫描以后，就能在检测结果中看到新增的「内容物」信息。", "Extinguisher bottles, gas cylinders and tanks usually hold something. Scan one with the measuring tool and a new ‘CONTENTS’ line appears in the reading."],
	"cx_s_contents_b": ["气体容器的接口标记为「编号-V」，液体容器的接口标记为「编号-D」。装有液体的储罐通常比较重，如果里面的液体还没有排出，可能会因为重量太大而无法搬动。", "Gas containers' ports are marked ‘ID-V’ and liquid containers' ports ‘ID-D’. A tank holding liquid is usually heavy, and until it is drained it may be too heavy to move."],
	"cx_s_contents_c": ["处理容器之前，先使用测量工具检查里面装的是什么，以及当前的压力有多高。确认情况以后，再决定是排放气体、抽出液体，还是直接把整个容器运走。", "Before dealing with a container, check with the measuring tool what is inside and how high the pressure is. Then decide whether to vent the gas, draw off the liquid, or take the whole container away."],
	"cx_s_contents_x": ["灭火瓶里通常装有压力约为 5.7 MPa 的二氧化碳，氧气瓶里的氧气压力则可以达到 15 MPa。其他容器还可能装有氮气、压缩空气、氦气或氢气，部分设备还带有蓄能器。液体储罐里可能装着水、泥浆、泡沫液、润滑油或者服务推进剂。即使两个容器的外形完全一样，里面装的东西也可能不同，直接切开以后造成的后果自然也不一样。", "An extinguisher bottle usually holds carbon dioxide at about 5.7 MPa, and an oxygen cylinder can hold oxygen at up to 15 MPa. Other containers may hold nitrogen, compressed air, helium or hydrogen, and some equipment carries accumulators. Liquid tanks may hold water, mud, foam concentrate, lubricating oil or service propellant. Two containers that look exactly alike can hold different things, and cutting them open has different consequences."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich": ["富氧助燃", "OXYGEN-RICH AIR"],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_a": ["舱内的氧气浓度超过了正常空气中的 21%，可能是氧气瓶破损造成了泄漏，也可能是舱室本身就处于富氧状态。", "The oxygen in the room is above the 21% of normal air. A broken oxygen cylinder may have leaked, or the room may be oxygen-rich by design."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_b": ["氧气浓度越高，周围的材料就越容易被点燃，起火以后也会燃烧得更快。激光切割产生的高温和火花都可能引起火灾，舱内如果还有氢气，危险就更大了。", "The more oxygen, the more easily things around catch fire, and the faster they burn once alight. The heat and sparks of laser cutting can start a fire, and if there is hydrogen in the room too, the danger is greater."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_c": ["使用激光切割前，先检测舱内的氧气浓度。如果浓度超标，就先排空舱内气体，处理完成以后再开始切割。", "Before laser cutting, measure the oxygen in the room. If it is too high, vent the room first, then start cutting."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_x": ["正常空气中的氮气能够稀释氧气，还能吸收燃烧时产生的一部分热量。当氧气浓度超过 30% 时，布料、塑料和润滑油的燃烧速度可能会增加好几倍。在纯氧环境下，就连钢丝都有可能被点燃。", "The nitrogen in normal air dilutes the oxygen and absorbs part of the heat of burning. Above 30% oxygen, cloth, plastics and lubricating oil can burn several times faster. In pure oxygen, even steel wire can be set alight."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- (end)
}
